const PRYD={"Lighter":{"slug":"lighter","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: L-Form Thundering Fist","d":"Press or hold to activate: Perform up to five forward strikes, dealing Physical DMG and Fire DMG. During the 3rd hit of the Basic Attack, drag the stick/joystick, and repeatedly press or hold to unleash a series of melee follow-up attacks. Release the stick/joystick to follow up with the 4th hit of the Basic Attack. While performing the startup light punch in the 5th hit of the Basic Attack, drag the stick/joystick and repeatedly press or hold to keep alternating between the light punch and 4th hit of the Basic Attack. Release the stick/joystick to follow up with the subsequent jab combo. Continue repeatedly pressing or holding to extend the duration of the jab combo. When you stop pressing or holding , or when the combo reaches its maximum duration, launches a Finishing Move forward. Lighter is invulnerable during the Finishing Move. During the 5th hit of the Basic Attack, Lighter takes 40% less DMG. While in the Morale Burst state, Anti-Interrupt Level is increased during the 5th hit of his Basic Attack, and the DMG reduction effect is increased to 80%.","m":["1st-Hit: 39.2%","2nd-Hit: 48%","3rd-Hit: 55.3%","Follow-Up 1st-Hit: 86.9%","Follow-Up 2nd-Hit: 47.7%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: V-Form Sunrise Uppercut","d":"Press to activate. Strikes enemies in front with an uppercut, dealing Fire DMG. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill. Press during a shuffle dodge to activate: Strike forward with a series of punches, dealing Fire DMG. This skill will not interrupt the combo count for Basic Attacks. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["36.3%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: V-Form Sunrise Uppercut - Full Distance","d":"With enough energy, press to activate: Leaps into the air with a powerful uppercut, striking enemies in front and dealing massive Fire DMG. Press again during this skill to spend additional Energy to perform a powerful follow-up attack, dealing massive Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. After using this skill, press or hold to follow up with the 4th hit of the Basic Attack. With enough Energy, press during the shuffle dodge to activate: Strike forward with a powerful punch combo, dealing massive Fire DMG. This skill will not interrupt the combo count for Basic Attacks. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. After using this skill, press or hold to immediately follow up with the 5th hit of the Basic Attack.","m":["486.3%","Follow-Up: 292.7%","Activation Energy Cost: 40%","Follow-Up Energy Cost: 20%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Shadowed Slide","d":"Press to activate. A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. Press while the character is attacking to activate: Perform a quick shuffle dodge in the direction of the stick/Joystick. This skill will not interrupt the combo count for Basic Attacks. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Charging Slam","d":"Press during a dodge to activate: Rapidly strikes enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["89.9%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Blazing Flash","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Strike enemies in front, dealing Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. After using the skill, press or hold to immediately follow up with the 5th hit of the Basic Attack.","m":["186.3%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: V-Form Scorching Sun","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Unleashes a powerful strike at enemies in front in a small area, dealing massive Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["712.1%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: W-Form Crowned Inferno","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate. Unleashes a powerful strike in a large area around, dealing massive Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1508%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Blazing Flash - Guard","d":"When the on-field character is launched, press to activate. Strike enemies in front, dealing Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. After using the skill, press or hold to immediately follow up with the 5th hit of the Basic Attack.","m":["69.7%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Swift Break","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, inflicting massive Daze. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Charging Slam - Stab","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate: Strike enemies in front, dealing Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. After using this skill, press or hold to immediately follow up with the 5th hit of the Basic Attack.","m":["219.8%"]}],"build":{"w":["Blazing Laurel","Ice-Jade Teapot","Hellfire Gears","The Restrained"],"a":["King of the Summit, Shockstar Disco","Proto Punk, Shockstar Disco","Shockstar Disco, Swing Jazz","King of the Summit, Swing Jazz"],"core":7,"st":[["CRIT Rate",55],["CRIT DMG",107],["ATK",2426]]},"how":"EXTENDED ROTATION Lighter Rotation: The rotation below assumes Lighter begins with 100 Morale but can also be started at 80 Morale in a pinch, but at the cost of losing some supportive and Dazing benefits. Additionally the rotation can also be initiated with any of Lighter\u0027s abilities which allow him to skip straight to his 5th Basic Attack. Defensive Assist: Swift Break Assist Follow-Up: Charging Slam - Stab Basic Attack: L-Form Thundering Fist (5th-Hit Combo)(Morale Boosted) Basic Attack: L-Form Thundering Fist (5th-Hit Powerful Finisher)(Morale Boosted) EX Special Attack: V-Form Sunrise Uppercut - Full Distance EX Special Attack: V-Form Sunrise Uppercut - Full Distance (Follow-Up) Basic Attack: L-Form Thundering Fist P4 Basic Attack: L-Form Thundering Fist (5th-Hit Startup) Basic Attack: L-Form Thundering Fist (5th-Hit Combo) Basic Attack: L-Form Thundering Fist (5th-Hit Finisher) Dodge Counter: Blazing Flash (Can be executed at any time) SHORTENED ROTATION Short Lighter Rotation: If desired - and you have another character that can make use of field time Lighter\u0027s rotation - can be shortened. The entire second Basic Attack Combo and Dodge Counter are all non-essential and can be cut simplifying his gameplay even more. Defensive Assist: Swift Break Assist Follow-Up: Charging Slam - Stab Basic Attack: L-Form Thundering Fist (5th-Hit Combo)(Morale Boosted) Basic Attack: L-Form Thundering Fist (5th-Hit Powerful Finisher)(Morale Boosted) EX Special Attack: V-Form Sunrise Uppercut - Full Distance EX Special Attack: V-Form Sunrise Uppercut - Full Distance (Follow-Up)","pros":"Incredible full team ICE and FIRE DMG% Boost. Grants substantial ICE and FIRE RES% Shred. Extends enemy Stun duration by 3 seconds, allowing for larger burst windows. Has an incredibly front-loaded combo capable of taking up minimal field time if desired. Simple and easy to play.","cons":"Daze application is much more concentrated than other characters, sometimes leading to downtime when Morale, Energy and Counter opportunities aren’t available. Primarily synergizes with Fire and Ice units only, limiting the scope of his potential. Loses supportive capabilities when unable to hit 270 Impact - something that isn’t easy to achieve without using 5-star W-Engines.","teams":[{"m":"Sigrid + Lighter + Astra Yao + Snap","c":"","r":"Rank 71"},{"m":"Hugo + Dialyn + Lighter + Robin","c":"","r":"Rank 83"},{"m":"Hugo + Lighter + Lycaon + Robin","c":"","r":"Rank 93"}]},"Billy":{"slug":"billy-kid","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Full Firepower","d":"Press to activate: Unleashes a piercing attack, dealing Physical DMG. Repeatedly press or hold to enter Crouching Shot to extend the attack duration. Drag the joystick during Crouching Shot to launch Rolling Shot and adjust the character\u0027s position, dealing Physical DMG. Stop pressing or holding during Crouching Shot to launch Finishing Shot at enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["Standing Fire: 68%","Standing Bullet: 7.6%","Crouching Fire: 61.8%","Crouching Bullet: 12.7%","Rolling Shot: 61.8%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Stand Still","d":"Press to activate. Performs up to 3 piercing attacks in a line, dealing Physical DMG. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["1st-Hit: 24.2%","2nd-Hit: 51.7%","3rd-Hit: 50.1%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Clearance Time","d":"With enough energy, press to activate. Launches a powerful piercing attack in a straight line, dealing massive Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["543.8%","Energy Cost: 60%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Risky Business","d":"Press to dodge. A rapid dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Starlight Sanction","d":"When dragging the during a dodge, press : Launches a piercing attack at nearby enemies within a large area, dealing Physical DMG. When not dragging the during a dodge, press : Launches a piercing attack at enemies in a line, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["360-degree Shot: 63.1%","Straight Shot : 39%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Fair Fight","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Pierces enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["221.4%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Starlight Mirage","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate. Unleashes a powerful piercing attack at surrounding enemies in a large area, dealing massive Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["735.2%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Starlight Sparkle","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate. Unleashes a powerful piercing attack at surrounding enemies in a large area, dealing massive Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1597.7%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Power of Teamwork","d":"When the on-field character is launched, press to activate. Launches a piercing attack at enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable during the attack.","m":["93.4%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Evasive Assist: Flash Spin","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Dodges the enemy\u0027s attack and activates Vital View. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Fatal Shot","d":"Press after an Evasive Assist to activate. Pierce enemies in a large area in front, dealing Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["388.8%"]}],"build":{"w":["Cloudcleave Radiance"],"a":["Shadow Harmony, Puffer Electro","Woodpecker Electro, Branch \u0026 Blade Song","Hormone Punk, Astral Voice","Puffer Electro, Woodpecker Electro"],"core":7,"st":[["CRIT Rate",72],["CRIT DMG",170],["ATK",2830]]},"how":"Billy does not have dedicated combos that he needs to use. There isn’t a “combo” list to memorize. Instead, Billy wants to react to enemy attacks, hit back with his Dodge Counters and EX Specials, and control the space around him while moving with Dash Attacks. This aspect of Billy’s improv gameplay is hard to convey in a written guide, because a lot of it relies on the enemy you are facing, what they are doing, where you are in relation to them, and the teammates you have. I highly recommend you look into gameplay from some dedicated Billy players, to better visualize how it looks. Beginner There are 3 key steps when trying to learn how to play Billy to optimize him, but mastering these makes learning intermediate and advanced techniques much easier. 1. How to Crouch Billy’s Core gives him a 50% DMG buff while he is Crouching, and as mentioned before, this applies to all attacks done in this state. To Crouch, simply hold Basic - that’s all. He will transition from Standing Fire, into a Rolling Shot, and into Crouching Fire. As long as you hold or repeatedly press Basic, he will continue to use Crouching Fire. Billy leaves the Crouching state when you: Use his Basic’s Finishing Shot. Get knocked back by enemies. Start to move around normally. Switch to another Agent. As a result, this means that it isn’t possible to get Chain Attacks to benefit from the Crouching state, as he has to be swapped out of. Keep this in mind, as it’s important to Crouch again before using Billy’s EXs or Ultimate after Chains. Aside from the above, as long as you continue to attack enemies, Billy will stay in the Crouching state. Managing this is very important to access Billy’s full damage output. Not only in ensuring that it is up for hard-hitting skills, but also when not to use it. Considering how long it can take to start Crouching and how saturated Billy tends to be in DMG bonuses, against certain enemies - like those with a short Stun duration - it can be optimal to ignore it altogether and prioritise getting damaging skills in instead. 2. How to Move While Crouching Another problem with Crouching Fire is that it makes Billy sit in one place, but there are ways around it. While using Crouching Fire, moving the joystick in any direction will cause him to use a Rolling Shot. This is the simplest way to move him around while Crouching, but it’s not the recommended solution. Instead, we want to utilize Billy’s Dodge and 360 Dash Attack. As before, while using Crouching Fire, move the joystick in any direction to use a Rolling Shot. Then, during the Rolling Shot, release Basi","pros":"Is Free! The 2nd Agent you acquire in the game. Has a very mobile playstyle, which lets him control space and manipulate some enemy behaviors. Low skill floor, high skill ceiling, having a rather simple but open-ended gameplan that gives him a lot of potential for optimisation. Biggest Starlight Knight fan…","cons":"A main damage dealer that hasn’t aged well, being objectively far weaker than recent Agent releases. Dated Additional Ability criteria limits his team options, with a large gap in performance if certain squad members aren’t available. Demands in-depth knowledge of different teams and encounters to excel, lacking clear-cut routes and combos for beginners to rely on. ...and he’ll make sure you’re well aware of it.","teams":[{"m":"Billy + Dialyn + Sunna + Biggest Fan","c":"","r":"Rank 388"},{"m":"Billy + Norma + Nicole + Bangvolver","c":"","r":"Rank 365"},{"m":"Billy + Norma + Sunna + Ultra Jake","c":"","r":"Rank 365"}]},"Hugo":{"slug":"hugo","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Dark Abyss Quartet","d":"Press to activate: Perform up to four attacks forward, dealing Physical DMG and Ice DMG. The fourth attack is a shot. During this attack, hold to charge and perform a charged shot. Anti-Interrupt level is increased during the fourth attack.","m":["1st-Hit: 43.1%","2nd-Hit: 74.1%","3rd-Hit: 169.6%","Slash: 149.1%","Shot: 58.6%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Dark Abyss Concerto","d":"After the 4th hit of Basic Attack: Dark Abyss Quartet, the shot of Dodge Counter: Phantasm - Slash, or the shot of Quick Assist: Elegy, press or hold to activate: Throw the scythe forward to perform a slash, followed by a shot, dealing Ice DMG. During the shot, hold to charge and perform a charged shot. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["Slash: 143.4%","Shot: 86.7%","Charged Shot: 170.6%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Soul Hunter - Judgment","d":"Press to activate. Spins the scythe and then unleashes a forward slash, dealing Ice DMG. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["85.3%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Soul Hunter - Punishment","d":"With enough Energy, press to activate. Spins the scythe and then executes a powerful upward attack, dealing massive Ice DMG. This skill is not counted as a heavy attack. After the skill is used, it can be directly followed up with the 4th hit of Basic Attack: Dark Abyss Quartet. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["373.2%","Energy Cost: 40%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Phantasm","d":"Press to activate. A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Phantasm - Shatter","d":"Press during a dodge to activate: Launch a dashing attack at enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["93.5%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Phantasm - Slash","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Performs a series of attacks on enemies in front, dealing Ice DMG. During the skill, hold to launch a shot. During the shot, hold to charge and perform a charged shot. The shot is considered a Basic Attack, with its DMG treated as Basic Attack DMG. After the skill is used, it can be directly followed up with the 4th hit of Basic Attack: Dark Abyss Quartet. Character is Invulnerable during the slashes and shooting retreat of the skill.","m":["245.9%","ALT Shot: 162.1%","ALT Charged Shot: 212.1%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Trick of Fate","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Dash forward to perform a slash across a large area, then launch a shot, dealing massive Ice DMG. The shot activated by this skill is considered a charged shot. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["701.1%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Blaspheme","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate. Throws the scythe in a powerful spinning attack, then catches the scythe and launches a slash in a large area, dealing massive Ice DMG. This skill is not counted as a heavy attack. After the skill is used, it can be directly followed up with the 4th hit of Basic Attack: Dark Abyss Quartet. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1527.1%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Elegy","d":"When the active character is launched, press to activate. Performs a series of attacks on enemies in front, dealing Ice DMG. During the skill, hold to launch a shot. During the shot, hold to charge and perform a charged shot. The shot is considered a Basic Attack, with the DMG treated as Basic Attack DMG. After the skill is used, it can be directly followed up with the 4th hit of Basic Attack: Dark Abyss Quartet. Character is Invulnerable during the slashes and shooting retreat of the skill.","m":["104.5%","ALT Shot: 124.7%","ALT Charged Shot: 163.2%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: The End Has Not Come","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Ace Reversal","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate: Dash forward and perform two slashes, dealing Ice DMG. After the skill is used, it can be directly followed up with the 4th hit of Basic Attack: Dark Abyss Quartet. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["291.7%"]}],"build":{"w":["Myriad Eclipse"],"a":["Puffer Electro, Branch \u0026 Blade Song","Hormone Punk, Woodpecker Electro","Hormone Punk, Branch \u0026 Blade Song","Puffer Electro, Hormone Punk"],"core":7,"st":[["CRIT Rate",78],["CRIT DMG",161],["ATK",3251]]},"how":"Rotations Hugo\u0027s rotations are rather simple. The core of his burst comprises of 2 Chain Attacks, followed by an EX Special or Ultimate to trigger Totalize. That\u0027s really all there is to it, ensuring the highest amount of damage possible without sacrificing much on stun time to maximise Totalize scaling. It\u0027s as simple as: Initiate stun by triggering a Chain Attack on a character that isn\u0027t Hugo Hugo Chain Attack Cancel Swap out of Hugo and trigger another Chain Attack Hugo Chain Attack EX Special or Ultimate Different teammates will have different ways of triggering a second Chain Attack, so being mindful of your options is important, as the faster Chains are triggered, the faster Hugo will work towards his Totalize, and the more damage it will do. In some circumstances, it is preferable to skip the second Hugo Chain Attack altogether, doing only a single Chain Attack into EX Special or Ultimate (such as if there isn\u0027t enough time left in a fight). In which case, swapping out of Hugo once he casts his EX Special then triggering a Chain Attack before Totalize hits allows for a Stunner Chain Attack to be used just as stun ends, giving a helpful boost of Daze to make speeding through to the next stun easier. Be mindful of any Drive Disc set effects, namely Hormone Punk, as swapping out to Hugo outside of stun periods or even being too fast can lead to losing out on its buffs. Baseline Rotation Chain Attack: Trick of Fate Chain Attack: Trick of Fate Ultimate: Blaspheme OR EX Special Attack: Soul Hunter - Punishment","pros":"The ultimate user of the Hormone Punk set, placing high emphasis on lots of CRIT-scaling damage accessed in short burst windows; Utilizes niche Double Stun team compositions to the fullest, allowing valuable Support-type Agents to be used elsewhere; Really easy to pick up gameplay-wise — just learn his short combos and they can be executed anywhere; Lots of buffs against smaller enemies, useful for hitting targets that aren\u0027t bosses in content like Shiyu Defense; Super cool villain bad guy-type character.","cons":"High reliance on limited Stun Agents who can at the same time buff Hugo and inflict Daze on enemies — team compositions are undeniably restrictive, be prepared to invest lots of resources; Necessitates to learn certain techniques to make good use out of him, such as Double Chains, otherwise his damage may see noticeable drop-offs; You don\u0027t get to see him much when playing him outside of brief Stun windows (which is unfortunate because we like Hugo).","teams":[{"m":"Hugo + Dialyn + Lighter + Robin","c":"","r":"Rank 83"},{"m":"Hugo + Lighter + Lycaon + Robin","c":"","r":"Rank 93"},{"m":"Hugo + Lighter + Norma + Robin","c":"","r":"Rank 103"}]},"Ye Shunguang":{"slug":"ye-shunguang","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Swiftedge","d":"Press to activate: Launches up to four forward slashes, dealing Physical DMG. Can be chained into Dash Attack: Phantasm Dash after the 4th hit.","m":["1st-Hit: 79.4%","2nd-Hit: 244.1%","3rd-Hit: 124.6%","4th-Hit: 368%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Cloudstream Sword Will","d":"Hold to activate: Launches a flurry of blade shockwaves, dealing Physical DMG. Hold to extend the attack. Anti-Interrupt Level is increased during this skill.","m":["Individual Blade Energy: 16.7%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Enlightened Mind - Splitting Currents","d":"While in the Enlightened Mind state and on the ground, press to activate: Performs up to three forward slashes, dealing Physical DMG. If struck by an enemy attack during the 3rd hit, triggers a block, negating that instance of DMG. If she possesses Qingming Sword Force, the 3rd hit is replaced with Basic Attack: Enlightened Mind - Skyward Ascent.","m":["1st-Hit: 112.6%","2nd-Hit: 155.9%","3rd-Hit: 216.6%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Enlightened Mind - Skyward Ascent","d":"While in the Enlightened Mind state and with Qingming Sword Force, after the 2nd hit of Basic Attack: Enlightened Mind - Splitting Currents, press to activate: Launches a swift rising attack, dealing Physical DMG and entering an airborne state. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["91%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Enlightened Mind - Sunderlight Maximum","d":"After activating Basic Attack: Enlightened Mind - Sunderlight Annihilation, and with Qingming Sword Force, press to activate: Launches a wide sweeping slash forward, dealing massive Physical DMG. On hit, 1 point of Qingming Sword Force is consumed. If struck by an enemy during the skill, triggers a block, negating that instance of DMG and increasing the skill\u0027s Interrupt Level. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. After using this skill and with Qingming Sword Force, press to consume 1 point of Qingming Sword Force and launch a hit of EX Special Attack: Enlightened Mind - Soaring Light. This skill is automatically followed up with Basic Attack: Enlightened Mind - Skyward Ascent, and Ye Shunguang enters an airborne state. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["604.8%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Enlightened Mind - Sunderlight","d":"In the Enlightened Mind state, and while airborne, press to activate: Launches up to two downward slashes in front, dealing Physical DMG. Ye Shunguang will not exit the Enlightened Mind state during this skill. Press or to follow up with Basic Attack: Enlightened Mind - Sunderlight Annihilation. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1st-Hit: 120.7%","2nd-Hit: 156.5%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Enlightened Mind - Sunderlight Annihilation","d":"After the 2nd hit of Basic Attack: Enlightened Mind - Sunderlight, press to activate: Performs a falling attack in front, entering a grounded state, and dealing Physical DMG. When launching this skill with 2 or more points of Qingming Sword Force, Ye Shunguang will perform a downward falling strike across a large area in front instead, dealing massive Physical DMG. On hit, 2 points of Qingming Sword Force are consumed, granting the Culmination effect. After using this skill, if Ye Shunguang possesses Qingming Sword Force, press to consume 1 point of Qingming Sword Force and launch a hit of EX Special Attack: Enlightened Mind - Soaring Light, which can be quickly followed up with Basic Attack: Enlightened Mind - Sunderlight Maximum. Ye Shunguang will not exit the Enlightened Mind state during this skill. During this skill, if attacked by enemies, triggers a block, negating that instance of DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["With Qingming Sword Force: 891.2%","Without Qingming Sword Force: 159.9%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Culmination","d":"During EX Special Attack: Enlightened Mind - Soaring Light, each time Qingming Sword Force is consumed while Culmination is active, the Qingming Sword Force cost is replaced by consuming Culmination instead. This effect does not stack, and lasts until the current Enlightened Mind ends.","m":[]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Guiding Tides","d":"Press to activate: If a dodge is available, 1 dodge chance is consumed, and the action is counted as activating a Dodge. If no dodge is available or a Perfect Dodge is not triggered, launches a quick sword energy attack that deals Physical DMG. If a Perfect Dodge is triggered at this time, launches a flying sword attack, dealing Physical DMG, and immediately follow up with the 2nd hit of Basic Attack: Swiftedge. Character is briefly invulnerable during the skill.","m":["98.9%","Perfect Dodge Triggered: 315.9%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Gale Suppression","d":"With enough Energy, press to activate: Launches a rushing slash and a flying sword attack at the enemy, dealing massive Physical DMG. Enemy attacks can be dodged during this skill. After this skill is used, gain 1 point of Qingming Sword Force. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1178.4%","Energy Cost: 60%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Enlightened Mind - Clean Exit","d":"While in the Enlightened Mind state and grounded, press to activate: Performs a swift backstep slash, dealing Physical DMG. If a dodge is available, 1 dodge chance is consumed, and the action is counted as activating a Dodge. If a Perfect Dodge is triggered at this time, press to quickly activate Enlightened Mind - Sunderlight Maximum and enter Vital View. After this Enlightened Mind - Sunderlight Maximum activates, it can be immediately followed up with Basic Attack: Enlightened Mind - Skyward Ascent. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["71%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Enlightened Mind - Soaring Light","d":"In the Enlightened Mind state and with Qingming Sword Force, hold to activate: Performs quick consecutive slashes, dealing massive Physical DMG while rapidly consuming Qingming Sword Force until none remains. The skill ends early if Qingming Sword Force is insufficient or if is released. Ye Shunguang will not exit the Enlightened Mind state during this skill. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1 Qingming Sword Force Consumed: 176.3%","6 Qingming Sword Force Consumed: 1058%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Enlightened Mind - Return to Dust","d":"In the Enlightened Mind state, press or hold when all Qingming Sword Force is expended to activate: Deals massive Physical DMG to enemies in a large area. Ye Shunguang will not exit the Enlightened Mind state during this skill. After using this skill, Ether Veil: Verdict is removed and the Enlightened Mind state ends. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1161.1%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Leave No Trace","d":"Press to activate: A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. During the Enlightened Mind state, and if a Perfect Dodge is triggered, press to activate Basic Attack: Enlightened Mind - Skyward Ascent.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Wandering Cloud","d":"While tilting the stick/joystick, hold to activate. Enters a high-speed movement state. Steer with the stick/joystick, and release the stick/joystick to stop.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Phantasm Dash","d":"Press during a dodge to activate: Slashes enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["105%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Swallow Strike","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate: Leaps into the air and thrusts forward, dealing Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["346.3%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Smite the Wicked","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Unleashes a powerful slash at enemies ahead in a large area, dealing massive Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["871.6%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Chasing Storms","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate: Summons a sword formation and enter the Enlightened Mind state, activating an Ether Veil: Verdict while also gaining 6 Qingming Sword Force. This skill deals massive Physical DMG. Upon activating this skill, if Decibels are consumed, press while in this Enlightened Mind state to launch an Ultimate: Cleaving Heavens that doesn\u0027t consume Decibels. Enter the airborne state after using this skill. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1925%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Enlightened Mind - Lure Thunder","d":"While in the Enlightened Mind state, and when a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Unleashes a powerful slash at enemies ahead in a large area, dealing massive Physical DMG. Ye Shunguang will not exit the Enlightened Mind state during this skill. Enter the airborne state after using this skill. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["908.6%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Cleaving Heavens","d":"After consuming Decibels to launch Ultimate: Chasing Storms and while in the Enlightened Mind state, press or hold when all Qingming Sword Force is expended to activate: Summons a massive blade, dealing massive Physical DMG to enemies. Ye Shunguang will not exit the Enlightened Mind state during this skill. After using this skill, the Enlightened Mind state ends, and Ether Veil: Verdict is removed. This skill doesn\u0027t consume Decibels. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["3084.3%"]},{"t":"Entry","n":"Entry Skill: Illuminating Darkness","d":"With 6 Qingming Sword Force and while not in the Enlightened Mind state, hold to activate, or press while in combat and switch on-field from off-field to activate: Enters the Enlightened Mind state and activates Ether Veil: Verdict. Deals Physical DMG to enemies in a large area in front. Activating this skill is considered as activating a Quick Assist. Enters the airborne state after using this skill. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["400.4%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Support Guard","d":"When the active character is launched, press to activate. Leaps into the air and thrusts forward, dealing Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["80.5%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Cease Hostility","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate: Deals massive Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["413.7%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: When I Return","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Enlightened Mind - Tactical Support","d":"While in the Enlightened Mind state, when the active character is launched, press to activate. Launches a forward slash, dealing Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["67.3%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Enlightened Mind - Unification","d":"While in the Enlightened Mind state and after a Defensive Assist, press to activate: Deals massive Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["430%"]}],"build":{"w":["Cloudcleave Radiance","The Brimstone","Steel Cushion","Severed Innocence"],"a":["White Water Ballad, Branch \u0026 Blade Song","White Water Ballad, Puffer Electro","White Water Ballad, Astral Voice","White Water Ballad, Woodpecker Electro"],"core":7,"st":[["CRIT Rate",50],["CRIT DMG",211],["ATK",3227]]},"how":"Despite Ye Shunguang\u0027s ridiculously verbose and complex kit, she is remarkably simple to play. Although many characters may need specific set-ups to build resources in time for stuns, may struggle with Energy/Adrenaline and Decibel alignment for critical burst periods, or must juggle their own field-time with Stunners\u0027, none of this really matters much for all but the highest level of play with Ye Shunguang. Her gameplan cycle can be neatly split into \"normal\" state and \"Enlightened Mind\" state phases. While in the normal state, the priority is to build Qingming Sword Force points as quickly as possible. This mostly entails using Basic Attacks over and over, with the occasional Dodge Counter to avoid being interrupted by enemy attacks. When there\u0027s enough energy in stock, use her normal EX Special and - as it has a very long animation - swap out to other Agents for any resource generation or buff/debuff application as required (e.g. Dialyn for Malicious Complaint or Zhao for Frostbite Point build-up and Ether Veil activation). Once 6 Qingming Sword Force points are built, apply any relevant buffs (e.g. King of the Summit or Astral Voice) and then make use of the Entry Skill to enter the Enlightened Mind state. Alternatively, if at 3 Qingming Sword Force points or below, use Ye Shunguang\u0027s Ultimate to immediately enter the state. Try not to be at above 3 points so as to not overcap with the 6 points from the Ultimate, as Bearer stacks do have a limit. In the Enlightened Mind state, there are 3 potential combos to follow: Short Combo: Basic Attack: Sunderlight Annihilation Basic Attack: Sunderlight Maximum EX Special: Soaring Light Basic Attack: Sunderlight Annihilation Basic Attack: Sunderlight Maximum EX Special: Soaring Light EX Special Return to Dust or Ultimate: Cleaving Heavens (hold Special/press Ultimate) Inputs would be: Special \u003e B \u003e EX \u003e Special \u003e B \u003e EX (Hold) Extended Combo: Basic Attack: Sunderlight x2 Basic Attack: Sunderlight Annihilation Basic Attack: Sunderlight Maximum Basic Attack: Splitting Currents x2 EX Special: Soaring Light Basic Attack: Sunderlight x1 Basic Attack: Sunderlight Annihilation EX Special: Soaring Light (Ground Ver.) Basic Attack: Sunderlight Maximum Basic Attack: Splitting Currents x3 - EX: Special Return to Dust or Ultimate: Cleaving Heavens (hold Special/press Ultimate) Inputs would be B \u003e B \u003e B \u003e B \u003e B \u003e B \u003e EX \u003e B \u003e B \u003e EX \u003e B \u003e B \u003e B \u003e B \u003e EX (Hold) Standard Combo: Basic Attack: Sunderlight x2 Basic Attack: Sunderlight Annihilation Basic Attack: Sunderlight Maximum EX Special: Soaring Light Basic Attack: Sunderli","pros":"Absurdly high power budget, able to perform well in every encounter as of her release, and steamrolling even Physical resistant enemies. Low skill floor that allows most players to pick up and excel with little effort needed. Constant invulnerability and unique mechanics that result in fight-specific adaptations being needed only in high-level play. Surprisingly easy to build, with low CRIT Rate needs and a variety of good W-Engine options. Raw power level means she can work with a variety of different teams. Has a neighborly, innocent young lady, girlfriend next door vibe.","cons":"Overly dependent on specific teammates to be at her best, with notable performance falloff without them (albeit still strong regardless). Some may find her boring and unengaging, with little effort needed and a repetitive gameplan. May get memory wiped when her Ultimate is used.","teams":[{"m":"Ye Shunguang + Sunna + Zhao + Sprout","c":"","r":"Rank 3"},{"m":"Ye Shunguang + Dialyn + Sunna + Sprout","c":"","r":"Rank 4"},{"m":"Ye Shunguang + Dialyn + Zhao + Sprout","c":"","r":"Rank 5"}]},"Soukaku":{"slug":"soukaku","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Making Rice Cakes","d":"Press to activate. Unleashes up to 3 attacks, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["1st-Hit: 66.2%","2nd-Hit: 216.3%","3rd-Hit: 293.1%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Making Rice Cakes (Frosted Banner)","d":"When Frosted Banner is active, press to activate. Unleashes up to 3 faster attacks in front, dealing Ice DMG.","m":["1st-Hit: 76.6%","2nd-Hit: 228.5%","3rd-Hit: 511.4%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Cooling Bento","d":"Press to activate. Soukaku releases a wind current in front of her and unleashes her finishing move, dealing Ice DMG. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill, and DMG taken is reduced by 40%. Holding while using this skill allows for a quick transition to Fly the Flag.","m":["1st-Hit: 28.4%","Finishing Move: 100.1%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Fanning Mosquitoes","d":"With enough energyy, press to activate. Releases wind currents of extended range in front of her, dealing massive Ice DMG. This skill can be used in rapid succession by pressing repeatedly. Each use consumes a specified amount of Energy. When Soukaku\u0027s Energy is depleted, or you stop pressing the button, she unleashes a powerful finishing move that deals massive Ice DMG. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill, and her DMG taken is reduced by 40%. Holding while using this skill allows for a quick transition to Fly the Flag.","m":["Chain Attack: 131.2%","Wind Current: 102.1%","Energy Cost to Use: 60%","Energy Cost of Each Attack: 30%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Rally!","d":"Hold to activate. Soukaku plunges her weapon into the ground, morphs it into a flag, and launches Fly the Flag, dealing Ice DMG. Hitting an enemy with Fly the Flag triggers a Quick Assist. Pressing or after Fly the Flag activates a Special Attack as she retracts the flag, dealing Ice DMG. If Soukaku owns 3 stacks of Vortex on using Fly the Flag, she consumes all 3 stacks and enters the Frosted Banner state. In the Frosted Banner state, she can unleash an enhanced Basic Attack or an enhanced Dash Attack, dealing massive Ice DMG This effect can last up to 45s or stack up to 6 times. Soukaku\u0027s weapon gains Vortexes in the following circumstances: Gains 1 stack of Vortex when launching an EX Special Attack, Gains 1 stack of Vortex when launching a Chain Attack, Gains 3 stacks of Vortex when launching an Ultimate. Soukaku can accumulate a maximum of 3 stacks of Vortex.","m":["Fly the Flag: 250.1%","Quick Fly the Flag: 140.1%","Lowering the Flag: 245%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Grab a Bite","d":"Press to dodge. A rapid dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: 50/50","d":"Press during a Dodge to activate. Slashes enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["76.7%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Away From My Snacks","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Slashes enemies in front, dealing Ice DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["247.3%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: 50/50 (Frosted Banner)","d":"When Frosted Banner is active, press during a Dodge to activate. Slashes enemies in front, dealing Ice DMG.","m":["131.5%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Pudding Slash","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Soukaku quickly unleashes a series of strikes at enemies in front of her and follows up with Fly the Flag, dealing massive Ice DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["748.8%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Jumbo Pudding Slash","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate. Soukaku quickly unleashes an extended series of strikes at enemies in front of her and follows up with Fly the Flag, dealing massive Ice DMG. Upon activating this skill, Soukaku enters the Masked state, increasing her CRIT Rate by 15% for 15s. Upon activating this skill, other squad members recover 10 Energy. The next character to switch in gains an additional 20 Energy. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1989.8%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: A Set for Two","d":"When the on-field character is launched, press to activate. Slashes enemies in front, dealing Ice DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["113.4%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Guarding Tactics","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. This skill excels at parrying enemy attacks and reduces the consumption of Assist Points when the character is under intense attacks. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Sweeping Strike","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate. Charges and strikes enemies in front, dealing Ice DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. Holding while using this skill allows for a quick transition to Fly the Flag.","m":["264%"]}],"build":{"w":["Kaboom the Cannon","Bashful Demon","Unfettered Game Ball"],"a":["Freedom Blues, Phaethon\u0027s Melody","Freedom Blues, Swing Jazz","Polar Metal, Swing Jazz","Phaethon\u0027s Melody, Freedom Blues, Flex"],"core":6.45,"st":[["CRIT Rate",50],["CRIT DMG",114],["ATK",2008]]},"how":"$undefined","pros":"Gives herself an absurdly high Flat ATK buff, which she can transfer to the next character in the party via Quick Assist or Chain Attack with permanent uptime if managed properly; Grants the team an Ice DMG Bonus after consuming her Vortex charges, which is doable quickly and easily with permanent uptime if managed properly. Also shreds Ice RES for a short period of time with M4, leading go high Ice-specific buffing potential; Surprisingly high damage potential with Mindscapes and a good build, not to be ignored on top of solid Ice Anomaly application. Overall one of the rare Supports who scale well with high investment; She’s free!","cons":"Cannot benefit off-field attackers/secondary DPS Agents in a significant way, due to only transferring her Flat ATK buff to 1 Agent on the team. Leads to restricted teambuilding options; Kit is definitely Ice-centric. Difficult to justify her use over other easily accessed general buffers such as Nicole and Lucy outside of Ice teams, even though she’s still definitely usable beyond the scope of Ice teams there’s just little reason to do so; The infamous Slowkaku. Chain Attack, Ultimate, EX Special and Fly The Flag (all of her main abilities) take a long while to execute in spite of the high buffing and personal damage, which makes rotations a lot rougher around the edges with her on the team.","teams":[{"m":"Miyabi + Yuzuha + Soukaku + Sharkboo","c":"","r":"Rank 56"},{"m":"Miyabi + Lycaon + Soukaku + Sharkboo","c":"","r":"Rank 202"},{"m":"Miyabi + Soukaku + Astra Yao + Sharkboo","c":"","r":"Rank 280"}]},"Sunna":{"slug":"sunna","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Mischief Meteor Hammer","d":"Press to activate: Unleashes up to four attacks ahead, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["1st-Hit: 43.4%","2nd-Hit: 175.9%","3rd-Hit: 181.2%","4th-Hit: 405.3%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Naughty Cat Spotted","d":"During combat, when Sunna is off-field and there are no enemies with Cat\u0027s Gaze, Bubblegum consumes 1 Claw Sharpener to automatically launch an attack, dealing Physical DMG. When any squad member activates Ether Veil, Sunna gains 2 Claw Sharpeners. When any squad member applies an Anomaly to an enemy, Sunna gains 1 Claw Sharpeners. This effect can trigger at most once every 10s. Bubblegum inherits Sunna\u0027s initial ATK. Sunna can hold up to 6 Claw Sharpeners.","m":["208%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Star Shooter","d":"Press to activate. Shoots Bubblegum to attack enemies in front using an air gun, dealing Physical DMG. After activation, Bubblegum enters combat.","m":["56.4%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Bubblegum Barrage","d":"With enough energy, press to activate. Hurls Bubblegum at the target, dealing Physical DMG. After activation, Bubblegum enters combat. Upon activating this skill, all Agents in the squad gain Angelic Chord-ination for 40s. Landing a heavy attack with this skill triggers a Quick Assist. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Bubblegum Barrage: 913.3%","Bubblegum Barrage when quickly chaining into Special Photography Technique: 794.1%","Energy Cost: 70%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Special Photography Technique","d":"While in the Angelic Chord-ination state, press to activate, or during EX Special Attack: Bubblegum Barrage, keep holding to quickly activate: Attacks the target enemy in coordination with Bubblegum, dealing Physical DMG. After activation, Bubblegum enters combat. Before the heavy attack is executed, activates Ether Veil: Delusion Reprise. While Ether Veil: Delusion Reprise is active, all squad members gain an additional 50 ATK for 40s. Re-activating Ether Veil: Delusion Reprise will cancel the existing instance of Ether Veil: Delusion Reprise. Landing a heavy attack with this skill triggers a Quick Assist. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. EX Special Attack: Special Photography Technique can be used once each time Angelic Chord-ination state is entered.","m":["828.1%","DMG Multiplier (Coordinated): 952.4%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Can\u0027t Hit Me","d":"Press to activate. A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Skyward Hammer","d":"Press during a dodge to activate: Launches enemies in front into the air, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["99.7%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Delusion Strikeout","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Strikes enemies in front with a series of hammer blows, dealing Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["318.8%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Don\u0027t Mess With the Cat","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Charges forward on Bubblegum, dealing massive Physical DMG. Landing a heavy attack with this skill triggers a Quick Assist. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["811.3%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Smash It All!","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate: After a series of hammer attacks, launches Bubblegum to cause an explosion, dealing massive Physical DMG to enemies in an area. On activating the heavy attack, gain 6 Claw Sharpeners. Upon landing the downward attack from above on an enemy, a Quick Assist is triggered, restoring some HP to all squad members. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["2090.9%","HP Recovery: 200%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Sonic Beatdown","d":"When the active character is launched, press to activate. Unleash a series of hammer attacks against enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["72.7%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Stage Fright","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Jump Training","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate: Continuously jumps forward on the inflatable hammer, dealing massive Physical DMG to enemies in front. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["535.7%"]}],"build":{"w":["Kaboom the Cannon","Thoughtbop","Weeping Cradle","Dreamlit Hearth"],"a":["Moonlight Lullaby, Swing Jazz","Moonlight Lullaby, Astral Voice","Moonlight Lullaby, King of the Summit","Moonlight Lullaby, Hormone Punk"],"core":6.99,"st":[["CRIT Rate",17],["CRIT DMG",74],["ATK",3529]]},"how":"Sunna’s gameplan ends up being quite simple in practice: Use “EX Special: Bubblegum Barrage” to apply Angelic Chord-ination to the team. Use “EX Special: Special Photography Technique” to activate Ether Veil: Delusion Reprise and gain 2 Claw Sharpener stacks. Swap out of Sunna to an Attacker to trigger Cat’s Gaze After 25 second pass, swap back to Sunna for an EX Special to refresh Moonlight Lullaby. This can be a singular cast, so that her second EX Special can be reserved for another refresh later, or both consecutively if doing good on Energy. Repeat the above until near stun, before which her Ultimate should be used if available to cap out Claw Sharpener stacks and maximise Cat’s Gaze triggers in stun. There isn’t much more to this. Depending on the fight, gear and team, there are some minor optimizations and variances that one can do. Her high EX Special Energy cost can demand some early Basic Attacks for quick resource build, and depending on the W-Engine being used, having effective management of her EX Specials for Moonlight Lullaby upkeep is important. Learning to weave in single vs double EX Special casts for buff maintenance and not overcapping on Claw Sharpener stacks where possible is ideal to get the most value out of Sunna. Even still, one of her greatest advantages is ease of play, so making good use of it to focus on getting the most out of your other Agents is the way.","pros":"A relatively undiluted buff offering that is compatible with most Attackers, all the while being very easy to play. Absurdly good for teams that need frequent Ether Veil activation and fills in a niche for endgame buff requirements. Is often better or at least on par with other premium Supports for many Attackers. Forgiving skill and stat threshold requirements, being inexpensive to build and get Drive Discs for. No way!","cons":"Restricted to a small set of Agents (Attackers, same Faction) which limits how flexible she can be as a Support. Can be overly dependent on her Signature W-Engine in some teams, with a low base Energy Regen rate that is demanding to work around. Stun DMG Multiplier buff is a sizable portion of her power budget, meaning she can struggle in double DPS or double Support teams. No way!","teams":[{"m":"Ye Shunguang + Sunna + Zhao + Sprout","c":"","r":"Rank 3"},{"m":"Ye Shunguang + Dialyn + Sunna + Sprout","c":"","r":"Rank 4"},{"m":"Aria + Nangong Yu + Sunna + Biggest Fan","c":"","r":"Rank 18"}]},"Aria":{"slug":"aria","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Sweet Melody","d":"Press to activate: Launches up to four consecutive attacks forward, dealing Ether DMG. After hitting an enemy with the fourth hit, 1 Fandom Power is generated on the field after the attack ends.","m":["1st-Hit: 33.2%","2nd-Hit: 71.6%","3rd-Hit: 93.8%","4th-Hit: 194.2%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Perfect Pitch","d":"Hold to activate: Aria enters a charging state and can reach three levels of charge. Releasing or reaching the maximum charge time causes Aria to unleash a powerful downward attack forward based on the current charge level, dealing massive Ether DMG. If there is Fandom Power nearby while Aria is charging, she will absorb the Fandom Power, with each absorbed Fandom Power instantly increasing charge level by 1 and granting 1 stack of a buff that increases the next Basic Attack: Perfect Pitch\u0027s Ether Anomaly Buildup by 10%. This buff can stack up to 2 times and is removed after the attack ends. After the 4th hit of Basic Attack: Sweet Melody, Special Attack: Full-Sugar Electronica - No Ice, an EX Special Attack, the 3rd hit of Basic Attack: Perfect Pitch, a Quick Assist, a Chain Attack, or an Ultimate, if there are at least 2 Fandom Power nearby, hold to consume 2 Fandom Power and quickly activate the 3rd hit of Basic Attack: Perfect Pitch. After the 3rd hit of Basic Attack: Perfect Pitch, a Chain Attack, or an Ultimate, if there are at least 2 Fandom Power nearby, the 3rd hit of Basic Attack: Perfect Pitch can also be quickly activated by pressing within a short window, consuming 2 Fandom Power. Anti-Interrupt Level is increased while charging, and received DMG is reduced by 40%. Character is invulnerable while using this attack.","m":["Charge Level One Attack: 181.5%","Charge Level Two Attack: 207.2%","Charge Level Three Attack: 275%","Charge Level Three Attack (Coordinated): 316.3%","Enhanced Charge Attack: 320.9%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Full-Sugar Electronica","d":"Press to activate. Delivers a forward kick, dealing Ether DMG. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["54.3%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Full-Sugar Electronica - No Ice","d":"After the 4th hit of Basic Attack: Sweet Melody, an Assist Follow-Up, a Chain Attack, or an Ultimate, press to activate. Delivers a quicker forward kick, dealing Ether DMG. If the attack hits an enemy, 1 Fandom Power is generated on the field after the attack ends. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["64.8%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Fall Into Delusion","d":"With enough energy, press to activate: Delivers a powerful forward kick followed by a sonic wave attack, dealing Ether DMG. If the attack hits an enemy, 3 Fandom Power are generated on the field after the attack ends. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["511.2%","Energy Cost: 40%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Instantly Hooked","d":"After launching EX Special Attack: Fall Into Delusion, and with enough Energy, press to activate: Performs a powerful downward attack in front, dealing Ether DMG. If the attack hits an enemy, 3 Fandom Power are generated on the field after the attack ends. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["544.5%","Energy Cost: 40%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: On-Beat Precision","d":"Press to activate. A quick dash dodge. If activated during a Basic Attack: Sweet Melody chain, this action does not reset the Basic Attack count. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Silky-Smooth Combo","d":"Press during a dodge to activate: Flies forward with a swift slashing attack, dealing Ether DMG. If activated during a Basic Attack: Sweet Melody chain, this action does not reset the Basic Attack count.","m":["45.8%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Slide-Shift Variation","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Unleashes a powerful slash against the target, dealing Ether DMG. After using this skill, it can be immediately followed up with the 3rd hit of Basic Attack: Sweet Melody. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["241.2%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Dream Collab","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Launches a series of attacks forward, dealing massive Ether DMG. 4 Fandom Power are generated on the field on skill activation. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["816.2%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: 100% Energy","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate: Releases all her power, entering Moment of Delusion, and fires multiple powerful shots at the target, dealing massive Ether DMG. Upon entering Moment of Delusion, Aria gains 3 stacks of All-Out Cheering and activates Ether Veil: Delusion Reprise. While Ether Veil: Delusion Reprise is active, all squad members gain an additional 50 ATK for 30s. Re-activating Ether Veil: Delusion Reprise will first cancel any existing instance of Ether Veil: Delusion Reprise. While Aria is charging, if she has All-Out Cheering, stacks of All-Out Cheering are consumed first to charge. Each stack of All-Out Cheering consumed increases the charge level by 2. Upon entering Moment of Delusion, if Aria already has All-Out Cheering, all remaining stacks of All-Out Cheering are first converted into Fandom Power and generated on the field. Each stack of All-Out Cheering is converted into 2 Fandom Power. Moment of Delusion lasts for up to 15s. During Moment of Delusion, Aria\u0027s Basic Attack: Perfect Pitch 3rd hit is upgraded to an enhanced version. When exiting Moment of Delusion, if Aria has All-Out Cheering, all remaining stacks of All-Out Cheering are converted into Fandom Power and generated on the field. Each stack of All-Out Cheering is converted into 2 Fandom Power. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1622.5%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Shatter Fantasy","d":"When the active character is launched, press to activate. Delivers a powerful slash to the target, dealing Ether DMG. After using this skill, it can be immediately followed up with the 3rd hit of Basic Attack: Sweet Melody. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["49.6%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Clutch Save","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Encore Song","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate: Unleashes a powerful series of slashes on the target, dealing massive Ether DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["363.5%"]}],"build":{"w":["Angel in the Shell","Weeping Gemini","Flight of Fancy","Electro-Lip Gloss"],"a":["Shining Aria, Phaethon\u0027s Melody","Phaethon\u0027s Melody, Shining Aria","Phaethon\u0027s Melody, Freedom Blues","Phaethon\u0027s Melody, Chaos Jazz"],"core":6.99,"st":[["CRIT Rate",12],["CRIT DMG",65],["ATK",2595]]},"how":"Aria’s gameplan is fundamentally very simple: try to keep her on-field and land her Basic 4, alternate Special and EX Special to generate Fandom Power stacks, then consume them to both maintain Anomaly and deal damage via Ablooms on enemies with her Level 3 Perfect Pitch (enhanced Basic Attack). Be careful to not use it if enemies have no Anomaly on them, as Abloom will not trigger, and ideally have it be Anomaly sourced from a built character (avoid triggering it on an Anomaly built by a generic Support Agent for example). As stun approaches, save up at least 4 Fandom Power and energy for one EX Special, set-up buffs where needed, and then get ready to unload. Assuming that said resources have been built: Ultimate (Enemy Stuns) Cancel Chain Level 3 Perfect Pitch Level 3 Perfect Pitch Level 3 Perfect Pitch Level 3 Perfect Pitch Level 3 Perfect Pitch Level 3 Perfect Pitch Level 3 Perfect Pitch Swap to another character for an Ether Veil trigger (e.g. Sunna EX2 or Zhao) Aria Quick Assist Level 3 Perfect Pitch Level 3 Perfect Pitch EX Special Swap to another character to trigger Chain Aria Chain Attack Cancel Chain Level 3 Perfect Pitch Level 3 Perfect Pitch Level 3 Perfect Pitch Depending on the team and enemy stun duration, try to land somewhere between 10 to 12 Level 3 Perfect Pitch (enhanced Basic Attacks) during it. There are optimisations which ride on her team and Drive Disc set-ups. For example, if using Phaethon’s Melody, then ally EX Specials will need to be used before and during the combo (ideally during the Ether Veil trigger point). If there are no characters that can provide Ether Veil, then it’s far more important to have Ultimate be used before a stun, so that Aria can do double Chain Attacks and have enough Fandom Power generated from them to make up for the loss.","pros":"Incredibly high damage output on an element that has many weaknesses and few resistances. Low skill floor and has a variety of possible gearing options, making her very accessible. Less susceptible to Anomaly and Disorder ICD issues than other Anomaly Agents. Huh??","cons":"Is Anomaly but with a burst-focused playstyle that\u0027s dependent on stuns, limiting her team options. Can have tricky buff management depending on personal and team Drive Disc sets. Overly reliant on Ether Veils (and the other Idols really) for best performance. Bad rolls may make you suddenly more poor.","teams":[{"m":"Remielle + Aria + Velina + Ariel","c":"","r":"Rank 10"},{"m":"Aria + Nangong Yu + Sunna + Biggest Fan","c":"","r":"Rank 18"},{"m":"Aria + Nangong Yu + Yuzuha + Biggest Fan","c":"","r":"Rank 50"}]},"Zhao":{"slug":"zhao","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Glacial Judgment","d":"Press to activate: Launches up to five slashes forward, the first dealing Physical DMG, and the following four Ice DMG.","m":["1st-Hit: 73.4%","2nd-Hit: 66%","3rd-Hit: 115.8%","4th-Hit: 185.6%","5th-Hit: 386.4%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Final Verdict","d":"Hold to activate: After getting ready, Zhao starts charging up, then launches a forward slash on release, dealing massive Ice DMG. While charging, Zhao accumulates up to 5s of charge time. When the Finishing Move of Basic Attack: Final Verdict, Chain Attack, or Assist Follow-Up hits, the stored charge time is consumed to deal additional DMG. For every 1 second of charge time, Zhao deals some of Max HP as additional DMG. When Zhao is in any Ether Veil, if she gets switched out while charging, the charge can continue. If Frostbite Points are maxed out when the skill activates, all Frostbite Points are consumed to trigger Ether Veil: Wellspring and a Quick Assist. If a squadmate is then switched in via Quick Assist, Zhao automatically follows up with Basic Attack: Final Verdict and begins charging. During skill activation, Anti-Interrupt level increases, and DMG taken is reduced by 40%. While not the currently controlled character, the character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["69.7%","Max Health Extra Multiplier at Full Charge: 13%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Shatterfrost Surge","d":"Press to activate. Launches a forward slash, dealing Ice DMG. Upon activating this skill, consumes 5% of current HP to grant all squad members HP regeneration equal to 1.1-2% of Zhao\u0027s Max HP per second for 5s. The HP-consuming effects of Special Attack: Shatterfrost Surge and EX Special Attack: Frostflow Tundra can trigger at most once every 30s.","m":["56.9%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Frostflow Tundra","d":"With enough energy, press to activate. Launches multiple forward slashes, dealing massive Ice DMG. Upon activating this skill, consumes 5% of current HP to grant all squad members HP regeneration equal to 1.1-2% of Zhao\u0027s Max HP per second for 5s. The HP-consuming effects of Special Attack: Shatterfrost Surge and EX Special Attack: Frostflow Tundra can trigger at most once every 30s. Upon activating this skill, gain 20 Frostbite Points. If Frostbite Points are maxed out, all Frostbite Points are consumed to activate Ether Veil: Wellspring. Upon activating this skill while in any Ether Veil, a Quick Assist is triggered. If a squadmate is then switched in via Quick Assist, Zhao automatically follows up with Basic Attack: Final Verdict and begins charging. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1210.8%","Energy Cost: 80%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Bunny Hop","d":"Press to activate. A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Bouncing Dash","d":"Press during a dodge to activate: Slashes forward, dealing Physical DMG and Ice DMG.","m":["86.3%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Swift Blink","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Performs a falling slash ahead, dealing Ice DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["338.8%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Temporary Alliance","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Launches multiple slashes in front, dealing massive Ice DMG. After using this skill, gains 5 Frostbite Points. If Frostbite Points are maxed out, all Frostbite Points are consumed to activate Ether Veil: Wellspring. Upon activating this skill while in any Ether Veil, a Quick Assist is triggered. If a squadmate is then switched in via Quick Assist, Zhao automatically follows up with Basic Attack: Final Verdict and begins charging. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["770.8%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Bunny Barrage","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate: Launches consecutive attacks in front, followed by a falling slash, dealing massive Ice DMG. After using this skill, gains 20 Frostbite Points. If Frostbite Points are maxed out, all Frostbite Points are consumed to activate Ether Veil: Wellspring. Upon activating this skill while in any Ether Veil, a Quick Assist is triggered. If a squadmate is then switched in via Quick Assist, Zhao automatically follows up with Basic Attack: Final Verdict and begins charging. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["2187.3%"]},{"t":"Entry","n":"Entry Skill: Burst of Frost","d":"When Zhao has maximum Frostbite Points, and is in combat, press to activate. Launches consecutive attacks forward, followed by a slash, dealing massive Ice DMG. Upon activating this skill, all Frostbite Points are consumed to activate Ether Veil: Wellspring. Upon activating this skill, a Quick Assist is triggered. If a squadmate is then switched in via Quick Assist, Zhao automatically follows up with Basic Attack: Final Verdict and begins charging. Activating this skill is considered as activating a Quick Assist. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["680.3%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Patch the Gaps","d":"When the active character is launched, press to activate. Launches a falling slash in front, dealing Ice DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["176%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Frostveil Suppression","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. This skill excels at parrying enemy attacks and reduces the consumption of Assist Points when the character is under intense attacks. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Frostlight Reflection","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate: Launch multiple slashes in front, dealing massive Ice DMG. Upon activating this skill, if Frostbite Points are maxed out, all Frostbite Points are consumed to activate Ether Veil: Wellspring. Upon activating this skill while in any Ether Veil, a Quick Assist is triggered. If a squadmate is then switched in via Quick Assist, Zhao automatically follows up with Basic Attack: Final Verdict and begins charging. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["366.1%"]}],"build":{"w":["Original Transmorpher","Half-Sugar Bunny","Tusks of Fury","Bunny Band"],"a":["Astral Voice, Yunkui Tales","Bunny in Wonderland, Yunkui Tales","Bunny in Wonderland, Moonlight Lullaby","Astral Voice, Moonlight Lullaby"],"core":6.97,"st":[["CRIT Rate",20],["CRIT DMG",80],["ATK",2056]]},"how":"Zhao is a very straightforward character to play: the less time you spend on her, the better she’ll do. As almost all of her attacks lead to Final Verdict, which itself is cast while Zhao is inactive, it\u0027s always better to spend time productively on another Agent. She does need to be occasionally swapped to, such as for EX Special use when Energy allows for, the occasional Ultimate, and - depending on the fight and Decibel requirements - some Defensive Assists and Assist Follow-Ups owing to the reduced Assist Point cost. Be sure to consume her Frostbite Points to activate Ether Veil: Wellspring often. There’s little active management required, as it rarely ever builds faster than 40 seconds, meaning that in most circumstances, it should be used whenever points max out so as to avoid overcapping. That is truly all there is to her. Cycle through her resources quickly so that she can maintain Ether Veil: Wellspring up at all times. If that isn’t possible, then some planning may be required to make sure it is at the very least activated in time for critical burst periods, but even then, the way Zhao is played remains the same. The decision of when and how often to swap to her, rather than what exactly to do when playing her, is most critical to her best performance.","pros":"Universally strong supportive Agent that slots in with most Agents. Easy to play and easy to build, with low field time and investment commitments. Is being handed out for free to all players. May be small, but packs a hell of a punch.","cons":"Not a best-in-slot pick for any team but 1 (Ye Shunguang), limiting her longevity. A fair amount of her power budget is in her Signature W-Engine. Defence class lacks Drive Discs and can still be restrictive when team building. Do you see what Damian has to go through?","teams":[{"m":"Ye Shunguang + Sunna + Zhao + Sprout","c":"","r":"Rank 3"},{"m":"Ye Shunguang + Dialyn + Zhao + Sprout","c":"","r":"Rank 5"},{"m":"Ye Shunguang + Astra Yao + Zhao + Sprout","c":"","r":"Rank 22"}]},"Manato":{"slug":"manato","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Blazing Wind Slash","d":"Press to activate: Perform up to three forward slashes, dealing Physical DMG. During each slash, pressing triggers Scorchwind, causing the attack to deal increased Fire DMG.","m":["1st-Hit: 28.7%","2nd-Hit: 82.7%","3rd-Hit: 134.6%","1st-Hit (Triggering Scorchwind): 63.1%","2nd-Hit (Triggering Scorchwind): 95.5%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Blazing Wind - Misty Slash","d":"While in the Molten Edge state, press to activate: Unleash up to four forward slashes, dealing Fire DMG. If Manato\u0027s HP is above 30% when the skill is activated, 3.5% of his Max HP will be consumed.","m":["1st-Hit: 53.1%","2nd-Hit: 111.2%","3rd-Hit: 154.5%","4th-Hit: 237.8%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Return to Ashes","d":"Press to activate. Slash forward at enemies, dealing Fire DMG. If hit by an enemy during the skill, restore 20% of missing HP when unleashing the slash. The healing effects of Special Attack: Return to Ashes and Special Attack: Return to Ashes - Sacrifice have a shared cooldown and can trigger once every 20s. If hit by an enemy during the skill, the slash is enhanced. DMG taken is reduced by 40% while using this skill. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["50.7%","(Charged or Successful Block): 130.7%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Return to Ashes - Sacrifice","d":"Hold to activate. Enter a charging state, consuming up to 10% of Max HP and gaining 100 Blazing Heart. HP consumption will at most reduce Manato\u0027s HP to 30% of Max HP. Release the button to activate Special Attack: Return to Ashes. If struck during the skill, the slash heals 20% of missing HP. The healing effects of Special Attack: Return to Ashes and Special Attack: Return to Ashes - Sacrifice have a shared cooldown and can trigger once every 20s. If hit by an enemy during the skill or if charging reaches a certain duration, the slash is enhanced. DMG taken is reduced by 40% while using this skill. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Return to Ashes - Fall","d":"While in the Molten Edge state and with sufficient Adrenaline, press to activate: Jump up and unleash a falling slash on enemies in front, dealing massive Fire DMG. Upon activating the skill, restore 33% of Max HP. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["652.6%","Adrenaline Cost: 80%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Radiant Blade","d":"Press to activate. A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Radiant Blade - Zanshin","d":"Press during a dodge to activate: Deliver a quick strike forward, dealing Ether DMG.","m":["58.7%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Radiant Blade - Battle Sweep","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Perform a slash followed by a punch at enemies ahead, dealing Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["198%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Blazing Eruption","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Hurls his sword forward, then charges the enemy to trigger an explosion, dealing massive Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["483.3%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Charge, Great Armor!","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate. Jump into the air and deliver a falling slash at enemies in front, followed by an explosion, dealing massive Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while performing the powerful strike.","m":["1562.3%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Lone Shadow - Regroup","d":"When the active character is launched, press to activate. Slashes and punches enemies in front, dealing Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["90.7%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Lone Shadow - Mountain Stand","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, inflicting massive Daze and dealing Fire DMG. Gain 75 Blazing Heart upon activating this skill. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["40%","Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Lone Shadow - Breaking Fang","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate: Unleash multiple slashes at enemies ahead, dealing Fire DMG. Repeated presses allow up to 7 extra consecutive slashes. During the consecutive slashes, if Manato\u0027s HP is above 30%, 2% of Max HP is consumed. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. The DMG taken during the consecutive slashes is reduced by 60%, and Anti-Interrupt Level is increased.","m":["166.7%","Combo Maximum: 570.1%"]}],"build":{"w":["Grill O\u0027Wisp","Wrathful Vajra"],"a":["Yunkui Tales, Branch \u0026 Blade Song","Yunkui Tales, Woodpecker Electro","Yunkui Tales, Flex","Yunkui Tales, Inferno Metal"],"core":7,"st":[["CRIT Rate",51],["CRIT DMG",147],["ATK",1869]]},"how":"$undefined","pros":"Strong DPS performance for an A-rank; Has good and accessible W-Engine choices; Part of the rare Rupture class that is against specific enemies and which can take advantage of specific endgame buffs.","cons":"Needs a lot of skills levelled up for damage - expensive on resources; Has many team options, but definitely wants to be played with Lucia and loses significant power without her Mindscapes alter his playstyle and can significantly boost performance.","teams":[{"m":"Manato + Norma + Lucia + Ultra Jake","c":"","r":"Rank 202"},{"m":"Manato + Dialyn + Lucia + Birkblick","c":"","r":"Rank 280"},{"m":"Manato + Roxy + Lucia + Miss Esme","c":"","r":"Rank 388"}]},"Piper":{"slug":"piper","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Load Up and Roll Out","d":"Press to activate: Unleashes up to 4 slashes, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["1st-Hit: 59%","2nd-Hit: 78.8%","3rd-Hit: 150.1%","4th-Hit: 320.6%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Tire Spin","d":"Press to activate. Piper spins and launches a sweeping slash around her, dealing Physical DMG. Hold to extend the skill duration, unleashing increasingly powerful spinning slashes and increasing the charge level of the skill, up to 2 times. If the skill is used after the first 3 hits of a Basic Attack, Dash Attack, or Dodge Counter, you can quickly activate Special Attack: Tire Spin of an increased charged level. During the skill activation, Anti-Interrupt level increases, and DMG taken is reduced by 40%.","m":["271.7%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Engine Spin","d":"With enough energy, continue holding after Special Attack: Tire Spin reaches maximum charge level to activate: Rapidly spins, unleashing powerful spinning slashes around her, dealing massive Physical DMG. This skill consumes Energy continuously for up to 3s. During the skill activation, Anti-Interrupt level increases, and DMG taken is reduced by 40%.","m":["93.5%","Energy Cost per second: 20%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: One Trillion Tons","d":"While Special Attack: Tire Spin is active, release to trigger a downward smash attack based on the charge level of Special Attack: Tire Spin, dealing Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Level-1 Charged Attack: 93.4%","Level-2 Charged Attack: 103.4%","Level-3 Charged Attack: 235%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Really Heavy","d":"During EX Special Attack: Engine Spin, release to activate: Piper unleashes a downward smash attack, dealing massive Physical DMG. If the duration of EX Special Attack: Engine Spin reaches its limit or Energy drops to 20, EX Special Attack: Really Heavy will automatically activate. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["612.9%","Energy Cost: 20%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Handbrake Drift","d":"Press to dodge. A rapid dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Pedal to the Metal","d":"Press during a dodge to activate. Slashes enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["90.1%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Power Drift","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Unleash a downward smash attack in front, dealing Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["269%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Buckle Up","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate. Unleashes a powerful downward smash at enemies ahead in a large area, dealing massive Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["652.3%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Hold On Tight","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate. Rapidly spins, unleashing powerful spinning slashes at enemies in a large area ahead, followed by a downward smash, dealing massive Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1660.4%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Brake Tap","d":"When the on-field character is launched, press to activate. Launches a downward smash attack at enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["130%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Emergency Brake","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, inflicting massive Daze. This skill excels at parrying enemy attacks and reduces the consumption of Assist Points when the character is under intense attacks. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Overtaking Maneuver","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate. Charge and slash enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["400.5%"]}],"build":{"w":["Roaring Ride","Practiced Perfection","Fusion Compiler","Weeping Gemini"],"a":["Fanged Metal, Freedom Blues","Freedom Blues, Fanged Metal","Fanged Metal, Phaethon\u0027s Melody","Fanged Metal, Chaos Jazz"],"core":6.97,"st":[["CRIT Rate",13],["CRIT DMG",64],["ATK",2845]]},"how":"$undefined","pros":"Very accessible and really good damage for an A-rank under the right conditions. Cheap to invest into, doesn\u0027t need skill level-ups, and has great F2P and premium W-Engine choices. Shares build with her competitors (Jane and Alice), contributing to her accessibility even more. Very easy to play at a baseline while retaining room for optimization.","cons":"A lot of her damage potential is locked behind Alice\u0027s Signature Practiced Perfection and Yuzuha. Her options outside of Vivian teams face a significant drop in power, and the competitors in her niche are directly competing for these teammates as well. Can have moments of vulnerability when played with focus on lengthy channelled EX Specials.","teams":[{"m":"Remielle + Piper + Velina + Ariel","c":"","r":"Rank 69"},{"m":"Remielle + Jane Doe + Piper + Ariel","c":"","r":"Rank 177"},{"m":"Piper + Velina + Yuzuha + Ultra Jake","c":"","r":"Rank 280"}]},"Claret":{"slug":"claret","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Bloodforging Four Forms ","d":"Press to activate: Performs up to four strikes forward, dealing Electric DMG.","m":["1st-Hit: 54.4%","2nd-Hit: 67.2%","3rd-Hit: 95.2%","4th-Hit: 289.5%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Bloodbloom Oath - Starforging ","d":"Press while in the Crimson Inscription state to activate: Use the Blood Axe to perform up to three slashes forward, dealing Electric DMG. When the second attack is launched, Claret leaps backward and throws the Blood Axe. A Perfect Dodge can be triggered during the retreat. When the third attack is launched, Claret performs a series of slashes before leaping up and performing a downward smash. During the repeated slashes, Anti-Interrupt Level is increased, and DMG taken is reduced by 40%. Repeatedly press or hold to extend the duration of the repeated slashes. Stop pressing or release to make Claret immediately leap up and perform a downward smash. A Perfect Dodge can be triggered while leaping. After successfully triggering a Perfect Dodge, press or hold to follow up with the 3rd hit of Basic Attack: Bloodbloom Oath - Starforging. Crimson Inscription will not end during this skill.","m":["1st-Hit: 107.7%","2nd-Hit: 287.4%","3rd Hit Consecutive Slashes: 452.1%","3rd Hit Downward Strike: 177.3%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Bloodbloom Oath - Subduing Axe","d":"While in the Crimson Inscription state, after launching [Special Attack: Bloodbloom Oath - Cleaving Gold and Iron] or [Special Attack: Bloodbloom Oath - Blood Burial Assault] and successfully triggering [Maim], press or hold to activate: Use the Blood Axe to spin and leap into the air, then slam down and slash the target enemy, dealing Electric DMG. A Perfect Dodge can be triggered while leaping. After using this skill, press or hold to chain into the 3rd hit of [Basic Attack: Bloodbloom Oath - Starforging]. [Crimson Inscription] will not end during this skill.","m":["328%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Night Vision ","d":"Press to activate: A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Tempering ","d":"While not in the Crimson Inscription state, press during a Dodge to activate: Perform a forward hammer strike, dealing Electric DMG.","m":["52.9%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Returning Edge ","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate: Use the hammer handle to deliver a powerful forward counterattack, dealing Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill","m":["272.5%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Bloodbloom Oath - Returning Edge","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate: Use the Blood Axe to deliver a powerful forward counterattack, dealing Electric DMG. Crimson Inscription will not end during this skill. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["330%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Return of the Dire Moon ","d":"When the active character is launched, press to activate: Deals Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["52.9%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Bloodbloom Oath - Return of the Dire Moon ","d":"When the active character is launched, press to activate: Deals Electric DMG. Crimson Inscription will not end during this skill. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["115.8%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Unyielding Heart of the Furnace ","d":"When the on-field character is about to be attacked, press to activate: Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. Crimson Inscription will not end during this skill. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Bloodbloom Oath - Pureforged Edge ","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate: Deals massive Electric DMG. Crimson Inscription will not end during this skill. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["446.2%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Counter Assist: Give Not an Inch of Steel ","d":"When the character or the on-field character is about to be hit by a Control Skill from certain enemies, press to activate: Engage the enemy in a power struggle. Win the struggle to neutralize the enemy\u0027s Control Skill and deal Electric DMG. Crimson Inscription\u0027s duration does not decrease during this skill. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1153%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Bloodbloom Oath - Hammer Into Shape ","d":"After using a Counter Assist, press to activate: Deals massive Electric DMG. When the heavy attack hits an enemy, it adds one stack of Gash to the target. Crimson Inscription\u0027s duration does not decrease during this skill. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["856.3%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Porcelume\u0027s First Call ","d":"Press to activate: Launch two bludgeoning attacks forward, dealing Electric DMG. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["90.1%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Bloodbloom Oath - Secret Forging Techniques","d":"With enough Sharpness, and while Claret is not in the Crimson Inscription state, press to activate: Transforms the forging hammer into the Blood Axe to slash the target enemy, dealing Electric DMG. After using this skill, Claret enters the Crimson Inscription state for 16s. While off-field, its duration no longer decreases. When Claret\u0027s attacks hit an enemy, if the enemy is defeated within 0.5s, the duration of Crimson Inscription is extended by 3s. This effect can trigger once every 3s. During this skill, keep holding Icon_SpecialReady_Ep to skip the slash and quickly chain into the alternate Special Attack: Bloodbloom Oath - Cleaving Gold and Iron and Special Attack: Bloodbloom Oath - Blood Burial Assault. After using this skill, press or hold to chain into the 3rd hit of Basic Attack: Bloodbloom Oath - Starforging. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["624.8%","Sharpness Cost: 60%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Bloodbloom Oath - Cleaving Gold and Iron","d":"While in the Crimson Inscription state, press or to activate: Perform a powerful upward slash forward, then follow up with a horizontal Slash, dealing Electric DMG. When the horizontal Slash hits an enemy suffering [Gash], inflict [Maim] on the target, dealing additional AoE Electric DMG. [Crimson Inscription] will not end during this skill. Anti-Interrupt Level is increased during this skill. After successfully triggering [Maim], Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Upward Attack: 76.6%","Horizontal Slash: 87.7%","Maim: 812.7%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Bloodbloom Oath - Blood Burial Assault","d":"While in the Crimson Inscription state and the upward slash of Special Attack: Bloodbloom Oath - Cleaving Gold and Iron, keep holding or to activate: Perform three consecutive horizontal slashes forward, dealing massive Electric DMG; Each horizontal slash that hits an enemy holding [Gash] triggers [Maim] on the target, dealing additional AoE Electric DMG. Up to 3 consecutive instances of [Maim] can be triggered during this skill, with the 3rd [Maim] having a higher Interrupt Level; Crimson Inscription will not end during this skill; Anti-Interrupt Level is increased during this skill. After successfully triggering [Maim], Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["312.8%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Bloodbloom Oath - Resonant Blood Pact","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Launch a series of slashes against enemies ahead, dealing massive Electric DMG. Crimson Inscription\u0027s duration does not decrease, and the state does not end during this skill. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1058%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Bloodbloom Oath - Trial After Trial","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate: Launch a series of slashes against enemies ahead, dealing massive Electric DMG; During this skill, Crimson Inscription\u0027s duration does not decrease, and the state does not end; Upon activating this skill, restore 10 Sharpness; Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["2252%"]}],"build":{"w":["Crimson Thirst","Catty Luck","Bloodmarrow Coffer","Candlelit Scheme"],"a":["Thorned Rose, Woodpecker Electro","Thorned Rose, Puffer Electro","Thorned Rose, Branch \u0026 Blade Song","Thorned Rose, Soul Rock"],"core":7,"st":[["CRIT Rate",91],["CRIT DMG",99],["ATK",1032]]},"how":"Claret’s game plan is simple but can be difficult to pull off in an actual run. Her EX Special is used to enter the Crimson Inscription state, and during it, use her enhanced Basic Attacks to apply Gash to enemies. If at risk of over-capping, her tap Special can be used to trigger 1 Maim and ensure she’s always building gauge. This can be difficult to do, though, as the time it takes for Claret to build 3 Gash stacks is enough to have her Crimson Inscription state be close to running out in many teams and encounters. So swapping out of her while building Gash to quickly apply Daze and refresh ally buffs can take precedence over out-of-stun Maim triggers. Certain Agents can help manage this, like Norma with her Chain Attack conversion, but the balance of how much time to spend on Claret vs other Agents ranges from team to team. What’s most important is to have at least 3 Gash stacks ready for when stun begins and enough time in the Crimson Inscription state that’ll last long enough to cover a hold Special. If Claret has her Ultimate available, she can fall back on this combo structure: Hold Special to trigger 3 Maims. Swap out of her and trigger Claret’s Chain Attack. Cancel the Chain, then go into a Basic 3 shortcut - this builds 1 Gash stack. Swap out of her and trigger Claret’s Chain Attack again. Shortcut into her Basic 3 Once the Basic 3 builds the second Gash stack, use Claret’s Ultimate, building the final Gash stack. Hold Special to trigger 3 Maims. Even against 12s base Stun duration enemies and without any extensions, this can fit in full. Other Agent skills can then be integrated into this, like making use of Quick Assists after the second Chain Attack to refresh Astral Voice, or using Norma’s Chain Attack conversion at the end for more damage. The Chain Attacks and Crimson Inscription duration pauses means that so long as Claret can go into the first while the state is active, she’s likely to be able to perform the full combo. Most optimisation then comes in managing how she’s played out-of-stun, as different teams and counters demand different routes to sustain her gauge and maximise Maims over the course of a fight.","pros":"Low-skill floor, high skill ceiling, and all-around high-performing, introducing a brand-new system to the game that can open up new routes. Exceptionally high burst damage and accommodating stun combos, not needing a specific character to sustain her game plan. Has the potential to get even better in the future, as more Armorer Agents and matching Stunners/Supports are released. Yeah, I ship it.","cons":"Crimson Inscription management can be tricky and can demand proper routing to maintain it in full. Armorer mechanics and being the first of her class mean she has few good synergies and limited teams. Few W-Engine alternatives to her Signature, being highly dependent on it for best performance. Needs to be bribed (with compliments) for any negotiations to proceed.","teams":[{"m":"norma, roxy + rina, nicole-demara","c":"","r":""},{"m":"koleda, lycaon + rina, nicole-demara","c":"","r":""},{"m":"trigger + nicole-demara","c":"","r":""}]},"Nekomata":{"slug":"nekomata","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Kitty Slash","d":"Press to activate. Unleashes up to 5 slashes, dealing Physical DMG. When the final slash lands on a Stunned enemy, it repeats three additional times.","m":["1st-Hit: 55.2%","2nd-Hit: 62.6%","3rd-Hit: 72.7%","4th-Hit: 170.2%","5th-Hit: 123.6%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Crimson Blade","d":"Hold down during the first 3 hits of Nekomata\u0027s Basic Attack to activate. Slashes enemies in front and passes through them, dealing Physical DMG. If this skill hits a Stunned enemy, it repeats three additional times.","m":["71.8%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Surprise Attack","d":"Press to activate. Unleashes a downward strike, dealing Physical DMG. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill. This skill\u0027s pursuit effect is enhanced.","m":["47.3%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Super Surprise Attack!","d":"With enough energy, press to activate. Unleashes a powerful falling slash, dealing massive Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. This skill\u0027s pursuit effect is enhanced.","m":["539.7%","Energy Cost: 40%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Can\u0027t Touch Me-ow~","d":"Press to activate: A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Over Here!","d":"Press during a dodge to activate. Slashes enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["35.1%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Phantom Claws","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Slashes enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["227.9%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Claw Swipe","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate. Unleashes a powerful slash at enemies ahead in a large area, dealing massive Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["536.2%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Claw Smash","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate. Unleashes powerful slashes at enemies ahead in a large area, dealing massive Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1571.1%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Cat\u0027s Paw","d":"When the on-field character is launched, press to activate. Slashes enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["94.5%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Desperate Defense","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate: Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Shadow Strike","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate. Charge and slash enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["300.4%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Disappearing Tail","d":"With at least 40 Purr Energy and after triggering a Perfect Dodge, press and consume 30 Purr Energy to activate: Nekomata enters Vital View and swiftly moves behind the enemy. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. This skill does not consume dodge uses.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Fluffy Piercing Claw","d":"Press after using Dodge: Disappearing Tail, or hold with at least 40 Purr Energy to activate: Unleashes a powerful slash at enemies in a large area ahead, dealing massive Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1263.9%","Purr Energy Cost: 40%"]}],"build":{"w":["Steel Cushion","The Brimstone","Starlight Engine","Cordis Germina"],"a":["Woodpecker Electro, Puffer Electro","Woodpecker Electro, Branch \u0026 Blade Song","Woodpecker Electro, Fanged Metal","Woodpecker Electro, Astral Voice"],"core":6.98,"st":[["CRIT Rate",84],["CRIT DMG",145],["ATK",3090]]},"how":"Nekomata’s gameplan revolves around getting as many of her enhanced Dodge Counters out in burst periods as possible. As her Purr Energy generates passively, optimisation lies in management of the resource. The goal is to go into stun with as much Purr Energy as possible, unleashing her enhanced Dodge Counter, then making use of EX Specials, Chain Attacks and Ultimates to build it back up for 3 uses. Having it be used early is important to get the Pawpad Ambush state active early and keep the natural Purr Energy regeneration going. Depending on how the fight lines up, it can be worth using her Dodge: Disappearing Tail to activate at least 1 stack of its buff early, but many of the fights Nekomata is best used for (like Thrall) may not afford the time for this to be done without sacrificing on Purr Energy availability in stun. Some fights with low Stun DMG Multipliers and extended invulnerability phases (like Defiler) could allow for an occasional use, so tailor it to the encounter. A sample combo with 60 Purr Energy at the start would be: Stun begins Dodge Counter: Fluffy Piercing Claw EX Special Chain Attack Cancel EX Special Chain Attack Dodge Counter: Fluffy Piercing Claw Ultimate Dodge Counter: Fluffy Piercing Claw As enemies tend to be stunned for almost 15s (12s base, then additional 3 seconds from stun recalcs), the Purr Energy generation should be able to sustain use of a third enhanced Dodge Counter at the very end. Characters like Dialyn and Norma make this even easier owing to the stun extension, and fitting in an Ultimate conversion or extra Chain Attack respectively gives even more resources to allow for 3 enhanced Dodge Counters in a stun.","pros":"Standard Agent that’s easy to get and isn’t overly dependent on a single Agent or synergy to do well, being an accessible DPS for all accounts. Can keep up and even surpass many limited Attackers in damage output. Incredibly good vertical throughout, making losing the 50/50 to her a passable consolation prize. Remember all of those “NEKOMATA IS BROKEN” YouTube thumbnail memes with Astra as the punchline? Turns out Nekomata got the last laugh.","cons":"Maintaining her Additional Ability can be difficult while still managing enough Purr Energy for multiple enhanced Dodge Counters in stun. Steep CRIT Rate demands, which can make building her effectively difficult. Reliant on Mindscapes and W-Engine dupes to truly shine, with a sizable performance gap between M0W1 and M6W5. Now that her Mindscapes are worth something, all your 50/50 failures are doomed to be Koleda instead.","teams":[{"m":"Nekomata + Dialyn + Sunna + Birkblick","c":"","r":"Rank 56"},{"m":"Nekomata + Dialyn + Astra Yao + Snap","c":"","r":"Rank 76"},{"m":"Nekomata + Norma + Sunna + Bangvolver","c":"","r":"Rank 136"}]},"Norma":{"slug":"norma","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Engineering Insurance","d":"Press to activate: Performs up to four attacks forward, dealing Fire DMG.","m":["1st-Hit: 26.1%","2nd-Hit: 37.8%","3rd-Hit: 73.3%","4th-Hit: 140.9%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Hat Trick","d":"When Norma is the active character and is in combat, she gains 1.5% [Preheated Chamber] per second. When [Top Hat Companion] is on her head, hold to activate: After firing, Norma throws out [Top Hat Companion], ordering it to unleash a round of aerial fire, dealing Fire DMG and storing the current [Preheated Chamber]. When the skill hits an enemy, it triggers the previous character\u0027s [Quick Assist]. This effect can trigger once every 5s. Once [Top Hat Companion] has been thrown out, it will accumulate and retain [Preheated Chamber] at the same speed on behalf of Norma. Norma does not need to stay on the field during this period. After Norma retrieves the [Top Hat Companion], she immediately gains the stored [Preheated Chamber]. When holding , the [Top Hat Companion] will accelerate toward Norma. If retrieving the [Top Hat Companion] would raise [Preheated Chamber] to 80% or higher, the [Top Hat Companion] will automatically accelerate toward Norma. When Norma switches from on field to off field while in combat, if [Preheated Chamber] is not full, [Top Hat Companion] automatically enters the battlefield. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["56.9%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Development Protocols","d":"Press to activate: A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Deadline Rush","d":"Press during a dodge to activate: Spins while firing at nearby enemies, dealing Fire DMG.","m":["82.3%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Compliance Testing","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate: Commands the Rumble Drill to continuously drill the target, dealing Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["313.1%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Roaring Backup","d":"When the active character is launched, press to activate: Commands the Rumble Drill to continuously attack the target, dealing Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["70.5%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Technological Bastion","d":"When the on-field character is about to be attacked, press to activate: Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. This skill excels at parrying enemy attacks and reduces the consumption of Assist Points when the character is under intense attacks. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Technological Suppression","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate: Unleashes a series of attacks, dealing Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["450.8%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Thermal Shutdown","d":"Press to activate: Bombards enemies, dealing Fire DMG.","m":["15%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: En-Nah Barrage","d":"With enough Energy, press to activate: Operates the turret to fire continuously and launch different types of missiles based on the target\u0027s state: When the primary target is not Stunned, launches an Armor-Piercing Warhead, dealing Fire DMG and inflicting a large amount of Daze. When the primary target is Stunned, launches a High-Explosive Warhead, dealing greater Fire DMG. After using this skill, Norma gains 16% Preheated Chamber and enters the En-Nah Barrage state for 32s. While En-Nah Barrage is active, Norma deploys two En-Nah Turrets to join the battle. Continuing to hold extends the firing time by up to 2s, continuously consuming energy. For each 1 point of energy consumed while holding, Norma gains an additional 0.4% Preheated Chamber, and this round of En-Nah Barrage lasts 0.8s longer, up to a maximum additional duration of 32s. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Shot: 205.4%","Armor-Piercing Warhead: 308%","High-Explosive Warhead: 341.4%","Energy Cost: 40%","Extended Shot Per Sec: 130.6%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Target Practice","d":"During battle, En-Nah Turrent automatically attacks enemies, dealing Fire DMG.","m":["195%","Auto-Fire Interval: 3%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Explosive Experiment","d":"When any squad member Stuns an enemy, or when Norma consumes Preheated Chamber to trigger a Chain Attack En-Nah Turrent, deploys its missile bay for 8s. Repeated triggers reset the duration. During this time, En-Nah Turrets automatically attack more frequently. When performing automatic attacks, they launch different missiles based on the enemy\u0027s state: When the primary target is not Stunned, launch an Armor-Piercing Warhead, dealing Fire DMG and inflicting a large amount of Daze. When the primary target is Stunned, launch a High-Explosive Warhead, dealing greater Fire DMG.","m":["Additional Armor-Piercing Warhead: 82.8%","Additional High-Explosive Warhead: 92.3%","Enhanced Form Auto-Fire Interval: 2%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Impact Drill","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Commands a swarm of Rumble Drills to deal multiple hits, dealing massive Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["752.7%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Doctrine of Superior Firepower","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate: Calls in tactical artillery to bombard enemies ahead, dealing massive Fire DMG. Upon activation, immediately gains 30% Preheated Chamber. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1936.5%"]}],"build":{"w":["Chief Sidekick","Hellfire Gears","Steam Oven","The Simmering Pot"],"a":["King of the Summit, Woodpecker Electro","King of the Summit, Moonlight Lullaby","King of the Summit, Swing Jazz","Astral Voice, Woodpecker Electro"],"core":6.99,"st":[["CRIT Rate",95],["CRIT DMG",103],["ATK",2306]]},"how":"Norma isn’t the kind of Agent that is going to be active much, so the fundamentals of her gameplan aren’t hard to grasp: Use her EX Special early! This puts her in the En-Nah Barrage state and ensures she’s building up Daze and dealing damage through turrets. Swap out of Norma and keep her off-field, as many W-Engine effects - like her Signature’s or Hellfire Gears - demand it. If needed, make use of her low Assist Point cost Defensive Assist to get a quick boost of Daze and Decibels. Try to use her EX Special every 15 seconds for King of the Summit, and make sure to have the Energy for it when Stun begins to refresh the buff. Halfway during a stun combo (ideally after 8 seconds, to get the most value out of her enhanced turrets), use her hold Basic to get an extra Chain Attack on a DPS. Repeat all of the above, making use of her Ultimate for faster stuns and more Preheated Chamber. Certain Agents may benefit from having extra Chain Attacks be used out of Stun instead (like Hugo, or Soldier 11 if Astra’s Ultimate is used), as not all combos will be accommodating of the time taken on them. On the aggregate though, a simple approach of “Use EX Specials often, parry occasionally, hold Basic for an extra Chain Attack in Stun” is good to start with, then tailor a route to an individual team and fight.","pros":"Builds a decent amount of Daze with very little field-time needed, making it easy to sit on other Agents for damage and resources instead. Notable personal damage despite being a Stunner, elevating weaker Agents while still contributing to stronger teams. Being able to provide a free Chain Attack to allies is especially useful for both damage and Decibels. Has a literal Bangboo inside her hat.","cons":"Lacking in burst Daze application outside of her Ultimate, limiting her prospects against certain bosses. Needs to be built with good substat rolls for her damage contribution to really make a difference. Very reliant on her W-Engine for best performance, especially when paired with weaker teammates. Will she be to 3.X what Ju Fufu was to 2.X…?","teams":[{"m":"pyrois + sunna, astra-yao, nicole-demara","c":"","r":""},{"m":"soldier-11 + sunna, astra-yao, nicole-demara","c":"","r":""},{"m":"cissia, orphie-and-magus + sunna, astra-yao, nicole-demara","c":"","r":""}]},"Ellen":{"slug":"ellen","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Saw Teeth Trimming","d":"Press to activate. Unleashes up to 3 slashes, dealing Physical DMG. Press repeatedly or hold during the 3rd attack to extend the skill duration.","m":["1st-Hit: 48.8%","2nd-Hit: 111.1%","3rd-Hit: 297.3%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Flash Freeze Trimming","d":"While Flash Freeze is in effect, press to activate. Launch up to 3 attacks at enemies in front, dealing Ice DMG. Each attack consumes 1 Flash Freeze Charge. Press repeatedly or hold during the 3rd attack to extend the skill duration.","m":["1st-Hit: 99.6%","2nd-Hit: 184%","3rd-Hit: 496.2%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Glacial Blade Wave","d":"After the 3rd hit of Basic Attack: Flash Freeze Trimming, Dash Attack: Arctic Ambush\u0027s charged scissor strike, Dodge Counter: Reef Rock, and Quick Assist, if Ellen has Flash Freeze Charges, pressing will launch Basic Attack: Glacial Blade Wave, dealing Ice DMG. This skill consumes 2 points of Flash Freeze Charge. After use, it can be directly followed up with the 3rd hit of her Basic Attack. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1st-Hit: 230.2%","2nd-Hit: 146.8%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Icy Blade","d":"After the 3rd hit of Basic Attack: Flash Freeze Trimming, EX Special Attack: Sharknami, Dodge Counter: Reef Rock, and Assist Follow-Up, automatically launch Basic Attack: Icy Blade, dealing multiple instances of Ice DMG to all enemies in a large area ahead. It inflicts additional instances of Ice DMG against Medium and Large foes. After the skill, Ellen gains the Quick Charge effect. Basic Attack: Icy Blade does not affect the branch or form of the original skill. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Multiplier to Small Enemies: 181.2%","Multiplier to Medium Enemies: 220.2%","Multiplier to Large Enemies: 259.2%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Drift","d":"Press to activate. Use a quick tail sweep attack in front, dealing Ice DMG. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["50.5%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Tail Swipe","d":"With enough energy, press to activate. Perform a forceful tail whip attack that deals massive Ice DMG. Gain 1 Flash Freeze Charge upon striking an enemy. After executing the move, you can immediately follow up with the 3rd hit of a Basic Attack. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["377.2%","Energy Cost: 40%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Sharknami","d":"After activating EX Special Attack: Tail Swipe, with enough Energy, press to activate: Perform a powerful series of slashes ahead that deal massive Ice DMG. Gain 1 Flash Freeze Charge upon striking an enemy. After executing the move, you can immediately follow up with the 3rd hit of a Basic Attack. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["553.3%","Energy Cost: 40%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Vortex","d":"Press to activate. A rapid dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. When Perfect Dodge is triggered, Ellen gains the Quick Charge effect, reducing the charge time of Dash Attack: Arctic Ambush, lasting up to 5 seconds or until it triggers.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash: Roaming Hunt","d":"Hold or double-tap to activate. Enter the Roaming state, allowing dashing movement. In the Roaming state, drag the stick/joystick to control Ellen\u0027s direction, and release to stop. Ellen is invulnerable for a brief time after activation.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Flash Freeze","d":"When Ellen has Flash Freeze Charges, the Flash Freeze effect is activated. Once Flash Freeze activates, Basic Attacks and Dash Attacks expend Flash Freeze Charges, dealing massive Ice DMG. Ellen can have up to a maximum of 6 Flash Freeze Charges.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Arctic Ambush","d":"While in the Roaming state, press to activate. Delivers a spinning slash to enemies before opening her scissors for a Swift Scissors strike, dealing Ice DMG. Gain 1 point of Flash Freeze Charge when the Swift Scissors strike hits. While in the Roaming state, hold to activate. Perform a spinning slash against the enemy, then pull apart the scissors to unleash a Charged Scissor strike, dealing massive Ice DMG. Gain 3 points of Flash Freeze Charge when the Charged Scissor strike hits. If the enemy is Frozen, it always triggers Shatter. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while charging the skill, and DMG taken is reduced by 40%. When taking DMG from enemies while the skill is charging, that instance of DMG is nullified, and charging instantly completes. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Spinning Slash: 62.3%","Swift Scissors: 127.6%","Charged Scissors: 158.2%","Swift Scissors Flash Freeze Charge Obtained: 1%","Charged Scissors Flash Freeze Charge Obtained: 3%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Monstrous Wave","d":"Press during a dodge to activate. Launches a dashing slash attack at enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["77%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Cold Snap","d":"While Flash Freeze is active, press during a dodge to activate: Launches a dashing slash attack at enemies in front, dealing Ice DMG. Consumes 1 Flash Freeze Charge.","m":["145.7%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Reef Rock","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Rapidly move through enemies with open scissors for a cutting strike, dealing Ice DMG. Character is invulnerable during the attack.","m":["152.6%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Avalanche","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, press the character icon to activate. Crash down from above and unleash an ice storm, dealing massive Ice DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["794.6%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Endless Winter","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate. Crash down from above and unleash an ice storm before a powerful scissor strike, dealing massive Ice DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1890.8%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Shark Sentinel","d":"When the character on the field is knocked back, press to activate. Speedily move through the enemy with open scissors for a cutting strike, dealing Ice DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. When the character on the field is launched, drag and press to activate. Enter the Roaming state, enabling dashing movement. While in the Roaming state, use the stick/joystick to change directions and release to stop. Character is invulnerable briefly when triggering the skill. Upon triggering a Quick Assist, Ellen gains the Quick Charge effect, shortening the charging time of Dash Attack: Arctic Ambush, lasting up to 5s or until it triggers once.","m":["121.1%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Wavefront Impact","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Shark Cruiser","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate. Charge and slash enemies in front, dealing Ice DMG. Press repeatedly or hold during the attack to extend the skill duration. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["437.9%"]}],"build":{"w":["Deep Sea Visitor","Myriad Eclipse","The Brimstone"],"a":["Woodpecker Electro, Puffer Electro","Puffer Electro, Branch \u0026 Blade Song","Puffer Electro, Hormone Punk","Woodpecker Electro, Polar Metal"],"core":6.99,"st":[["CRIT Rate",79],["CRIT DMG",145],["ATK",3205]]},"how":"Ellen gets a lot of value from on-fielding, being able to dish out good damage and being able to exploit Perfect Dodges to speed up her Flash Freeze Charge generation with the Quick Charge effect. Her low EX Special cost makes it possible to slot in an occasional cast for the B3 shortcut, and anytime Icy Blade is used it’s an opportunity to briefly swap out to other characters for buffs/debuffs/Daze. Even if Ellen does benefit from being the active character, it is far from the focus, and working so as to not under or overshoot Ice Anomaly build-up can help if bosses are Freezeable. As stun approaches, be more conservative with Energy spend, as being able to get a Tail Swipe into Sharknami string, then still be able to generate enough Energy mid-stun to do another Tail Swipe into B3 is ideal (Support Ultimates can help with this). Being at around 80 - 100 Energy depending on the team and available Ultimates is ideal. Which combo is used depends on the team. For example: Ellen | Dialyn | Nicole Dialyn Ultimate Conversion Ellen Ultimate Nicole Chain Attack Ellen Chain Attack EB1 Ellen Ultimate Swap to Nicole for her Ultimate Quick Assist to Ellen (Dash Cancel) EX Special: Tail Swipe EX Special: Sharknami Swap to Nicole for her EX Special Icy Blade Quick Assist to Ellen (Dash Cancel) EX Special: Tail Swipe EB3 Icy Blade Ellen | Lighter | Filler EX Special: Tail Swipe EX Special: Sharknami Swap to Lighter for a Chain trigger Icy Blade Ellen Chain Attack Cancel EB1 EB2 EB3 Icy Blade Swap to Lighter for Chain trigger Ellen Chain EX Special: Tail Swipe EB3 Icy Blade Ellen Ultimate Try to maintain any relevant W-Engine buffs where applicable (such as Deep Sea visitor, with Basics in combos to refresh stacks) and make use of Freeze to extend stun durations. From there, it’s back to building up resources again while doing as much damage as possible between stuns without sacrificing on set-ups and other Agents’ contribution to a fight.","pros":"High Ice damage output which is easy to access; Cohesive kit with high movement speed, self-buffs, invulnerability and parry mechanics. Easy to adapt to several kinds of enemies; Wide AoE capabilities, small enemy grouping capabilities and increased damage against larger targets — versatile to where she’s capable of handling all kinds of situations.","cons":"On-fielder playstyle with lots of different combos may make her harder to pilot than a lot of other DPS Agents; Notably lengthy Chain Attack, which may cause some issues with ensuring all of her key abilities fit during a single Stun window.","teams":[{"m":"Ellen + Dialyn + Astra Yao + Snap","c":"","r":"Rank 108"},{"m":"Ellen + Dialyn + Sunna + Sharkboo","c":"","r":"Rank 119"},{"m":"Ellen + Dialyn + Zhao + Sharkboo","c":"","r":"Rank 136"}]},"Velina":{"slug":"velina","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Dancing Fans","d":"Press to activate: Launches up to five attacks against enemies ahead, dealing Wind DMG. During the 5th attack, Velina\u0027s Anti-Interrupt Level increases, and DMG taken is reduced by 40%.","m":["1st-Hit: 51.7%","2nd-Hit: 48.9%","3rd-Hit: 169.1%","4th-Hit: 125.6%","5th-Hit: 229.6%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Windward Sweep","d":"Press to activate: A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Gale Step","d":"Press during a dodge to activate: Delivers a quick attack forward, dealing Wind DMG.","m":["99.7%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Cloudrend","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate: Launch a series of attacks on the target, dealing Wind DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["394.9%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Support: Emergency Protocol","d":"When the active character is launched, press to activate: Unleashes consecutive attacks against the target, dealing Wind DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["203.8%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Judicious Intervention","d":"When the on-field character is about to be attacked, press to activate: Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Negotiation Techniques","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate: Unleash a series of attacks, dealing Wind DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["532.7%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Wind Shear - Purging Surge","d":"Press to activate: Unleash a sweeping gust forward, dealing Wind DMG.","m":["58.6%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Wind Shear - Purifying Rise","d":"With enough Energy, press to activate: Dodges backward, then unleashes a massive wind blast to attack enemies, dealing Wind DMG. During the backward dodge, a dodge effect is active. Successfully dodging an enemy attack triggers Vital View. After using this skill, press to chain into the 5th hit of the Basic Attack. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["440.5%","Energy Cost: 45%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Wind Shear - Triple Deathblow","d":"With enough energy and after using EX Special Attack: Wind Shear - Purifying Rise, press or hold to activate: Continuously swing the fan, dealing Wind DMG. After using this skill, press to chain into the 5th hit of the Basic Attack. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["725.2%","Energy Cost: 45%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Wind Shear - Eye of the Storm","d":"With 90 or more , hold or to activate: Velina channels a whirlwind and summons a to continuously attack enemies and triggers the previous character\u0027s Quick Assist. Sweeping Cyclone lasts for 5s and deals Wind DMG to nearby enemies once every 0.5s.","m":["216.7%","Windbloom Cost: 90%","Sweeping Cyclone Wind Attribute Single-Hit: 39%","Sweeping Cyclone Attribute-Converted Single-Hit: 19.5%","Condensed Cyclone: 32.5%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Thousandfold Spiral","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Transforms into a hurricane to unleash multiple attacks against enemies, followed by a Finishing Move, dealing massive Wind DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["800.4%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Heed the Tempest","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate: Unleashes multiple attacks against enemies ahead, dealing massive Wind DMG. After using this skill, the previous character\u0027s Quick Assist is triggered. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["2188.3%"]}],"build":{"w":["Joyau Dore","Boisterous Echoes","Weeping Gemini","Flamemaker Shaker"],"a":["Wuthering Salon, Moonlight Lullaby","Wuthering Salon, Swing Jazz","Wuthering Salon, Phaethon\u0027s Melody","Wuthering Salon, Freedom Blues"],"core":6.99,"st":[["CRIT Rate",13],["CRIT DMG",65],["ATK",2596]]},"how":"Velina is an exceptionally simple character to play, with limited field-time being required to get the most out of her. As inflicting Windswept is required for Vortex, making use of a quick EX1 into her enhanced EX early on is often ideal, as there’s enough resources for it when coupled with the 45 Windbloom when entering the battlefield. This also gets a Sweeping Vortex out early, which can lower enemies’ Anomaly build-up RES and make it easier to push for both the first Windswept as well as maximising the build-up from other Agents’ skills. With that done, priority shifts to being on other Anomaly Agents and getting as many Vortexes as possible. This passively builds Windbite and leads to more Sweeping Cyclones being cast automatically. Given that Velina is built for high Energy Regen, she’ll accumulate resources for more EX casts quickly, which can then be spent on EX1s or EX1 + 2 casts to keep generating Windbloom so as to sustain more Sweeping Cyclones through enhanced EX uses. This then helps with building Daze and refreshing Windswept on enemies, all the while assisting with damage too owing to the Abloom triggers. That’s really the basics to Velina. Different Agents can then optimise by capitalising on their own mechanics, like making use of Aria’s Ultimate to get an immediate Vortex shortly after a Corruption is built, or using Burnice’s enhanced Basic Attack to get the most Anomaly build-up. Simply bring Velina in as needed to spend her resources.","pros":"The only way to reliably access Wind Anomaly as of her release, being a huge upscale to many older Anomaly Agents. Notably high Daze on her skills, allowing for much faster stuns and/or 3-stun routes previously not possible to double Anomaly teams. Anomaly Buildup RES reduction and her Signature W-Engine also allow her to work as a pseudo-Support. Rina is getting dangerously close to being “powercrept”.","cons":"Doesn’t offer much beyond being a Wind Anomaly applier, with only limited synergies via her Ablooms. Awkward gearing and team building priorities, as Vortex doesn’t scale with her stats, but Ablooms and Windswept DMG do. Locking out Disorders makes her very anti-synergistic with much of the Anomaly cast. Did you see what she did to Bruce?","teams":[{"m":"ukinami-yuzuha + aria","c":"","r":""},{"m":"ukinami-yuzuha + promeia","c":"","r":""},{"m":"ukinami-yuzuha + jane-doe","c":"","r":""}]},"Sigrid":{"slug":"sigrid","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Frost-Tipped Spear","d":"Press to activate: Launches up to four forward slashes, dealing Ice DMG. The 4th hit of Basic Attack: Frost-Tipped Spear is considered an Unbridled Spear attack.","m":["1st-Hit: 77%","2nd-Hit: 143.8%","3rd-Hit: 101.4%","4th-Hit: 221%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Converging Spear ","d":"While in the Aerial Patrol Spear state and Basic Attack: Converging Spear can be used, hold to activate: Launches the corresponding Basic Attack: Converging Spear based on the current stage, dealing Ice DMG. Basic Attack: Converging Spear has three stages. Each use advances it to the next stage. After performing the third stage of Basic Attack: Converging Spear, it resets to the first stage. If Sigrid is attacked while charging the 1st or 2nd stage of Basic Attack: Converging Spear, she blocks with her shield. On a successful block, the attack\u0027s DMG is negated, the next Basic Attack: Converging Spear deals 100% more Daze, the Aerial Patrol Spear state is refreshed, and she gains one use of Basic Attack: Converging Spear. Press after a successful block to perform the corresponding stage of Basic Attack: Converging Spear. Basic Attack: Converging Spear performed after Basic Attack: Frost-Tipped Spear retains the current stage of Basic Attack: Frost-Tipped Spear. DMG taken is reduced by 60% during this skill. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill. Character is invulnerable during the third stage of Basic Attack: Converging Spear.","m":["Basic Attack: Converging Spear 1st Stage: 358.3%","Basic Attack: Converging Spear 2nd Stage: 609.1%","Basic Attack: Converging Spear 3rd Stage: 814.6%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Cloudstep","d":"Press to activate: A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Windchase ","d":"Press during a dodge to activate: Performs a forward cleaving slash, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["119%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Counterthrust","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate: Condenses frost around the spearhead before unleashing a powerful counterattack, dealing Ice DMG. When performed after Basic Attack: Frost-Tipped Spear, Dodge Counter: Counterthrust retains the current stage of Basic Attack: Frost-Tipped Spear. This skill is considered an Unbridled Spear attack. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["243.1%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Iron Sentinel ","d":"When the active character is launched, press to activate: Condenses ice before lunging forward, dealing Ice DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["39.7%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Dauntless Cold","d":"When the on-field character is about to be attacked, press to activate: Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Devouring Frost ","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate: Swings the spear upward before following with a powerful downward attack, dealing massive Ice DMG. This skill is considered an Unbridled Spear attack. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["514.9%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Frostflower ","d":"Press to activate: Performs three forward thrusts, dealing Ice DMG. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["53.7%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Scattered Jade","d":"With enough Energy and while not in the Aerial Patrol Spear state, press to activate: Performs a series of powerful stabs ahead, dealing massive Ice DMG. This skill is considered an Unbridled Spear attack. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["438.8%","Energy Cost: 60%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Shattered Jade ","d":"With enough Energy and while in the Aerial Patrol Spear state, press to activate: Performs a series of powerful lunging stabs ahead, dealing massive Ice DMG. This skill is considered an Unbridled Spear attack. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1047.8%","Energy Cost: 50%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Encroaching Ice ","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Performs a powerful piercing attack against enemies ahead, dealing massive Ice DMG. Upon activating this skill, gains the Tempered effect, increasing the DMG dealt by subsequent Basic Attack: Converging Spear attacks by 20% for 50s. When the current skill hits a Stunned elite or boss enemy for the first time, the current stage of Basic Attack: Converging Spear is recorded and then reset before entering the Formation Breaker state. While in Formation Breaker, Aerial Patrol Spear\u0027s duration will not be reduced. Hold Icon_Normal to continuously activate the 1st through 3rd stage of Basic Attack: Converging Spear. After activating the 3rd stage of Basic Attack: Converging Spear, Formation Breaker ends and Basic Attack: Converging Spear\u0027s stage is restored to the recorded stage. Formation Breaker can trigger at most once against the same target before the target recovers from Stun. This skill is considered an Unbridled Spear attack. While in the Formation Breaker state, Basic Attack: Converging Spear does not trigger the Chain Attack window when hitting Stunned enemies. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["943.7%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Frozen Heavens","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate: Gathers the power of extreme cold before unleashing a devastating series of lunging attacks, dealing massive Ice DMG. This skill is considered an Unbridled Spear attack. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["2189.8%"]}],"build":{"w":["Knight\u0027s Extolment","The Brimstone","Severed Innocence","Riot Suppressor Mark VI"],"a":["Dawn\u0027s Bloom, Puffer Electro","Dawn\u0027s Bloom, Branch \u0026 Blade Song","Dawn\u0027s Bloom, Astral Voice","Hormone Punk, Puffer Electro"],"core":7,"st":[["CRIT Rate",36],["CRIT DMG",201],["ATK",3196]]},"how":"Although every team and encounter will need to be tailored, the principle behind Sigrid’s game plan is very simple: cycle through as many enhanced Basics as possible. There is a degree of resource management needed. Trying open stun with an enhanced Basic 3 can help squeeze in a bit more damage, so timing attacks or swapping out of Sigrid to maintain the short 6-second duration of the Aerial Patrol Spear so that it’s up for the start of stun is a form of skill expression on her. With Formation Breaker storing the string, though, it can also be left to mid-stun, even if it’d demand an Unbridled Spear attack to build up to. With how strong her EX is, saving it to stun combos as a means to progress her enhanced Basic and deal its own damage is helpful too. That’s about it for the fundamentals though; Sigrid is quite simple in her gameplan. The difficulty is in the execution, so as to maximise the number of enhanced Basics in a fight and optimise around getting the highest value skills during burst windows. A sample combo for Sigrid with Norma would be: Enhanced Basic 3 Sigrid Chain Attack Enhanced Basic 1 Enhanced Basic 2 Enhanced Basic 3 Sigrid Chain Attack Enhanced Basic 1 Enhanced EX Enhanced Basic 2 Norma Chain Attack conversion to Sigrid Enhanced Basic 3 Ultimate Norma’s Chain Attack conversion is best used between enhanced Basics so as to trigger while Sigrid is in animation to speed things up. Keep in mind that this is only a template, as it’ll change depending on enemy stun durations, freezeable state and the team. Try to get as many enhanced Basics in stun between EXs, Chain Attacks and Ultimates for the most damage.","pros":"Incredibly high damage output, being a step above most CRIT DPS Agents that came before her. Diverse team options, being able to get great results with a variety of Stunners and Supports, be they limited or standard. Flexible builds, with multiple usable Drive Disc sets and having competitive W-Engine alternatives to her Signature. A in Track, an S in Distance, and an S in Style.","cons":"Managing resources can be tricky, as aligning her enhanced Basics and Decibels for combos can demand specific routing. Misses out on her full Additional Ability’s value without Wind, and can be too saturated in certain multipliers, which lessen some teammates’ value. Frustrating to roll substats for, as she can easily overcap on CRIT Rate. 1-star Guts Spark.","teams":[{"m":"norma, dialyn + rina, sunna","c":"","r":""},{"m":"lycaon + rina","c":"","r":""},{"m":"nangong-yu + sunna","c":"","r":""}]},"Cissia":{"slug":"cissia","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Tongue Flick","d":"Press to activate: Launch up to four attacks forward, dealing Electric DMG. When the 4th hit lands, gain 2 points of Venom. Hitting a Stunned enemy grants an additional 1 point of Venom.","m":["1st-Hit: 77.7%","2nd-Hit: 138.7%","3rd-Hit: 135.1%","4th-Hit: 250.2%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Serpent\u0027s Kiss","d":"With Serpentine Shadow, hold to launch: Cissia leaps into the air and locks onto a target, then slams down, dealing Electric DMG to enemies in the area. While locking on, continue to hold and drag the / to extend the lock-on duration and freely control the landing position. For every 6 points of Venom gained, gain 1 stack of Serpentine Shadow, stacking up to 3 times. Upon entering the battlefield, gain 1 stack of Serpentine Shadow. Using this skill consumes 1 stack of Serpentine Shadow. Upon hitting an enemy, all Venom is consumed to trigger Corrode Bone. Upon activating this skill, a Quick Assist is triggered. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["504.2%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Corrode Bone","d":"Deal Electric DMG to nearby enemies. Each trigger increases CRIT Rate by 6% for 15s, stacking up to 3 times. Repeated triggers refresh the duration.","m":["126.8%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Bared Fangs","d":"Press to activate. Launches a long-range snake bite forward, dealing Electric DMG. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["52%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Venomous Bite","d":"With enough Energy, press to activate. Unleash multiple long-range snake bites forward, dealing Electric DMG. Grants 5 Energy when the move is used. When activating by holding, consumes additional Energy. For every 20 additional Energy consumed, unleash 1 extra strike that deals Electric DMG, up to a maximum of 60 additional Energy. After activation, gain 3 Venom. For every additional 20 Energy consumed while holding, gain 1 more Venom. After using this skill, it can be immediately followed up with the 4th hit of Basic Attack: Tongue Flick. A Quick Assist is triggered when this skill hits an enemy. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["668%","Additional Strike: 200.4%","Energy Cost: 65%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Slither","d":"Press to activate. A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Bite Mark","d":"Press during a dodge to activate: Dash forward with a swift slash, dealing Electric DMG.","m":["147.3%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Bite Back","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Leap forward and perform a sweeping attack upon landing, dealing Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["324.5%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Gang Operation","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Launch multiple attacks ahead, dealing massive Electric DMG. After using this skill, gain 3 Venom. A Quick Assist is triggered when this skill hits an enemy. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["737.8%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Ophidiophobia","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate: Deliver a thunderbolt attack in front, dealing massive Electric DMG.After using this skill, obtain 3 Venom. After using this skill, activate Ether Veil: Cold-Blooded, lasting 30s. All squad members\u0027 CRIT DMG increases by 5% for the duration. Re-activating Ether Veil: Cold-Blooded a second time will first deactivate the active Ether Veil: Cold-Blooded. A Quick Assist is triggered when this skill hits an enemy. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1811%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Alarm System","d":"When the active character is launched, press to activate. Leaps forward and performs a sweeping attack upon landing, dealing Electric DMG. During this skill, you can quickly chain into Special Attack: Bared Fangs, EX Special Attack: Venomous Bite, and Basic Attack: Serpent\u0027s Kiss. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["74.8%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Extra Prison Rations","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Partners in Crime","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate: Unleash a series of attacks, dealing Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["520.6%"]}],"build":{"w":["Serpentine Seeker","Drill Rig - Red Axis","Cordis Germina","Bellicose Blaze"],"a":["Dawn\u0027s Bloom, Moonlight Lullaby","Astral Voice, Moonlight Lullaby","Dawn\u0027s Bloom, Swing Jazz","Astral Voice, Swing Jazz"],"core":7,"st":[["CRIT Rate",53],["CRIT DMG",122],["ATK",2640]]},"how":"Cissia’s primary playstyle is one that takes the role of a sub-DPS. Since she can provide a decent amount of Daze, it makes it easier for double Attacker teams to run a Support while still managing enough stuns in a fight. Owing to Cissia’s high Energy Regen, it’s good to use her EX Special frequently to build Venom, both with its own cast and the shortcut to Basic 4. As Serpentine Shadow stacks build, spend it on her enhanced Basic Attack dive for Corrode Bone to quickly build Daze and deal damage. It’s better to make use of multiple EX Specials rather than extending it when out of stun, as this gives more opportunities to shortcut to Basic 4 and is slightly more damage and Daze. Try to have enough Energy for an EX Special (perhaps even an extended one) when Stun arrives. Use it, her Ultimate and Chain Attack to build Venom quickly, as overcapping stacks all lead to Corrode Bone triggers, then spend it all with her enhanced Basic Attack dive. As her burst is decently fast and has multiple swap points - like from an early Quick Assist off her EX or while she does her dive - balancing her burst with that of a main-DPS’ combo is ideal. She can be played as a main-DPS, but not much changes. It’s easier to manage as there is no longer a need to swap in and out of Cissia to spend her Energy, and the fundamental goal of building and spending Venom stacks is the same. Here’s a sample combo with Seed/Sunna/Cissia Seed Enhanced Basic Attack Swap to Cissia EX Special: Venomous Bite Cissia Ultimate Cancel Chain Enhanced Basic Attack: Serpent’s Kiss Quick Assist to Seed Seed Ultimate Cissia Chain Attack Seed Chain Attack Seed Enhanced Basic Attack Swap to Cissia EX Special: Venomous Bite Enhanced Basic Attack: Serpent’s Kiss","pros":"Strong numbers given her limited field time, being a “sub-DPS” that can almost match the damage of a main carry. Very well rounded character, able to deal damage, build decibels and has Daze build that’s competitive with many Stunners. Flexible build options in both Drive Discs and W-Engines, making her relatively inexpensive to work with. girl","cons":"Sub-DPS character who will perform worse in a main-DPS position than alternatives without vertical investment. Very limited comp choice, being a BiS pick for Seed alone and strictly limited to Electric Attacker teams. Difficult to balance Energy Regen and Crit Rate without her Signature, which can severely limit her personal damage. failure","teams":[{"m":"seed + sunna","c":"","r":""},{"m":"seed + astra-yao, nicole-demara","c":"","r":""},{"m":"seed + dialyn, trigger, qingyi, ju-fufu","c":"","r":""}]},"Seth":{"slug":"seth","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Lightning Strike","d":"Press to activate: Unleashes up to 4 attacks in front, dealing Physical DMG and Electric DMG.","m":["1st-Hit: 36.2%","2nd-Hit: 56.5%","3rd-Hit: 193.3%","4th-Hit: 97.4%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Lightning Strike - Electrified","d":"When Resolve is above 75%, hold to activate: Consume 75% Resolve to launch continuous attacks in front, followed by a finishing strike that deals Electric DMG. When the finishing strike hits an enemy, it triggers the Quick Assist of the squad member positioned before Seth. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["Combo: 382.8%","Finishing Strike: 424.2%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Thunder Shield Rush","d":"Hold to activate. Launch two shield strikes forward, dealing Electric DMG. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["69.2%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Thunder Shield Rush - High Voltage","d":"When Seth has enough energy, press to activate: Unleash a series of slashes in front, dealing massive Electric DMG. Hold to charge the move, and Seth will dash forward, unleashing a series of powerful slashes, dealing massive Electric DMG. Activating the move accumulates 75% Resolve. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while charging this skill, and damage taken is reduced by 40%. Seth is invulnerable during the continuous slashes.","m":["646%","Charged: 999.8%","Energy Cost per second: 80%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Evasion Maneuver","d":"Press to activate. A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Thunder Assault","d":"Press during a dodge to activate. Charge forward with a shield attack, dealing Physical DMG. Damage received during the move is decreased by 40%.","m":["110%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Retreat to Advance","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Unleash a quick downward strike on enemies in front, dealing Electric DMG. After the move, hold to chain into EX Special Attack: Thunder Shield Rush - High Voltage, enabling faster charging. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["230%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Final Judgement","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select Seth to activate: Launch a series of slashes in front, dealing massive Electric DMG. Activating the move accumulates 75% Resolve. After the move, hold to chain into EX Special Attack: Thunder Shield Rush - High Voltage, enabling faster charging. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["704.1%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Justice Prevails","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate. Launch a series of upward slashes in front, followed by a finishing strike, dealing massive Electric DMG. Activating the move accumulates 75% Resolve, and grants 3 additional Assist Points. After the move, hold to chain into EX Special Attack: Thunder Shield Rush - High Voltage, enabling faster charging. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["2024.3%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Armed Support","d":"When the on-field character is launched, press to activate. Unleash a quick downward strike on enemies in front, dealing Electric DMG. After the move, hold to chain into EX Special Attack: Thunder Shield Rush - High Voltage, enabling faster charging. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["100%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Thundershield","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, inflicting massive Daze. Seth gains 25% Resolve upon activating the skill. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Public Security Ruling","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate. Launch a forward thrust attack, followed by two horizontal slashes, dealing Electric DMG. When the finishing strike hits an enemy, it triggers the Quick Assist of the squad member positioned before Seth. After the move, hold to chain into EX Special Attack: Thunder Shield Rush - High Voltage, enabling faster charging. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["428.5%"]}],"build":{"w":["Spring Embrace"],"a":["Astral Voice, Swing Jazz"],"core":7,"st":[["CRIT Rate",15],["CRIT DMG",74],["ATK",3831]]},"how":"$undefined","pros":"High duration buff/debuff uptime and they are also easy to apply, which makes keeping them all active easy. Takes up minimal field time. Offers decent Defensive shields. Grants a big Anomaly efficiency bonus to himself and an ally of your choosing. Debuffs enemies causing them to lose 20% Anomaly Buildup Resistance of all element types.","cons":"Can only consistently buff himself and 1 other teammate with his shield and Anomaly Efficiency. Attack animations on most important attacks his EX Special and Charged Held Basic are on the slower side.","teams":[{"m":"Remielle + Jane Doe + Seth + Officer Cui","c":"","r":"Rank 388"},{"m":"Cissia + Astra Yao + Seth + Plugboo","c":"","r":"Rank 388"},{"m":"Jane Doe + Lucy + Seth + Agent Gulliver","c":"","r":"Rank 388"}]},"Anton":{"slug":"anton","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Enthusiastic Drills","d":"Press to activate. Unleashes up to 4 mixed attacks in front, dealing Physical DMG. The 4th-hit is a Piledriver Attack.","m":["1st-Hit: 67.8%","2nd-Hit: 92.3%","3rd-Hit: 109.3%","4th-Hit: 229.1%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Enthusiastic Drills (Burst Mode)","d":"Press while Anton is in Burst Mode to activate: Unleashes up to 3 mixed attacks in front, dealing massive Electric DMG. During the 2nd Drill Attack and 3rd Pile Driver Attack, press repeatedly or hold to extend the skill duration.","m":["1st-Hit: 240.9%","2nd-Hit: 469.2%","3rd-Hit: 456.9%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Spin, Bro!","d":"Press to activate. Unleashes a Pile Driver Attack against enemies in a line in front, dealing Electric DMG. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["44.2%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Smash the Horizon, Bro!","d":"With enough energy, press to activate: Launches several Pile Driver Attacks at enemies in a line in front of him, dealing massive Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. Anton enters Burst Mode after using this skill. When in Burst Mode, Anton\u0027s attacks become more powerful, dealing massive Electric DMG while continually consuming Energy upon hitting an enemy. Burst Mode remains active until his Energy is depleted.","m":["195.1%","Energy Cost: 40%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Explosive Drill (Burst Mode)","d":"Press while in Burst Mode to activate. Launches a Pile Driver Attack at enemies in front, dealing Electric DMG. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["231.4%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Let\u0027s Move","d":"Press to dodge. A rapid dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Fire With Fire","d":"Press during a Dodge to activate: Rams into enemies in front of him, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["68.4%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Retaliation","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Continuously strikes enemies in front with heavy punches, dealing Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable during the attack.","m":["271.2%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Overload Drill (Burst Mode)","d":"While in Burst Mode, press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Launch a Drill Attack at enemies in front of him, dealing massive Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable during the attack.","m":["465.4%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Go Go Go!","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Unleashes a Pile Driver Attack onto the ground in front of him over a large area, dealing massive Electric DMG to enemies within range. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["640.7%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Go Go Go Go Go!","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate. Unleashes a Pile Driver Attack onto the ground in front of him over a large area, dealing massive Electric DMG to enemies within range. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1816.4%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Shoulder-To-Shoulder","d":"When the character in combat is launched, press to activate. Continuously strikes enemies in front of him with heavy punches, dealing Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable during the attack.","m":["263.4%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Protective Drill (Burst Mode)","d":"When the on-field character is launched, press to activate. Attacks enemies in front with a Drill Attack, dealing massive Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable during the attack.","m":["365.4%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Iron Wrist","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. This skill excels at parrying enemy attacks and reduces the consumption of Assist Points when the character is under intense attacks. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Limit Burst","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate. Launches a Drill Attack that ends in a Pile Driver Attack, dealing Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["325.8%"]}],"build":{"w":["Cordis Germina","Severed Innocence","The Brimstone"],"a":["Astral Voice, Woodpecker Electro","Thunder Metal, Branch \u0026 Blade Song","Puffer Electro, Thunder Metal","Woodpecker Electro, Branch \u0026 Blade Song"],"core":7,"st":[["CRIT Rate",72],["CRIT DMG",163],["ATK",2923]]},"how":"$undefined","pros":"Has the unique mechanic to retrigger Shocks every 0.5 seconds after dealing 4 Critical Hits while in Burst mode giving him one of the highest potential kits for an A-rank unit. Has great Mindscapes, giving him good scaling potential as you develop your account. His M1 prolongs his Burst Mode duration by a good amount, and his M4 gives the whole team a Crit Rate buff after he uses a Chain or Ultimate attack for 12 seconds. Is a Bro.","cons":"Has a large amount of his potential damage within his kit tied to his ability to trigger additional damage against Shocked enemies, making him reliant on ensuring enemies remain Shocked as much as possible and for as large amount of damage as possible. Has limited options outside of S-rank’s when it comes to team building. Relies heavily on being in Burst Mode to deal the majority of his damage and feels lackluster outside of it, making Anton one of the most energy-reliant characters in the game.","teams":[{"m":"Anton + Dialyn + Astra Yao + Plugboo","c":"","r":"Rank 388"},{"m":"Anton + Dialyn + Astra Yao + Plugboo","c":"","r":"Rank 365"},{"m":"Anton + Cissia + Astra Yao + Snap","c":"","r":"Rank 365"}]},"Corin":{"slug":"corin","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Wipeout","d":"Press to activate: Unleashes up to 5 slashes, dealing Physical DMG. Repeatedly press or hold the button during the 3rd and 5th hits to extend the chainsaw slash attack.","m":["1st-Hit: 82%","2nd-Hit: 76.6%","3rd-Hit: 179.2%","4th-Hit: 233.4%","5th-Hit: 421.2%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Clean Sweep","d":"Press to activate: Unleashes a series of slashes upon enemies in front, before detonating the chainsaw, dealing Physical DMG. Repeatedly press or hold the button to extend the duration of the chainsaw slash attack. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill, and DMG taken is reduced by 40%.","m":["Spinning Slash: 66.7%","Extended Slash Maximum: 37.5%","Explosion: 25%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Beware the Skirt","d":"With enough energy, press to activate: Unleashes a series of powerful slashes upon enemies in front, before detonating the chainsaw, dealing massive Physical DMG. Repeatedly press or hold the button to extend the duration of the chainsaw slash attack at the cost of Energy if the attack connects. Character is invulnerable during the spinning Slash. Anti-Interrupt level is increased during the extended slash, and DMG taken is reduced by 40%.","m":["Spinning Slash: 345.1%","Extended Slash Maximum: 1035.1%","Explosion: 345.1%","Spinning Slash Energy Cost: 20%","Extended Slash Maximum Energy Cost: 40%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Shoo!","d":"Press to dodge. A rapid dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Oopsy-Daisy!","d":"Press during a dodge to activate. Slashes enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG. Repeatedly press or hold the button to extend the chainsaw attack\u0027s duration.","m":["96.7%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Nope!","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate: Slashes enemies in front before detonating her chainsaw, dealing Physical DMG. Repeatedly press or hold the button to extend the chainsaw slash attack. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["271.2%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Sorry...","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Unleashes a powerful slash at enemies in a small area, dealing massive Physical DMG. Repeatedly press or hold the button to extend the chainsaw slash attack. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["687.3%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Very, Very Sorry!","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate: Unleashes a powerful slash at enemies in a small area, dealing massive Physical DMG. Repeatedly press or hold the button to extend the chainsaw slash attack. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["2028.8%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Emergency Measures","d":"When the on-field character is launched, press to activate. Slashes enemies in front before detonating her chainsaw, dealing Physical DMG. Repeatedly press or hold the button to extend the chainsaw slash attack. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["215%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: P—Please allow me!","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. This skill excels at parrying enemy attacks and reduces the consumption of Assist Points when the character is under intense attacks. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Quick Sweep","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate: Unleash a series of slashes against enemies in front followed by an explosive chainsaw, dealing Physical DMG. Repeatedly press or hold to extend the chainsaw slash attack. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["547.5%"]}],"build":{"w":["Steel Cushion","Heartstring Nocturne","Cordis Germina"],"a":["Puffer Electro, Woodpecker Electro","Puffer Electro, Branch \u0026 Blade Song","Hormone Punk, Woodpecker Electro","Puffer Electro, Hormone Punk"],"core":7,"st":[["CRIT Rate",85],["CRIT DMG",161],["ATK",2820]]},"how":"$undefined","pros":"Surprisingly high damage potential with a high skill ceiling. Can give surprisingly good results under the right conditions; Extremely accessible W-Engines, ready to go with permanent banner options; Is free!","cons":"Particularly reliant on player skill and the right teammates to perform. Wants proper management of Decibels and Assist Follow-Ups to access Ultimate every Stun which is complex in her best teams, also wants proper combos that are swap-intensive; Has a huge gap in performance going from her best teammates to more accessible, or even second-best options; Performance will also vastly vary depending on match-up. Particularly good against Physical-weak enemies and enemies with lots of Perfect Assist opportunities, will face severe drops in performance against other kinds of enemies.","teams":[{"m":"Corin + Roxy + Sunna + Luckyboo","c":"","r":"Rank 280"},{"m":"Corin + Dialyn + Astra Yao + Birkblick","c":"","r":"Rank 280"},{"m":"Corin + Norma + Sunna + Bangvolver","c":"","r":"Rank 388"}]},"Roxy":{"slug":"roxy","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Do Stay a While","d":"Press to activate: Performs up to four strikes forward, dealing Wind DMG.","m":["1st-Hit: 52.4%","2nd-Hit: 107.9%","3rd-Hit: 172.4%","4th-Hit: 192.5%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Excuse Me","d":"Press to activate: Perform a quick dodge to the side.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Forgive My Rudeness","d":"Press during a dodge to activate: Strike forward, dealing Wind DMG.","m":["35.6%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Returned Courtesy","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate: Strike enemies in front, dealing Wind DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["392%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist: More Overtime?","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate: Roxy stays on field and Strikes enemies in front, dealing Wind DMG. Upon activating this skill, it is considered a Basic Attack. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["39%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: At Your Service","d":"When the on-field character is launched, press to activate: Strikes enemies in front, dealing Wind DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["100.8%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Allow Me to Assist","d":"When the on-field character is about to be attacked, press to activate: Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. This skill excels at parrying enemy attacks and reduces the consumption of [Assist Points] when the character is under intense attacks. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Midnight Code","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate: Perform a forward strike, dealing Wind DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Hit: 611.6%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Much Obliged","d":"Press to activate: Perform a forward strike, dealing Wind DMG.","m":["50.9%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Forgive Me for Not Seeing You Off","d":"After activating EX Special Attack: Kindly Rest in Peace, this attack is automatically activated when the total number of Storm\u0027s Eye Eyes of the Storm on the field and Roxy\u0027s Wind Energy reaches at least 3: Throws her hammer at enemies on the field, dealing Wind DMG. Eyes of the Storm hit by this attack are detonated, up to 3 Eyes of the Storm at a time. Based on the number detonated, a corresponding number of Miniature Windstorms are generated, dealing Wind DMG. If 3 Eyes of the Storm are detonated at once, a Giant Windstorm is generated instead, dealing Wind DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["250%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Don\u0027t Catch a Chill","d":"With enough energy, press or hold to activate: Slide forward, dealing Wind DMG. While sliding, press and hold to have Roxy enter the Whirlwind state: While in the Whirlwind state, Roxy transforms into a tornado. Drag the joystick to control its direction. During this, Energy is continuously consumed, dealing Wind DMG to enemies along its path. When Energy is depleted, or when is released while the joystick is not being moved, Roxy exits the Whirlwind state. When the slide ends or when exiting the Whirlwind state, automatically follow up with EX Special Attack: Kindly Rest in Peace. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["13.7%","Energy Cost to Use: 25%","Energy Cost: 10%","Whirlwind Per Second: 1304%","Energy Cost Per Second: 30%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Kindly Rest in Peace","d":"Automatically activates after EX Special Attack: Don\u0027t Catch a Chill ends: Consume all Wind Energy to fire a wind cannon forward, dealing Wind DMG. After the attack, for each point of Wind Energy consumed, deals an additional instance of Wind DMG and generates 1 Storm\u0027s Eye at the current position.","m":["31.9%","Additional Explosion: 26.1%"]},{"t":"","n":"Storm\u0027s Eye","d":"Generated after [EX Special Attack: Kindly Rest in Peace] consumes Wind Energy, lasting 30s before automatically detonating; Up to 9 Storm\u0027s Eye can exist at the same time. If this limit is exceeded, the earliest generated [Storm\u0027s Eye] will automatically detonate; Detonates when hit by [Special Attack: Forgive Me for Not Seeing You Off]. If fewer than 3 are hit at the same time, 1 Miniature Windstorm is generated at the location of each [Storm\u0027s Eye], tracking enemies and dealing Wind DMG for 1s; If 3 are hit at the same time, 1 Giant Windstorm is generated instead, dealing Wind DMG for 1s. When detonated by any means, a [Storm\u0027s Eye] releases a blast, dealing 1 instance of Wind DMG to nearby enemies.","m":["Detonation: 52.1%","Miniature Windstorm per Second: 52.1%","Giant Windstorm per Second: 208.4%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Gale-Burial Great Hammer","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Unleashes a powerful strike at enemies in front, dealing massive Wind DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["902.2%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Requiem for the Night-Burial","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate: Unleashes a powerful strike at enemies in front in a large area, dealing massive Wind DMG; After using this skill, gain 1 Wind Energy; Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["2131.5%"]}],"build":{"w":["Crimson Moon Casket","Steam Oven","Hellfire Gears","The Restrained"],"a":["King of the Summit, Swing Jazz","King of the Summit, Moonlight Lullaby","Astral Voice, Moonlight Lullaby","Astral Voice, Swing Jazz"],"core":6.97,"st":[["CRIT Rate",73],["CRIT DMG",95],["ATK",2243]]},"how":"Roxy’s kit isn’t all that complicated, and it mostly amounts to holding down EX and channelling it for as long as possible when high in Energy, then occasionally swapping to her for Assists and Ultimates to build extra Daze. In actual fights, though, there are some key points to keep in mind when playing her: After a Windswept or Cleanse, make sure to attack with the main DPS (or another Agent with a matching attribute) to have them apply Contamination. Keep a close eye on the Anomaly Buildup of other Agents in the team, as Vortex will change the Contamination element, so be sure to have a Cleanse (or Windswept) ready to flip it back to the main DPS. Since Contamination’s Direct DMG Bonus is what makes Roxy competitive with other Stunners, always have it up for stuns! If using King of the Summit, make use of Roxy’s low EX initial Energy cost to refresh the buff mid-Stun. If using Astral Voice, it may be better to actively get hit to get Quick Assist triggers to build stacks, and look to manage Support EXs and Ultimates to maintain it on the DPS. The real difficulty with Roxy comes with making sure that she has the time and resources to build the Daze needed to get enough stuns, or a fast enough stun, to sustain a high score. How this is done will depend a lot on her team and the fight she runs in, so being more mindful of teammate resource needs and enemy attack patterns, as well as taking the time to plan out routes, will make a big difference to her performance.","pros":"Very high personal damage, and does so in a wide area with a vacuum effect, making her ideal for grouping and clearing out weak enemies. One of the few Stunners that isn’t reliant on her Signature W-Engine or absurd substat distribution for Daze, having similar routing even with F2P options. Gives CRIT DPS teams access to Direct DMG (and does so for extended periods), being an incredibly strong unique multiplier. Looks like she belongs in Guilty Gear.","cons":"Lacklustre Daze, and what she does get needs her to be active, taking time away from other team members. Frustrating to build, needing Energy Regen, CRIT RATE, good damage substats and lacks a good 4-piece Drive Disc set that lets her max out her passives. Too much of her value is in Contamination, meaning future dual-damage teams with mixed elements or Wind Supports may struggle to use her effectively. For all the Claret x Roxy fanservice, she isn’t even a best-in-slot for her…","teams":[{"m":"claret + rina","c":"","r":""},{"m":"sigrid, pyrois + sunna, rina","c":"","r":""},{"m":"yidhari, banyue + lucia","c":"","r":""}]},"Pulchra":{"slug":"pulchra","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Swift Strike","d":"Press to activate: Unleashes up to 3 attacks forward, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["1st-Hit: 35.7%","2nd-Hit: 94.1%","3rd-Hit: 167.6%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Leaping Strike","d":"Hold to activate: Leap forward and unleash a series of slashes, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["135%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Rending Claw","d":"Press to activate. Perform a rapid back-and-forth piercing attack, dealing Physical DMG. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["25.1%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Rending Claw - Nightmare Shadow","d":"While Pulchra is in the Hunter\u0027s Gait state, and when another active character in the squad hits an enemy with a heavy attack from a Special Attack or EX Special Attack: Dash back-and-forth piercing enemies surrounding the target, dealing Physical DMG. After using this skill, if another active character in the squad hits an enemy, Pulchra will repeat the attack up to 5 additional times, with the final attack being a more powerful Finishing Move. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. Special Attack: Rending Claw - Nightmare Shadow is an Aftershock attack.","m":["46.3%","Finishing Move: 53.5%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Rending Claw - Flashstep","d":"With enough Energy, press to activate. Pierce back and forth times, dealing massive Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["347.7%","Energy Cost: 60%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Reversal Shot","d":"Press to activate. A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: First Strike Advantage","d":"Press during a dodge to activate: Dash forward and slash, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["48.3%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Relentless Retribution","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Thrust at enemies in front, then follow up with a swift slash, dealing Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["201.8%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Hey, Didn\u0027t Expect That, Right?","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Unleashes a charged shot forward, dealing massive Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["534.1%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Oh, Time to Play?","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate. Unleash a powerful shot at enemies in a large area ahead, dealing massive Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1393.8%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Contract - Bodyguard","d":"When the on-field character is launched, press to activate. Thrust at enemies in front, followed by rapid slashes, dealing Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["78.3%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Evasive Assist: Contract - Outsourced Combat","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Dodges the enemy\u0027s attack and activates Vital View. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Independent Pricing","d":"Press after an Evasive Assist to activate: Leap forward into the air and fire, dealing Physical DMG. Upon activating this skill, consume 1 Assist Point to enter the Hunter\u0027s Gait state. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["307.1%"]}],"build":{"w":["Box Cutter","Hellfire Gears","Steam Oven","Precious Fossilized Core"],"a":["King of the Summit, Shockstar Disco","Shadow Harmony, Shockstar Disco","King of the Summit, Shadow Harmony","King of the Summit, Swing Jazz"],"core":6.93,"st":[["CRIT Rate",52],["CRIT DMG",108],["ATK",2209]]},"how":"$undefined","pros":"Completely free unit everyone will get on their account, Offers a team-wide buff for Aftershock Agents (All Agents at M6) while dealing solid Daze, Uses incredibly minimal field to implement her entire kit.","cons":"Has limited options to support with only 1 other Aftershock character in the game, Requires M6 to unlock her more generic supportive capabilities.","teams":[{"m":"Yixuan + Pulchra + Lucia + Belion","c":"","r":"Rank 280"},{"m":"Burnice + Pulchra + Yuzuha + Butler","c":"","r":"Rank 388"},{"m":"Nekomata + Pulchra + Sunna + Bild N. Boolok","c":"","r":"Rank 388"}]},"Grace":{"slug":"grace-howard","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: High-Pressure Spike","d":"Press to activate. Unleashes up to 4 attacks, dealing Physical DMG and Electric DMG. While launching Basic Attacks, drag the stick/joystick to move while attacking. This allows Grace to reposition herself and deal Physical DMG. If used after the 1st or 2nd hit of a Basic Attack, pressing again resumes the combo from the 3rd or 4th hit of the Basic Attack. While Grace is launching Basic Attacks, her Basic Attack combo will not be interrupted by her Special Attacks, EX Special Attacks, Dodge, Dash Attacks, or Dodge Counter.","m":["1st-Hit: 55.1%","2nd-Hit: 59.7%","3rd-Hit: 124.8%","4th-Hit: 186.3%","Moving Shot: 40.3%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Obstruction Removal","d":"Press to activate. Throws a grenade to the front, dealing Electric DMG. During the skill, drag the stick/joystick to reposition in that direction. When activated via consuming Zap, dodge incoming enemy attacks. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["42.1%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Supercharged Obstruction Removal","d":"With enough Energy, press to activate: Leaps into the air and throws two grenades forward, dealing massive Electric DMG. During the skill, drag the stick/joystick to change directions. If Zap reaches max stacks, throws an additional Vortex Cluster Grenade, generating an electromagnetic field at the point of detonation that pulls in enemies and deals Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["166.9%","Energy Cost: 40%","Vortex Cluster Grenade Base: 87.5%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Pulse","d":"Activating an Ultimate grants 25 stacks of Pulse (max 25 stacks). When gaining Zap, consumes 1 stack of Pulse. After consuming Pulse to obtain 8 stacks of Zap, the next grenade throw includes an additional Pulse Grenade. If it hits an enemy suffering Ether, Electric, Fire, Physical, Ice, or Wind Anomaly, it triggers Abloom: deals an additional instance of DMG equal to 560%/280%/700%/50%/70%/28 of the original Anomaly\u0027s DMG. While in the Pulse state, Special Attack: Obstruction Removal - Cycle is unlocked.","m":["42%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Obstruction Removal - Cycle","d":"While in the Pulse state, hold to activate: Repeatedly hurls grenades forward during the skill, dealing Electric DMG and granting 1 Zap stack each time grenades are thrown. During the skill, tilt the stick/joystick to reposition and dodge enemy attacks. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["563.4%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Safety Regulation","d":"Press to dodge. A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Quick Inspection","d":"Press during a dodge to activate. Slide forward while shooting, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["33.3%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Violation Penalty","d":"Press during a perfect dodge to activate. Throws a grenade at enemies, dealing Electric DMG, then automatically triggers the Basic Attack\u0027s 4th hit. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["164.2%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Collaborative Construction","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the corresponding character to activate. Throws three grenades into the air then strafes to detonate them, dealing massive Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["571.3%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Demolition Blast - Beware","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum press to activate. Throws a custom grenade which explodes in the air and splits into four smaller grenades, dealing massive Electric DMG. Gains 8 stacks of Zap and 25 stacks of Pulse (max 25 stacks). Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1478.8%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Incident Management","d":"When the on-field character is launched in the air, press to activate. Throws a grenade at the enemy, dealing Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["45.5%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Evasive Assist: Rapid Risk Response","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Dodges the enemy\u0027s attack and activates the Vital View. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Counter Volt Needle","d":"Press after an Evasive Assist to activate. Unleashes a spinning hail of bullets against enemies in front and throws a grenade, dealing Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["359.3%"]}],"build":{"w":["Fusion Compiler","Weeping Gemini","Timeweaver","Electro-Lip Gloss"],"a":["Freedom Blues, Thunder Metal","Freedom Blues, Phaethon\u0027s Melody","Freedom Blues, Chaos Jazz","Thunder Metal, Freedom Blues"],"core":6.91,"st":[["CRIT Rate",12],["CRIT DMG",63],["ATK",2499]]},"how":"Grace’s general plan comes down to using her Basic Attacks to build Zap, then spending them with Special or EX Specials, juggling Anomalies and Disorders with another Anomaly Agent or even looping Shock triggers given her high Shock DMG values. Once there are enough Decibels, make sure to spend Zap before using Ultimate to get full benefit from its 8 Zap refill. The Pulse stacks give a boost to her damage through Ablooms, with the cycle of building and spending Zap repeating throughout. Even out-of-stun, there are some “combos” that Grace can do to maximise Zap cycling, Anomaly build-up and Decibel generation. B1 B2 B3 Special or EX Special B4 Special or EX Special Is the bread and butter of Grace’s rotations. After B1 or B2, slotting in a Side Input Basic works just fine and still allows for full Zap build and spend without sacrificing on time. Doing 2 sets of these will consume 25 Pulse and yield 4 Ablooms, while being the most effective in terms of damage (both raw DMG Multipliers and Anomaly build-up) as well as Energy and Decibel generation. When in Stun, holding Special for Special: Obstruction Removal - Cycle can work due to its rapid Zap generation. It isn’t as strong as looping Basics with regular Specials/EX Specials, but when the goal is to get as many Anomalies and Ablooms to fit within a short period, it can pull out ahead. The biggest potential point of optimisation is in managing her Ultimate use and its Abloom triggers. It may be better to hold onto it for a little longer if it may align with a Stun, and given that Ablooms scale with the current Anomaly inflicted on the enemy, timing its triggers to land on the strongest Anomaly (be it Grace’s Shock due to her Additional Ability, or a higher scaling element/better built Agent’s Anomaly) can go a long way at improving scores.","pros":"Has quick in-and-out rotations while being able to extend her field time if necessary; Big Anomaly application making her able to apply Shock effectively — particularly good in Disorder teams; Has no reliance on owning Limited weapons whatsoever, rather cheap to invest into when it comes to Skills since most of her damage comes from Anomaly.","cons":"All of her Specials and Ultimate (which are the focus of her kit) tend to make her step back which can cause positioning issues; Outside of Disorder teams, applying Shock multiple times will not provide any increase in damage Strong reliance on having multiple other Limited S-ranks in order to perform up to today\u0027s standard; Generally outclassed in any team she can be present in. In the meta, is only serviceable as a replacement option when certain Limited S-rank Agents are missing.","teams":[{"m":"Remielle + Grace + Velina + Ariel","c":"","r":"Rank 86"},{"m":"Grace + Velina + Yuzuha + Ultra Jake","c":"","r":"Rank 230"},{"m":"Remielle + Burnice + Grace + Ariel","c":"","r":"Rank 230"}]},"Nangong Yu":{"slug":"nangong-yu","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Shooting Star Step","d":"Press to activate: Perform up to three attacks forward, dealing Ether DMG.","m":["1st-Hit: 114.9%","2nd-Hit: 136.9%","3rd-Hit: 263.8%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Adorable Explosive Impact","d":"Hold to launch a charged attack, dealing Ether DMG. Release the button at the right moment to trigger precise charging, increasing the Daze dealt by the skill by 20%. Nangong Yu can perform up to three hits. The second and third hits each must consume 50 Downbeats. After using a Chain Attack, Ultimate, or EX Special Attack, if enough Downbeats are available, hold to skip the first hit and directly perform the second and third hits, which always trigger precise charging. When Nangong Yu is the active character, Chain Attacks, Ultimates, and EX Special Attacks do not interrupt the combo count of Basic Attack: Adorable Explosive Impact. While charging the first hit, Anti-Interrupt Level increases and DMG taken decreases by 60%. While charging the second and third hits, the character is Invulnerable. During the dash phase of the first hit, enemy attacks can be Blocked. On a successful Block, the attack is treated as a precise charging attack. Character is invulnerable during all attacks.","m":["1st-Hit: 104%","2nd-Hit: 304.4%","3rd-Hit: 510.8%","3rd-Hit (Coordinated): 587.5%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: The Weight of Love","d":"Press to activate. Delivers a morning star attack, dealing Ether DMG.","m":["83.5%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: The Unbearable Weight of Love","d":"With enough Energy, press to activate. Delivers a morning star attack, dealing Ether DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["533%","Energy Cost: 40%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Natural Dancer","d":"Press to activate. A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Spinning Meteor","d":"Press during a dodge to activate: Deliver a quick attack forward, dealing Ether DMG.","m":["190.7%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Asteroid Waltz","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Launch a series of attacks on the target, dealing Ether DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["355.3%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Comet Gravity","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Launch a series of attacks forward, dealing massive Ether DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["798.2%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Meteor Shower","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate: Launch multiple attacks forward, dealing massive Ether DMG. Upon activating this skill, Nangong Yu activates Ether Veil: Delusion Reprise. While Ether Veil: Delusion Reprise is active, all squad members gain an additional 50 ATK for 30s. If Nangong Yu activates Ether Veil: Delusion Reprise again, the current Ether Veil: Delusion Reprise will first deactivate. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["2101.7%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Emergency Save","d":"When the active character is launched, press to activate. Launches a series of attacks on the target, dealing Ether DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["74.8%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Perfected Choreography","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. This skill excels at parrying enemy attacks and reduces the consumption of Assist Points when the character is under intense attacks. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Improvised Performance","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate: Launches a series of attacks on the target, dealing massive Ether DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["535.8%"]}],"build":{"w":["Neon Fantasies","Hellfire Gears","The Simmering Pot","Steam Oven"],"a":["Phaethon\u0027s Melody, Freedom Blues","Phaethon\u0027s Melody, Chaos Jazz","Freedom Blues, Phaethon\u0027s Melody","Phaethon\u0027s Melody, Shining Aria"],"core":6.99,"st":[["CRIT Rate",14],["CRIT DMG",66],["ATK",2410]]},"how":"Nangong may have a lot of different resources and triggers, but her gameplan amounts to: Build-up her Downbeats gauge to 100, making use of Anomalies every 6 seconds to boost it faster. Land a full Charged Basic Attack or her Ultimate to apply Misstep, with either a Charged Basic Attack or EX Special hit to activate her Core Passive buffs. Once an enemy is stunned, use up her Dance Prowess stacks by swapping to her and/or landing EX Specials - the latter of which gets one free use every stun - and inflicting Ablooms/Disorders/Anomalies to trigger a max-Vibrato stack Abloom. This then repeats between every stun, making sure that all of her buffs and debuffs are maintained. Since a lot of Nangong’s Daze is loaded on resource-consuming skills, like her Charged Basic Attack, EX Special, and Ultimate, look to make use of her low-cost Defensive Assist where needed. With how loaded Nangong teams’ damage output is in stun, prioritise getting as many stuns as possible in a fight to maximise her value. As Nangong builds Anomaly quickly, managing her resources in-stun can be important depending on the team: a Miyabi team, for example, would demand clever use of EX Specials to sustain the Ether Anomalies required to get the multiple Disorders to fuel Shimotsuki casts. Aria teams, however, may benefit more from having Nangong’s EX Special come around when Anomaly gauges are high up, as despite her high damage, it would still partially dilute Corruption when compared to Aria’s own build-up. Each team will have its own distinct priorities, so tailoring how much Energy is needed on Nangong before going into a stun, how many parries each Agent gets for Decibel management as well as who on-fields and for how long will vary. Since her kit is rather straightforward though, it isn’t too difficult to be flexible and work around different character needs.","pros":"Jack-of-all trades, master of all: very high Daze, buffs the team, and can function as a sub-DPS. Multitude of niche but valuable benefits, like fast Heavy Attacks for Chain triggers, free EX Special casts and even lower cost Defensive Assists. Unlocks new routes and combos for Anomaly teams owing to fast stuns, Anomaly build-up buffs and extended stun durations. Such a broken unit that even her character demo acknowledges that she’s a Mary Sue","cons":"“Anomaly” Stunner, a class that few Anomaly Agents have matching Additional Abilities for, limiting many teams’ damage ceiling. Heavily reliant on her Signature W-Engine for best performance, with no alternative even coming close. High Anomaly build-up can be tricky to work with, be it in terms of dilution or Disorder ICD, depending on the team. Tako sausage hair is not edible; please do not munch on it.","teams":[{"m":"Miyabi + Nangong Yu + Yuzuha + Biggest Fan","c":"","r":"Rank 2"},{"m":"Aria + Nangong Yu + Sunna + Biggest Fan","c":"","r":"Rank 18"},{"m":"Miyabi + Nangong Yu + Astra Yao + Snap","c":"","r":"Rank 25"}]},"Koleda":{"slug":"koleda","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Smash \u0027n\u0027 Bash","d":"Press to activate: Unleashes up to 4 strikes, dealing Physical DMG. When Koleda has the Furnace Fire effect, she can launch an enhanced Basic Attack after the 2nd hit, consuming the Furnace Fire effect and dealing massive Fire DMG. Enhanced Basic Attack consists of two stages. After performing the first stage, press or hold to follow up with the second stage. The pursuit effect of the first-stage enhanced Basic Attack is also strengthened. Furnace Fire can stack up to 2 times. Performing an enhanced Basic Attack consumes all stacks of Furnace Fire. When Furnace Fire is consumed, all Agents deal 35% more damage for 40s. Repeated triggers refresh the duration. For each stack of Furnace Fire consumed, the second stage of the enhanced Basic Attack deals 10% more damage and inflicts 20% more Daze. When switching Agents during the first stage of the enhanced Basic Attack, Koleda remains on-field and automatically launches the second stage of the enhanced Basic Attack. When Koleda and Ben are both in the squad, using an enhanced Basic Attack without switching Agents during the first stage of the enhanced Basic Attack causes the two to perform a Coordinated Attack, further increasing the skill\u0027s power. Character is Invulnerable during the 4th hit of her Basic Attack and her enhanced Basic Attack. The invulnerability duration of the second-stage enhanced Basic Attack is increased.","m":["1st-Hit: 63.6%","2nd-Hit: 79.2%","3rd-Hit: 126.1%","4th-Hit: 317.4%","Enhanced Basic Attack 1st-Hit: 160.8%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Hammer Time","d":"Press to activate: Strikes enemies in front and triggers an explosion, dealing Fire DMG. This skill launches faster and directly triggers the explosion when used after the 2nd or 4th hit of Koleda\u0027s Basic Attack or enhanced Basic Attack. During the 2nd hit of her Basic Attack, holding can also trigger the explosion directly. When Koleda and Ben are both in your squad, and this skill is quickly launched after an enhanced Basic Attack, they team up to launch a coordinated attack, further increasing the power of the skill. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["Strike: 51.9%","Explosion: 77.8%","Explosion (Teamwork): 85.5%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Boiling Furnace","d":"With enough Energy, press to activate: Strikes enemies in front and triggers a powerful explosion, dealing massive Fire DMG. Koleda also gains the Furnace Fire effect. This skill activates faster and triggers an explosion when used after the 2nd or 4th hit of Koleda\u0027s Basic Attack or enhanced Basic Attack. Explosions triggered this way inflict 10% more Daze. When Koleda and Ben are both in your squad and this skill is quickly launched after an enhanced Basic Attack, they team up to launch a coordinated attack, further increasing the power of the skill. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. Hold to follow up with Dash Attack: Tremble!.","m":["Strike: 152.3%","Explosion: 606%","Explosion (Teamwork): 666.6%","Energy Cost: 60%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Wait \u0027n\u0027 See","d":"Press to dodge. A rapid dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Tremble!","d":"Press during a dodge to activate: Perform a forward strike, dealing Physical DMG. During this skill, if she has Furnace Fire, then Anti-Interrupt Level is increased. Hold to follow up with an enhanced Basic Attack.","m":["56.1%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Don\u0027t Look Down on Me","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate: Strikes enemies in front and creates an explosion, dealing Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. If Furnace Fire is active, hold to follow up with an enhanced Basic Attack.","m":["343.9%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Natural Disaster","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Unleashes a powerful explosion on enemies in a large area, dealing massive Fire DMG while also obtaining the Furnace Fire effect. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Hit: 636%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Hammerquake","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate: Unleashes a powerful explosion on enemies in a large area in front, dealing massive Fire DMG while also obtaining the Furnace Fire effect. Koleda and Ben can team up when fighting together to launch a coordinated attack, further increasing the power of the attack. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. Hold to follow up with Dash Attack: Tremble!.","m":["Hit: 1548.8%","Hit (Teamwork): 1694%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Coming Thru!","d":"When the active character is launched, press to activate: Strikes enemies in front, dealing Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["183.8%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Protective Hammer","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate: Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. This skill excels at parrying enemy attacks and reduces the consumption of Assist Points when the character is under intense attacks. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Hammer Bell","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate: Koleda charges and strikes enemies in front, dealing Fire DMG and obtaining Furnace Fire effect. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. Hold to follow up with Dash Attack: Tremble!.","m":["359.2%"]}],"build":{"w":["Hellfire Gears","Steam Oven","Precious Fossilized Core","The Restrained"],"a":["King of the Summit, Shockstar Disco","Shockstar Disco, Swing Jazz","Astral Voice, Shockstar Disco","Astral Voice, King of the Summit"],"core":6.93,"st":[["CRIT Rate",47],["CRIT DMG",100],["ATK",2380]]},"how":"Koleda is a very straightforward character. As the bulk of her buff value is in her Furnace Fire buff, it’s good to try and shoot for an Assist Follow-Up early in the fight, then use its Dash Attack into an enhanced Basic shortcut to activate it quickly. If she has the Energy for it, this can also be done with her EX, although it may be better to save its use for later if King of the Summit is being used to get better uptime on its effect. There is no value to staying on Koleda after she begins her enhanced Basic owing to its automatic transition, so swapping out of her to a damage dealer is best, but keep in mind that as she does stay on field for a while, this can lock her out of Defensive Assists. Once the buff is up, Koleda’s Basic Attacks aren’t all that useful, so look to bring her in with Defensive Assists instead to keep generating Furnace Fire and benefiting from its boost to her enhanced Basic. Some Agents do better with an on-field Stunner, though, and in such cases, using her Dodge Counter against aggressive enemies will work out. As she has no passive Daze and needs to use skills for it, Koleda allows for the fine-tuning of routes, especially as she can get very high burst Daze with her EX Special. Although using up her Furnace Fire on enhanced Basics is good, it can often be fine to prioritise field-time on other Agents even if it means overcapping on it, so long as the buff is refreshed every 40 seconds. Optimising her comes down to balancing out how often she’s on-field with the needs of other team members.","pros":"Some of the highest burst Daze in the game, which is a valuable Daze profile considering many endgame bosses and Shiyu’s timer requirements. Lower Assist Point consumption makes her sustainable and easy to use even against highly aggressive enemies. Accessible standard Stunner with well-rounded buffs, being one of the few that works directly with Armorers. Undeniably a sweet pea.","cons":"Ideally wants to have her M2 for best performance, as without it, she can struggle with resource management. Can be awkward to play at times, treading a fine line between active and inactive states if optimising Furnace Fire use. Actual buff value still falls behind that of most other Stunners, and even in the Armorer niche she isn’t always the best Standard pick. I thought this was a guide on the CEO of Belobog? Who’s this kid?","teams":[{"m":"Claret + Koleda + Rina + Plugboo","c":"","r":"Rank 12"},{"m":"Yixuan + Koleda + Lucia + Belion","c":"","r":"Rank 127"},{"m":"Billy - Starlight + Koleda + Lucia + Miss Esme","c":"","r":"Rank 161"}]},"Trigger":{"slug":"trigger","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Cold-Bore Shot","d":"Press to activate: Unleashes up to 4 shots ahead. The first 3 hits deal Physical DMG, the 4th hit deals Electric DMG.","m":["1st-Hit: 34.5%","2nd-Hit: 56.9%","3rd-Hit: 110.9%","4th-Hit: 243%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Silenced Shot","d":"Hold to activate: Trigger enters the Sniper Stance and fires forward continuously, dealing Electric DMG. While continually firing, when attacked by an enemy, Trigger will automatically evade. This effect can trigger once every 8s. While continually firing, you can drag the stick/joystick to adjust her position to the left/right/back. Automatically evading attacks or adjusting position when about to be hit will trigger a Perfect Dodge, followed by an automatic charged counter. After releasing , Trigger will step back, ready her weapon and unleash a Finishing Move, then exit Sniper Stance. Character is invulnerable during the charged counter and Finishing Move. When the continuous firing or the charged counter hits an enemy, Trigger gains 25 Purge, up to a maximum of 100 Purge. When the Finishing Move hits an enemy, it triggers the Quick Assist of the previous character in the squad.","m":["Shot: 47.6%","Counter: 233.9%","Finishing Move: 131.2%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Harmonizing Shot","d":"When Trigger has Purge, use another active character in the squad to hit an enemy with a Basic Attack, Dodge Counter, Special Attack, Dash Attack or Quick Assist to activate: While encircling the enemy, rapidly fire two shots at the enemy, dealing Electric DMG. Upon activating this skill, consume 3 Purge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. Basic Attack: Harmonizing Shot is an Aftershock attack. The squad can trigger Basic Attack: Harmonizing Shot once every 3s.","m":["47.9%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Harmonizing Shot - Tartarus","d":"When Trigger has Purge, use another active character in the squad to hit an enemy with a heavy attack from an EX Special Attack, Assist Follow-Up, or Ultimate to activate: While encircling the enemy, rapidly fires three shots at the enemy, followed by a Finishing Move, dealing Electric DMG. Upon activating this skill, consume 5 Purge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. Basic Attack: Harmonizing Shot - Tartarus is an Aftershock attack. The same skill type can trigger Basic Attack: Harmonizing Shot - Tartarus up to 2 times within 20s for the entire squad.","m":["Continuous Fire: 22.6%","Finishing Move: 45.2%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Spectral Flash","d":"Press to activate. Lunge forward with a slash, dealing Electric DMG. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["71.5%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Flash Burial","d":"With enough Energy, press to activate. Lunge forward with a slash, then leap up with a powerful shot to the ground, dealing massive Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. When this skill hits an enemy, it triggers the Quick Assist of the previous character in the squad. When this skill hits an enemy, Trigger enters Coordinated Support. While in this state, when another active character in the squad hits an enemy with any attack, it triggers a Basic Attack: Harmonizing Shot without consuming Purge and with no cooldown restrictions. This state lasts 8s and the effect can trigger up to 4 times. Each repeated trigger extends the duration and grants additional triggers, lasting a maximum of 20s and triggering up to a maximum of 10 times.","m":["634.4%","Energy Cost: 60%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Phantom Concealment","d":"Press to activate. A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Vengeful Specter","d":"Press during a dodge to activate: Rapidly lift the gun and fire, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["51.4%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Condemned Soul","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Rotate and fire a quick shot at enemies in front, dealing Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["219.7%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Stygian Guide","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Unleashes continuous powerful shots forward, dealing massive Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["574.7%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Underworld Requiem","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate. Deliver a powerful shot at enemies in a large area ahead, dealing massive Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. When the skill hits an enemy, it triggers the Quick Assist of the previous character in the squad. When the skill hits an enemy, Trigger enters Coordinated Support. While in this state, when another active character in the squad hits an enemy with any attack, it triggers a Basic Attack: Harmonizing Shot without consuming Purge and with no cooldown restrictions. This state lasts 12s and the effect can trigger up to 6 times. Each repeated trigger extends the duration and grants additional triggers, lasting a maximum of 20s and triggering up to a maximum of 10 times.","m":["1480.5%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Cold-Bore Cover Fire","d":"When the on-field character is launched, press to activate. Rotate and fire a quick shot at enemies in front, dealing Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["84.4%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Delaying Demise","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Piercing Thunder","d":"Press after an Evasive Assist to activate: Unleash a series of slashes at enemies ahead, followed by a powerful charged shot after landing, dealing Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["432.9%"]}],"build":{"w":["Spectral Gaze","The Restrained","Ice-Jade Teapot","Precious Fossilized Core"],"a":["King of the Summit, Woodpecker Electro","King of the Summit, Shockstar Disco","Shadow Harmony, Woodpecker Electro","Astral Voice, Woodpecker Electro"],"core":6.99,"st":[["CRIT Rate",85],["CRIT DMG",99],["ATK",2275]]},"how":"$undefined","pros":"Strong off-field presence via Aftershock attacks that inflict a lot of Daze and damage; Very simplistic in playstyle: just do 4 charged shots, swap out, rarely come back; Automatic dodge mechanic and lots of range for extra comfort — very easy to avoid enemy attacks; Universal Stun DMG Multiplier debuffer, making her a top choice way beyond Aftershock teams, not only as a Stun but as a Support too.","cons":"Really enjoys having her signature W-Engine, as it’s an amazing increase to her supportive presence via a practically permanent 25% DEF reduction on enemies. Her M1 is also amazing but both are expensive to acquire; Is locked out of several Anomaly team choices due to her Additional Ability activation condition, which hinders some of her massive team flexibility potential; Has trouble filling in for field time during the downtimes of certain Agents’ damage windows.","teams":[{"m":"Claret + Trigger + Rina + Plugboo","c":"","r":"Rank 14"},{"m":"Anby Soldier 0 + Orphie y Magus + Trigger + Mercury","c":"","r":"Rank 16"},{"m":"Cissia + Seed + Trigger + Plugboo","c":"","r":"Rank 30"}]},"Lycaon":{"slug":"lycaon","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Moon Hunter","d":"Press to activate. Unleashes up to 5 strikes in front, dealing Physical DMG. Hold down to charge up, increasing the power of the attack and dealing Ice DMG.","m":["1st-Hit: 29.2%","1st-Hit Charged: 37.1%","2nd-Hit: 34.9%","2nd-Hit Charged: 56.4%","3rd-Hit: 58.4%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Time to Hunt","d":"Press to activate. Unleashes a series of strikes in front, dealing Ice DMG. Hold down to charge up, increasing its power. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["77.1%","Charged: 133.1%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Thrill of the Hunt","d":"With enough energy, press to activate. Unleashes a series of powerful strikes in front, dealing massive Ice DMG. Hold down to charge up, consuming Energy and enhancing the power of the attack. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Base: 534.3%","Charged: 789.5%","Activation Energy Cost: 40%","Charged Attack Energy Cost: 20%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Suitable Positioning","d":"Press to dodge. A rapid dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Keep it Clean","d":"Press during a dodge to activate. Slide forwards, launching a series of strikes in front, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["47.3%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Etiquette Manual","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Strikes enemies in front, dealing Ice DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["181%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: As You Wish","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate. Unleashes a series of powerful strikes at enemies in a small area in front of him, dealing massive Ice DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["637.8%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Mission Complete","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate. Unleashes multiple powerful strikes at enemies in a large area, dealing massive Ice DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1694.1%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Wolf Pack","d":"When the on-field character is launched, press to activate. Strikes enemies in front, dealing Ice DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["63.1%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Disrupted Hunt","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Vengeful Counterattack","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate. Creates an icicle in front, which strikes all enemies within range, dealing Ice DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["288.3%"]}],"build":{"w":["The Restrained","Steam Oven","Hellfire Gears","Precious Fossilized Core"],"a":["King of the Summit, Shockstar Disco","Astral Voice, King of the Summit","Astral Voice, Shockstar Disco","King of the Summit, Woodpecker Electro"],"core":6.9,"st":[["CRIT Rate",51],["CRIT DMG",104],["ATK",2254]]},"how":"Despite having the ability to charge his Basic Attacks, keeping Lycaon as the active character and manually using them tends to not be ideal. Considering how much Daze he can build with his Assist Follow-Ups, and how it is required to enter the Encircle Prey state and being the most accessible way to apply Lycaon’s RES Shred and DMG Bonus, it’s often ideal to sit on another character until an opportunity to parry presents itself. Assist Follow-Up: Vengeful Counterattack - Glacial Waltz can then be used to consume to Encircle Prey charge and enter the state, after which he can be swapped out of and continue to build Daze and attack enemies. If Daze and Decibels are needed, frequent parries back to Lycaon can be repeated - but make sure to not accidentally use the Glacial Waltz variant on Assist Follow-Ups unless ending Encircle Prey pre-emptively is needed. As Energy builds up, it’s often worth using Lycaon’s EX Special Attack: Thrill of the Hunt for Daze and even some Anomaly build-up, as aligning Freeze timings for stuns can make a difference. This is true even for non-Freezeable enemies, owing to the CRIT DMG taken effect from Frostbite. It’s not often good to charge Lycaon’s EX in full. Although its multipliers are proportional to the extra Energy cost, it’s not quite a 50% improvement and takes more time, so splitting up EX Specials across more uses tends to be better, while also having the added benefit of maintaining buffs (like King of the Summit). As Stun approaches, make sure to open stun with Lycaon in some way to get the Stun DMG Multiplier increase, ideally with his EX Special for King of the Summit alignment. Once Stun is over, a new Encircle Prey stack is built and the cycle repeats, with the occasional Ultimate use where needed. Note that Lycaon’s playstyle can change depending on the team, with characters like Miyabi, Hugo, Yidhari and others all having distinct adjustments to be made. This can be in more precise management of Ice Anomaly build-up (important, as Encircle Prey attacks do not build any), having more frequent bouts of taking centre stage as the active character to make up for teammates that aren’t well suited to it, or stick to the standard, quick-swap Stunner playstyle. So long as buffs/debuffs are maintained and stun breakpoints are met, Lycaon is a flexible unit that can adjust to the needs of the team.","pros":"Very strong buff value, all the while having low EX Special costs (better enabling effects like King of the Summit) and strong Daze build. Demands surprisingly little field time to perform and can adjust to fit team needs. Standard Agent that’s easy to build and can work well with a variety of W-Engines, making him a strong and accessible pick. Best housekeeping service in all of New Eridu.","cons":"Only thrives in Ice teams, limiting his flexibility as a Stunner. Needs to be the one to initiate stuns, else he loses a significant portion of his value. Strictly a buff/daze unit only, with no additional effects (e.g. Ultimate conversions, Decibel bonuses, stun extensions) to support his value. Does not abide by child labor laws.","teams":[{"m":"Claret + Lycaon + Rina + Plugboo","c":"","r":"Rank 39"},{"m":"Sigrid + Lycaon + Rina + Butler","c":"","r":"Rank 74"},{"m":"Sigrid + Lycaon + Astra Yao + Sharkboo","c":"","r":"Rank 76"}]},"Ben":{"slug":"ben","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Debt Reconciliation","d":"Press to activate. Unleashes up to 3 strikes, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["1st-Hit: 65.9%","2nd-Hit: 189%","3rd-Hit: 348.3%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Fiscal Fist","d":"Press to activate. Ben lifts his weapon, blocking the enemy\u0027s attack before unleashing a forward strike, dealing Physical DMG. Successfully blocking an attack enhances the power of this skill and triggers Block Counter, dealing massive Physical DMG. Hold to remain in the Blocking stance. While in the Blocking stance, Ben gains a Shield that weakens over time. After leaving the blocking stance, the Shield is removed and recovers over time. The Shield cannot exceed 16% of Ben\u0027s Max HP. Ben is invulnerable when activating Block. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while launching strikes.","m":["Active Attack: 41.7%","Block Counter: 233.4%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Cashflow Counter","d":"With enough energy, press to activate. Ben lifts his weapon, blocking the enemy\u0027s attacks before unleashing a forward strike, dealing Fire DMG. Successfully blocking an attack enhances the power of this skill and triggers Block Counter, dealing massive Fire DMG. Hold to remain in the Blocking stance. While in the Blocking stance, Ben gains a Shield that weakens over time. After leaving the blocking stance, the Shield is removed and recovers over time. The Shield cannot exceed 16% of Ben\u0027s Max HP. When this skill is activated, the Shield is restored to its maximum value. After activating the skill, press again to follow up with a powerful forward strike, dealing massive Fire DMG. Ben is invulnerable when activating Block. Ben is invulnerable while launching strikes.","m":["Active Attack: 438.5%","Follow-Up: 438.5%","Block Counter: 500.5%","Block Follow-Up: 551.2%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Missing Invoice","d":"Press to dodge. A rapid dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Incoming Expense","d":"Press during a Dodge to activate. Strikes enemies in front of him, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["138.4%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Accounts Settled","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Strike enemies in front, dealing Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["225.7%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Signed and Sealed","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate. Unleashes a powerful slash at enemies in front of him in a large area, dealing massive Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["627.3%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Complete Payback","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate. Unleashes a powerful strike at enemies in front in a large area, dealing massive Fire DMG. When activating the skill, additionally recover 3 Assist Points. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1643%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Joint Account","d":"When the on-field character is launched, press to activate. Strikes enemies in front, dealing Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable during the attack.","m":["96.7%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Risk Allocation","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. This skill excels at parrying enemy attacks and reduces the consumption of Assist Points when the character is under intense attacks. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Don\u0027t Break Contract","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate. Charge and strike enemies in front, dealing Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["325.9%"]}],"build":{"w":["Tremor Trigram Vessel","Tusks of Fury"],"a":["Inferno Metal, Puffer Electro","Woodpecker Electro, Puffer Electro","Puffer Electro, Flex","Bunny in Wonderland, Swing Jazz"],"core":7,"st":[["CRIT Rate",55],["CRIT DMG",143],["ATK",3532]]},"how":"Ben tends to take an on-field role, as it gives him plenty of opportunities to build energy and make use of his EX Special Block Counter. He doesn’t constantly remain on field though, as his slow Basic 3 animation is a good opportunity to swap cancel to other characters for daze and damage. As he can shortcut into Basic 2 from his EX Special Block Counter (no follow-up attack needed!), it’s an effective way to speed through to the better parts of his string, helping recover the expended energy faster. Much of his gameplan adaptations ride around managing resource generation and Woodpecker stacks if the set is being run. This can involve quickswapping out of Ben shortly after starting attack animations to maximise energy gain, mixing up Dodge Counters with EX Special Block Counters to maintain Woodpecker stacks, or making use of dodges and Block Counters to animation cancel is Basic 3 animation if not swapped out of for faster transitions. Ben will want as much energy as possible going into stuns, to be able to make use of at least 2 full EX Special casts during it: Orphie EX Heat Charge (Enemy Stuns) Ben Quick Assist Basic 1 EX Special EX Special Follow-up Attack Dialyn Chain Attack Ben Ultimate (Dialyn Chain Conversion) Orphie Chain Orphie Ultimate Ben Quick Assist Basic 1 EX Special EX Special Follow-up Attack Ben Ultimate Basic 1 Basic 2 Orphie EX Heat Charge Ben Quick Assist Basic 1 Basic 2 Even without Dialyn, these rotations can follow broadly the same route, with Ben’s Chain taking place instead of the Ultimate conversion. Basics are used before EX Specials to help maintain Woodpecker stacks, and where possible, Stunners should be using their own EX Specials prior to stun start for King of the Summit, although the refresh halfway through with their Chain Attacks makes it easy to upkeep during the combo itself. Once over, repeat the process of building energy, Decibels, and pushing through to another stun to burst again.","pros":"Applies a sizable team-wide Shield when executing his EX combo. Grants all other Fire and Belobog agents 16% Crit Rate while Shielding them, allowing him to stand out from other Stun and Defense-based characters. When paired with Koleda will modify and significantly improve her Ultimate and Enhanced Basic Attacks.","cons":"Has far slower Movement Speed than any other character in the game making main fielding him cumbersome when moving around and not attacking. Despite having the potential to be played as a Daze character has less base Impact and no additional bonuses to his Daze potential in his kit causing him to fall noticeably behind dedicated Stun characters in the role. There\u0027s a limited amount of teams that can make use of his kit.","teams":[{"m":"Orphie y Magus + Norma + Ben + Ultra Jake","c":"","r":"Rank 388"},{"m":"Orphie y Magus + Lighter + Ben + Rocketboo","c":"","r":"Rank 388"},{"m":"Orphie y Magus + Dialyn + Ben + Rocketboo","c":"","r":"Rank 388"}]},"Remielle":{"slug":"remielle","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Leap","d":"Press to activate: Perform up to four attacks ahead, dealing Lumiflux DMG. If the Basic Attack hits the target, gain Floating Radiance after the skill ends. After the 4th hit of the Basic Attack ends, 1 Lumiflux Buildup is applied to enemies hit.","m":["1st-Hit: 31.2%","2nd-Hit: 54.5%","3rd-Hit: 84.3%","4th-Hit: 250.8%","1st Hit Floating Radiance Gained: 5%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Solo Dance","d":"Hold to activate: Perform a slash in an area ahead, dealing Lumiflux DMG. If it hits a target, gain Floating Radiance after the skill ends.","m":["96.5%","Floating Radiance Gained: 30%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Rainbow\u0027s End","d":"When Remielle has Voidflare, hold to activate: Unleash a powerful large area attack ahead, dealing Lumiflux DMG. Grants a large amount of [Floating Radiance] when the skill ends. If the attack hits a target, triggers the Luminize effect after the skill ends with a X% multiplier. Consumes all stored [Voidflare] upon use.","m":["195%","Floating Radiance Gained: 120%","Luminize Multiplier: 105%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Fleeting Grace","d":"When Remielle has stored Voidflare and is in the Luminous Reflection state, hold to activate: Unleash a powerful large area attack ahead, dealing Lumiflux DMG. Grants a large amount of Floating Radiance when the skill ends. If the attack hits a target, it triggers the Luminize effect after the skill ends with a multiplier of X%. Consumes all stored Voidflare upon use.","m":["597.2%","Floating Radiance Gained: 120%","Luminize Multiplier: 210%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Retreating Light","d":"Press to activate: A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Keen Light","d":"Press during a dodge to activate: Launch a quick attack ahead, dealing Lumiflux DMG.","m":["39%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Mirrored Shadow","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate: Unleash a powerful slash at the target, dealing Lumiflux DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["214.5%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Featherglow Rebirth","d":"When the active character is launched, press to activate: Unleash a slash at the target, dealing Lumiflux DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["32.5%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Fleeting Light","d":"When the on-field character is about to be attacked, press to activate: Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Awakening Glimmer","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate: Unleashes a series of slashes against the target, dealing Lumiflux DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["381.1%"]},{"t":"","n":"Assist: Flower \u0026 Feather Dance","d":"Enter the battlefield and unleash an attack in a large area, dealing Lumiflux DMG. Consumes 40 Floating Radiance upon activation. With 90 or fewer Floating Radiance remaining upon activation, this Assist: Flower \u0026 Feather Dance does not consume Floating Radiance. The character also enters the Luminous Reflection state, and the next Basic Attack: Rainbow\u0027s End is upgraded to Basic Attack: Fleeting Grace. When this skill hits a Stunned enemy, its Stun duration is extended by 3s. Each enemy can be affected by this effect only once per Stun. This Stun duration increase cannot stack with other effects of the same type. If the skill hits, the Luminize effect can be triggered after the skill ends with a multiplier of X%. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["453.5%","Luminize Multiplier: 210%","Floating Radiance Consumed: 40%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Sliver of Light","d":"Press to activate: Launch a ranged attack ahead, dealing Lumiflux DMG.","m":["49.9%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Ode to Dawn","d":"Upon entering the battlefield, if the character has less than 60 Energy, recover Energy to 60. In Investigation Zone Mode, this effect can trigger once every 180s; With enough Energy, press to activate: Unleash a powerful attack across a large area ahead, dealing Lumiflux DMG; After the skill ends, apply 2 [Lumiflux Buildup] to all enemies hit; Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["721.5%","Energy Cost: 60%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Ode to Dawn - Radiant Turn","d":"When Remielle is in-combat and [Floating Radiance] reaches its maximum of 120, hold after a [Special Attack] or [EX Special Attack] to enter [Stance Shift]. Switching Characters while in [Stance Shift] enters the [Phase Flow] state: While in the [Phase Flow] state, Remielle acts autonomously to assist in combat. Some attacks also apply [Lumiflux Buildup] to the target. [Floating Radiance] is consumed over time while in the [Phase Flow] state. When [Floating Radiance] is depleted or Remielle leaves the in-combat state, she exits the [Phase Flow] state. Before exiting the [Phase Flow] state, Remielle cannot be switched in except via a [Chain Attack]; If Remielle triggers 3 Refringe reactions while in the [Phase Flow] state, or has at least 1 stored Voidflare when [Floating Radiance] is depleted, [Assist: Flower \u0026 Feather Dance] is activated, unlocking normal switch-ins and automatically triggering [Assist: Flower \u0026 Feather Dance] on Remielle\u0027s next normal switch-in; Upon entering the [Phase Flow] state, all squad members\u0027 DMG dealt is increased by X% for 60s. Repeated triggers reset the duration; If Remielle uses a [Special Attack] or [EX Special Attack] that hits a Stunned enemy and [Floating Radiance] has reached its maximum of 120, switching Characters during the [Special Attack] or [EX Special Attack] also enters the [Phase Flow] state; If no character is switched in after entering [Stance Shift], Remielle uses a downward attack to return to the ground.","m":["164.7%","DMG Increase: 1.5%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Interwoven Dance Steps","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Launch multiple attacks ahead in a large area, dealing Lumiflux DMG. Enter the Luminous Reflection state upon activation. The next Basic Attack: Rainbow\u0027s End is upgraded to Basic Attack: Fleeting Grace. After the skill ends, apply 2 Lumiflux Buildup to enemies hit. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["785.2%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Dazzling Curtain Call","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate: Launch a attack across a large area in front, dealing Lumiflux DMG. If the skill hits, the Luminize effect can be triggered after the skill ends with a multiplier of X%. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["2009.7%","Luminize Multiplier: 220.5%"]}],"build":{"w":["Ode of Resurrected Wings","Weeping Gemini","Flamemaker Shaker","Timeweaver"],"a":["Feathered Fate, Freedom Blues","Feathered Fate, Chaos Jazz","Feathered Fate, Astral Voice","Feathered Fate, Hormone Punk"],"core":7,"st":[["CRIT Rate",12],["CRIT DMG",64],["ATK",3991]]},"how":"For all of Remielle’s mechanics, she has a straightforward gameplay loop: Begin by holding Special to enter Phase Flow early in the fight. Apply 3 Anomalies to generate 3 Voidflares for Remielle. Swap to Remielle for her Assist, Ultimate if available, then use her enhanced Basic for Luminizes. Hold Special to enter Phase Flow again. That’s the gist of how she’s used. There is potential for optimisation, as following this strict criteria isn’t always best. If possible, opening stuns with Remielle’s hold Basic is best, as it allows for it to do damage without losing stun time to its long animation. This can be hard to set-up though, so while ideal it won’t always be possible. As her enhanced Basic also has a very long animation, it isn’t always worth using in stun. Agents that can build Anomaly while still contributing damage (like Abloomers), or in Vortex teams, it can be better to delay its use to after stun and prioritise other Agents damage then. If an Ultimate is available shortly before a stun, it may be best to save its use to in stun if it doesn’t come at the cost of total Ultimate count or alignment later. Likewise, overcapping on Voidflares can sometimes be fine if it doesn’t lead to fewer Luminizes in a fight. Remielle might be close or at max Voidflares, but going into her long animations could lead to buffs or Anomalies dropping, or mean she ends up getting a bad combo in stun. In these situations, holding back on a swap to her may be best. On Vortex teams, this isn’t as much of a concern owing to the long 30-second duration, but it can still be a factor at times. In the aggregate though, getting as many Luminizes out as possible is a priority, and much of her teams’ optimisation comes in making good use of the other 2 Anomaly Agents instead, like by maximising the number of Vortexes or keeping Disorders going in spite of Remielle’s long animations.","pros":"A “Void Hunter” who is both incredibly strong and versatile, packing great buffs, Daze application and personal damage contribution. Lumiflux and Luminize inheriting elements means that she can always have a matching weakness no matter the enemy and can also get around any resistances. Surprisingly simple to pick up, with a straightforward gameplan that makes her be highly accessible. Kind of a baddie... actually definitely a baddie.","cons":"Ridiculously long animations for her burst and Phase Flow, with Anomalies and ally buffs being at the risk of falling off, robbing Agents of field time. Limited synergy with most Anomaly Agents, as Lumiflux doesn’t work like a traditional Anomaly and Luminize fails to benefit from many forms of Anomaly DMG. Highly reliant on her own and other Agents’ Signature W-Engines, as her Voidflares scale with other Agents’ Anomalies, demanding the whole team to be well built. Qualifies for senior discounts twice over.","teams":[{"m":"aria, promeia, burnice + velina","c":"","r":""},{"m":"promeia + vivian","c":"","r":""},{"m":"jane-doe + velina, alice","c":"","r":""}]},"Vivian":{"slug":"vivian","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Feathered Strike","d":"Press to activate: Unleashes up to 4 attacks in front, dealing Physical DMG and Ether DMG. After triggering the fourth attack, enter the Noblewoman state. With Flight Feathers available, holding during the fourth attack will activate the Fluttering Frock state.","m":["1st-Hit: 34.1%","2nd-Hit: 24.2%","3rd-Hit: 76.9%","4th-Hit: 128.4%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Noblweoman - Waltz","d":"Press while in the Noblewoman state to activate: Dash forward with an attack that deals Ether DMG and restores 1 Flight Feather upon hitting an enemy. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. If a Perfect Dodge is triggered during the dash, gain 1 additional Flight Feather. If Flight Feathers are available after the skill, enter the Fluttering Frock state, which can be canceled by holding when the skill is used.","m":["47.8%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Fluttering Frock - Suspension","d":"Press while in the Fluttering Frock state to activate: Attack an area ahead, dealing Ether DMG. After activation, this skill consumes all Flight Feathers, and each one consurned grants 1 Guard Feather. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. When switching characters during the Fluttering Frock state, Vivian will automatically perform Basic Attack: Fluttering Frock - Suspension. While in the Fluttering Frock state, press to exit the state.","m":["80.2%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Featherbloom","d":"After any character in the squad hits a target with an EX Special Attack, Vivian will consume 1 Guard Feather to launch Basic Attack: Featherbloom against the target, dealing Ether DMG, triggering at most once per use of a skill. This effect can trigger even while Vivian is off-field. A maximurn of 5 Guard Feathers can be stored.","m":["220%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Song of Silver Wings","d":"Press to activate. Quickly attack forward, dealing Physical DMG and Ether DMG. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["56.9%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Violet Requiem","d":"With enough Energy, press to activate. Unleash a powerful forward attack that deals massive Ether DMG and grants 3 Flight Feathers. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. Enter the Fluttering Frock state after using the skill. Hold during the skill to enter the Noblewoman state.","m":["592.6%","Energy Cost: 60%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Lightstream","d":"Press to activate. A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Silver Thorned Melody","d":"Press during a dodge to activate: Launches a forward thrust at enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["59.6%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Wingblade Reverb","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Launches an attack on enemies ahead, dealing Physical DMG and Ether DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. After activating the skill, enter the Noblewoman state. When there are Flight Feathers available, hold during skill activation to enter the Fluttering Frock state.","m":["236.4%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Dainty Steps","d":"When in the Noblewoman state and about to be attacked, an automatic dodge will trigger, during which the character will be Invulnerable, but a Perfect Dodge will not be triggered. This can trigger once each time the Noblewoman state is entered.","m":[]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Chorus of Celestial Wings","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Launch a powerful attack on a large area of enemies ahead, dealing massive Ether DMG and gaining 2 Flight Feathers. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. After the skill activates, enter the Fluttering Frock state, which can be canceled by holding during the skill.","m":["658.9%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":" Ultimate: Soarding Bird\u0027s Song","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate. Launch a powerful attack on a large area of enemies ahead, dealing massive Ether DMG and gaining 5 Flight Feathers. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. After the skill is activated, enter the Fluttering Frock state, which can be canceled by holding during the skill.","m":["1686.8%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Frostwing Guard","d":"When the active character is launched, press to activate. Launches an attack on enenies ahead, dealing Physical DMG and Ether DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. After the skill activates, enter the Noblewoman state. With Flight Feathers available, hold during skill activation to enter the Fluttering Frock state.","m":["97.3%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Silver Umbrella Formation","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Featherblade Execution","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate: Launch an attack at enanies ahead, dealing Ether DMG and gaining 2 Flight Feathers. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. After the skill activates enter the Fluttering Frock state, which can be canceled by holding during the skill.","m":["373.9%"]}],"build":{"w":["Flight of Fancy","Weeping Gemini","Electro-Lip Gloss","Rainforest Gourmet"],"a":["Phaethon\u0027s Melody, Freedom Blues","Phaethon\u0027s Melody, Chaos Jazz","Phaethon\u0027s Melody, Feathered Fate","Phaethon\u0027s Melody, Freedom Blues, Flex"],"core":7,"st":[["CRIT Rate",14],["CRIT DMG",67],["ATK",2521]]},"how":"Rotations Vivian\u0027s rotations are dynamic depending on the enemy you\u0027re fighting, the resources you have available (Decibels, Chain Attacks, EX Specials, Assist Points...) and your 2 other party members. However, we listed below some possible combos to help you build Flight Feathers from 0 to 4 or 5 and quickly convert them into Guard Feathers to activate her Ablooms as fast as possible.Note: Chain Attack can replace any Defensive Assist + Assist Follow-Up or Noblewoman - Waltz if available. It\u0027s also possible in very rare cases to Chain twice into Vivian to perform a 4 Flying Feather combo only using 2 Chain Attacks, however other teammates may want to execute Chain Attacks instead.IMPORTANT: If Vivian has any Guard Feathers, only use EX Specials on any character if an Attribute Anomaly is present on the enemy! Otherwise, Abloom will not activate and the Guard Feather will be wasted. OPENER COMBO Use this combo at the start of runs in modes where EX Special Energy is available. If Energy is not available right away, perform the No Energy Combo with 1 less Defensive Assist and Assist Follow-Up. Start with 2 Flying Feathers (Core Passive) EX Special (Swap) Fluttering Frock: Suspension NO ENERGY COMBO: Basic P4/Quick Assist/Dodge Counter Noblewoman - Waltz Defensive Assist Assist Follow-Up Defensive Assist Assist Follow-Up (Swap) Fluttering Frock: Suspension EX SPECIAL COMBO: Defensive Assist Assist Follow-Up EX Special (Swap) Fluttering Frock: Suspension NO ASSIST ENERGY COMBO: This combo will only give you 5 Flying Feathers if Noblewoman - Waltz also activates a Perfect Dodge. Otherwise, this will give you 4 Flying Feathers (still acceptable). Noblewoman - Waltz EX Special (Swap) Fluttering Frock: Suspension ULTIMATE COMBO: Make sure to only use Ultimate when all Guard Feathers have been consumed, as it regenerates them fully. Ultimate (Swap) Fluttering Frock: Suspension","pros":"Damage scales directly with Anomaly DPS strength — the more Anomaly damage your DPS does, the better she becomes; Great team flexibility with many strong and viable synergies; Very capable F2P W-Engine option.","cons":"Potential damage can suffer if your other anomaly characters aren\u0027t sufficiently invested into; Relies on Perfect Assists to make the best use of her kit, making her enemy-dependent to an extent,","teams":[{"m":"Miyabi + Vivian + Yuzuha + Robin","c":"","r":"Rank 19"},{"m":"Remielle + Phoenix + Vivian + Ariel","c":"","r":"Rank 34"},{"m":"Promeia + Vivian + Yuzuha + Robin","c":"","r":"Rank 41"}]},"Pyrois":{"slug":"pyrois","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Emberglow","d":"Press to activate: Performs up to three attacks forward, dealing Ether DMG.","m":["1st-Hit: 45.6%","2nd-Hit: 64.1%","3rd-Hit: 276.3%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Celestial Light","d":"With 30 or more , hold to activate: Unleashes up to four attacks forward, dealing massive Ether DMG. If another character is switched in during the 3rd hit, Pyrois automatically performs the 4th hit off-field. Each hit consumes a certain amount of Solar Prominence. Character is invulnerable during the 3rd and 4th hits.","m":["1st-Hit: 107%","2nd-Hit: 143.8%","3rd-Hit: 549%","4th-Hit: 641%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Twilight","d":"Press to activate: A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Sunrise","d":"Press during a dodge to activate: Delivers a quick slash forward, dealing Ether DMG.","m":["95.3%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: First Light","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate: Performs a forward spinning slash, dealing Ether DMG. After using the skill and with 30 or more , hold Icon_Normal to immediately follow up with the 3rd hit of Basic Attack: Celestial Light. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["228.7%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Duskguard","d":"When the active character is launched, press to activate: Launches a series of attacks against the target, dealing Ether DMG. After using the skill and with 30 or more , hold Icon_Normal to immediately follow up with the 3rd hit of Basic Attack: Celestial Light. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["41.2%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Ironhide Behemoth","d":"When the on-field character is about to be attacked, press to activate: Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Return to Daylight","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate: Performs a forward thrust attack, dealing Ether DMG. After using the skill and with 30 or more , press or hold to immediately follow up with the 3rd hit of Basic Attack: Celestial Light. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["338.6%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Fading Rays","d":"Press to activate: Performs a rush attack, dealing Ether DMG.","m":["52.1%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Sun\u0027s Halo","d":"With enough Energy, press to activate: Quickly charges forward and performs a series of consecutive attacks, dealing massive Ether DMG. If hit by an enemy attack during the charge, triggers a Perfect Block effect, nullifying the damage and increasing the move\u0027s Interrupt Level to that of a Heavy Defensive Assist. After using the skill and with 30 or more , hold to immediately follow up with the 3rd hit of Basic Attack: Celestial Light. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["737.4%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Assault Directive","d":"When an Ultimate or EX Special Attack: Sun\u0027s Halo is used, Phaethon performs an assist attack, dealing Ether DMG. This effect can trigger once every 2.5s, and is guaranteed to trigger when using an Ultimate.","m":["82.8%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Ceremonial March","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Performs a coordinated attack with Phaethon, dealing massive Ether DMG. After using the skill and with 30 or more , press or hold to immediately follow up with the 3rd hit of Basic Attack: Celestial Light. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1058.3%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Total Annihilation","d":"When Decibel Rating is at or above Blasting, press and select the upper branch to activate: After charging, performs a downward slash, dealing massive Ether DMG. After using the skill and with 30 or more , press or hold to immediately follow up with the 3rd hit of Basic Attack: Celestial Light. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["866.2%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Triumphant Return","d":"When Decibel Rating is at or above Blasting, press and select the lower branch to activate: Releases an energy burst in the surrounding area, dealing massive Ether DMG. After using the skill and with 30 or more , hold to immediately follow up with the 3rd hit of Basic Attack: Celestial Light. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["866.2%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Unbound Swordstorm","d":"When Decibel Rating is at or above Blasting, press and select the left branch to activate: Unleashes consecutive attacks forward, dealing massive Ether DMG. After using the skill and with 30 or more , hold to immediately follow up with the 3rd hit of Basic Attack: Celestial Light. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["973.3%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Eternal Imprisonment","d":"When Decibel Rating is at or above Blasting, press and select the right branch to activate: Gathers energy ahead before unleashing a Finishing Move, dealing massive Ether DMG. After using the skill and with 30 or more , hold to immediately follow up with the 3rd hit of Basic Attack: Celestial Light. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["997%"]}],"build":{"w":["Sol Exuvia","Marcato Desire","Gilded Blossom","The Brimstone"],"a":["The Sky Ablaze, Woodpecker Electro","The Sky Ablaze, Branch \u0026 Blade Song","The Sky Ablaze, Puffer Electro","The Sky Ablaze, Astral Voice"],"core":7,"st":[["CRIT Rate",68],["CRIT DMG",132],["ATK",3427]]},"how":"Despite the various Ultimates, Pyrois has a rather flowcharty approach to gameplay. Once enemies spawn, make use of their “Lower” Ultimate to get its buffs applied for the encounter. This can then be followed by their EBA3 and 4, or an EX Special, which links into an EBA3. Pyrois can then build resources in the out-of-stun period and expend them on EBAs as needed to avoid overcapping. As EBA1 and 2 have low multipliers, reserve resources for EBA3, which shouldn’t be difficult to do so as almost all skills in their kit will shortcut to it. Since they can parry for extra Solar Prominence, it’s worth trying to get some to squeeze in more damage out-of-stun. Ideally, Pyrois needs to have plenty of Decibels stored to be able to do 2 Ultimates in a single stun. A combo then follows with: “Upper” Ultimate Cancel Chain Attack EBA3 + 4 Swap out to another Agent, as EBA4 will cast automatically. Trigger Pyrois’ Chain Attack EX Special EBA3 + 4 “Right” Ultimate Decibels may not always allow for this, in which case, doing 2 Pyrois Chain Attacks and ending with the “Right” Ultimate will be best. After which push to another stun while trying to optimise Decibels to sustain double Ultimates where possible.","pros":"Completely free and should always be attainable, regardless of banner changes! Not only rivals, but exceeds many limited Agents that came before him, having exceptionally good multipliers. Easy to build, having their ideal W-Engine also being free and very strong. Looks like a FromSoftware boss.","cons":"Optimal combos are heavily Decibel-dependent, which can make them reliant on specific Agents or routing to excel. Isn’t immediately accessible, so new or returning players who want to experience story progression will take time to acquire him. No traditional vertical investment, which may limit their longevity as time passes. Urban Fantasy?","teams":[{"m":"dialyn + sunna, nicole-demara","c":"","r":""},{"m":"sunna + nicole-demara","c":"","r":""},{"m":"ju-fufu + astra-yao, sunna, nicole-demara","c":"","r":""}]},"Yidhari":{"slug":"yidhari","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Crushing Strike","d":"Press to activate: Unleashes up to 3 strikes, dealing Ice DMG. On the 3rd hit, Yidhari recovers 10% HP.","m":["1st-Hit: 60.7%","1st-Hit (ALT): 62.4%","2nd-Hit: 86%","3rd-Hit: 207.8%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Frostbite Embrace","d":"Hold to activate: Yidhari begins charging, continuously consuming HP to reach up to three levels of charge. When is released, Yidhari unleashes a powerful charged hammer attack in front based on the current charge level, dealing massive Ice DMG. The higher Yidhari\u0027s HP, the faster charging consumes it. HP consumption will at most reduce Yidhari\u0027s HP to 25% of Max HP. At 2 charge levels, after using the skill, press to immediately follow up with the 3rd hit of Basic Attack: Crushing Strike. The DMG of a Basic Attack: Crushing Strike triggered this way increases based on the current charge level, up to 30%. At 3 charge levels, Yidhari gains increased Anti-Interrupt level during the charged skill. Press to chain early into the finishing smash.","m":["Level-1 Charged Attack: 161.4%","Level-2 Charged Attack: 254.1%","Level-3 Charged Attack: 345.9%","Level-3 Charged Spin DMG: 235.8%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Frost\u0027s Crushing Weight","d":"While charging or spinning during Basic Attack: Frostbite Embrace, if hit by an enemy, Yidhari can block with her tentacles, reducing the DMG taken by 25%. If charging or not yet at full charge, Yidhari counterattacks with her tentacles, returning to the charging stance and instantly gaining 1 charge level, while also dealing Ice DMG to enemies ahead. While Frost\u0027s Crushing Weight is active, pressing makes Yidhari immediately unleash the finishing slam of Basic Attack: Frostbite Embrace based on her current charge level. While Frost\u0027s Crushing Weight is active, pressing or makes Yidhari unleash a Special Attack: Surging Cold, Crushing Pursuit that is guaranteed to trigger Surging Cold.","m":["48.7%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Cease Thoughts","d":"Press to activate. Launches enemies in front into the air, dealing Ice DMG. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["39.6%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Frost Coil","d":"With enough Adrenaline, press to activate. Perform two consecutive upward strikes, then release an icy mist, dealing massive Ice DMG. If EX Special Attack: Frost Coil hits an enemy, Yidhari recovers HP at the end of the skill equal to 33% of her missing HP. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["510.2%","Adrenaline Cost: 60%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Surging Cold, Crushing Pursuit","d":"Press or while charging or spinning during Basic Attack: Frostbite Embrace, or press while holding to activate: Launches enemies in front into the air, dealing Ice DMG. When the skill\u0027s attack collides with an enemy\u0027s attack, it triggers Surging Cold. If the skill hits a Stunned enemy, and with sufficient Adrenaline, it triggers Crushing Pursuit. Triggering Surging Cold or Crushing Pursuit instantly raises the charge level to maximum. During this skill, press and Yidhari will immediately unleash the finishing slam of Basic Attack: Frostbite Embrace based on the current charge level. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["83.7%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Glacial Crush","d":"When triggering Surging Cold or Crushing Pursuit, and with enough Adrenaline, press or to activate.Dash forward with an upward attack, then leap into the air before delivering a powerful downward smash, dealing massive Ice DMG. If EX Special Attack: Glacial Crush hits an enemy, Yidhari heals at the end of the skill for 33% of her missing HP. If the skill is used after Surging Cold, it grants an additional 15 Adrenaline. This effect can trigger once every 1s. After using this skill, press to immediately unleash the finishing slam of Basic Attack: Frostbite Embrace based on the current charge level. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["EX Special Attack: Glacial Crush: 1007.6%","Additional Ability Icy Tentacle: 79.2%","Adrenaline Cost: 60%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Dreamshift","d":"Press to activate. A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Frostbloom Impact","d":"Press during a dodge to activate: Strike forward, dealing Ice DMG.","m":["70.5%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Icehaul Reverb","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Strikes enemies in front, dealing Ice DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["185.3%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Frostbound Oath","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Unleash a powerful strike against enemies in a small area ahead, dealing massive Ice DMG. If inside Ether Veil: Wellspring, tentacles join in the assault, further enhancing the skill\u0027s power. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["572.7%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Ether Veil: Wellspring","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, the final hit of Basic Attack: Frostbite Embrace, EX Special Attack: Frost Coil, EX Special Attack: Glacial Crush, and Chain Attack: Frostbound Oath will consume 3,000 Decibels to activate an Ether Veil: Wellspring. While Ether Veil: Wellspring is active, all squad members\u0027 Max HP increase by 5% for 30s. Repeated triggers extend the duration, up to a maximum of 300s. While Yidhari is within Ether Veil: Wellspring, the charge speed of Basic Attack: Frostbite Embrace increases, and HP is consumed faster during charging.","m":["Ether Veil: Wellspring: 629.9%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Final Act - Crossing the River of Regret","d":"After Yidhari expends Decibels to activate Ether Veil: Wellspring, press within 30s to activate: Deliver a powerful strike to enemies in a large area ahead, dealing massive Ice DMG. Character is invulnerable while performing the powerful strike. Each time Yidhari expends Decibels to activate an Ether Veil: Wellspring, she can use Ultimate: Final Act - Crossing the River of Regret once.","m":["1522.1%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Frostshock Reinforcement","d":"When the active character is launched, press to activate. Strikes enemies in front, dealing Ice DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["82.2%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Flashquake Rejection","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Glacial Onslaught","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate: Execute an ice shard hammer attack against enemies in front, dealing Ice DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["313.4%"]}],"build":{"w":["Kraken\u0027s Cradle","Cauldron of Clarity"],"a":["Yunkui Tales, Branch \u0026 Blade Song","Yunkui Tales, Woodpecker Electro","Yunkui Tales, Polar Metal"],"core":7,"st":[["CRIT Rate",64],["CRIT DMG",150],["ATK",2041]]},"how":"Yidhari’s approach to fights is rather straightforward: stay on-field as much as possible and loop her charged Basic Attack (Frostbite Embrace) finisher into her Basic 3 (Crushing Strike). This both has her constantly dish out damage and build resources for stun combos. It is not recommended to allow the spin from fully charging her Basic Attack to go through, as its damage and resource build values are too low to make it worthwhile - although it can be useful in some modes, like Shiyu Defence, to gather up mobs due to its wide vacuum effect. Rather than using Dodge Counters on Yidhari, allow her to get hit while charging, as this provides faster charge build. If the charge is just beginning, use her Special counter (Surging Cold) to instantly max out charge and shortcut straight into the charged Basic Attack finisher, or if at above half charge, it’s faster to just get hit for a max charge. Do try to always link into the Basic 3 after a charged Basic Attack, as it’s the only way for Yidhari to self-heal without expending resources. Anything that shortcuts into the charged Basic Attack finisher means Basic 3 can follow right after, so there’s many opportunities to use it. Since her Decibel generation is primarily tied to HP loss, cycling between healing and consuming HP is an important part of her gameplan. Between attacks, it’s good to build a habit to swap to other characters every so often, like to a Stunner via Defensive Assists or during Yidhari’s Basic animations to use EX Specials for daze and King of the Summit. Alternatively, swap to a Support to ensure their buffs and Drive Disc effects (like Moonlight Lullaby) are maintained. When Adrenaline is near cap out-of-stun, a Special counter into her enhanced EX Special (Glacial Crush) should be used, as its obscenely high damage and daze multipliers make it the highest single source of damage for Yidhari. Be careful to not do so when too close to stun though, as Yidhari will want to fit in 2 casts of her enhanced EX Special, but the 15 Adrenaline refund can enable its use even if high in daze build. Her ideal stun combo demands at least 100+ Adrenaline at stun start and is as follows: Be on another character to trigger Chain Yidhari Chain Attack Cancel Special: Crushing Pursuit (Hold Basic, then tap Special) EX Special: Glacial Crush Swap to another character to trigger Chain Yidhari Chain Attack Ultimate Special: Crushing Pursuit (Hold Basic, then tap Special) EX Special: Glacial Crush Charged Basic Attack Basic 3 If correctly executed, all hits up to and including the Charged Basic Attack will land","pros":"Easy to pick up, with a straightforward gameplan while being effectively immortal. Performs well even at low investment costs, with ‘cheap’ teams and flexible W-Engine options. Relatively well-rounded and self-sufficient; has damage, survivability, mob grouping ability, etc. Tentacles.","cons":"Damage is spread out across multiple skills, making her expensive to invest in. Limited value pull, with only one encounter where she is the best pick for (Wandering Hunter). Can feel awkward to play in certain teams, especially if missing Lucia. Tentacles.","teams":[{"m":"Yidhari + Dialyn + Lucia + Miss Esme","c":"","r":"Rank 32"},{"m":"Yidhari + Lycaon + Lucia + Sharkboo","c":"","r":"Rank 97"},{"m":"Yidhari + Norma + Lucia + Miss Esme","c":"","r":"Rank 116"}]},"Anby: Soldier 0":{"slug":"anby-demara-soldier-0","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Penetrating Shock","d":"Press to activate: Perform up to five slashes ahead, dealing Electric DMG. On the 3rd hit of the Basic Attack, enemies are continuously pulled in. After the 4th attack hits the enemy, repeatedly press or hold to quickly pass through enemies in front up to 5 times.","m":["1st-Hit: 32.7%","2nd-Hit: 62.2%","3rd-Hit: 100.1%","3rd-Hit Finisher: 39.9%","4th-Hit: 154.5%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Celestial Thunder","d":"Press to activate. Dash diagonally forward, then unleash a cross slash, dealing Electric DMG. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["59.6%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Azure Flash","d":"When Soldier 0 - Anby\u0027s attacks hit an enemy, they apply the Silver Star mark and charges the target. For every one-third of charge, the enemy receives 1 stack of White Thunder, stacking up to 3 times. When the enemy has White Thunder, press to activate: Quickly dash forward, slashing through enemies and dealing multiple hits of Electric DMG. When the skill hits an enemy, it will consume 1 stack of White Thunder to trigger an Aftershock that deals 1 extra instance of Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["White Thunder: 167.2%","43%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Thunder Smite","d":"When the additional damage from White Thunder triggers 3 times on the same enemy: A lightning strike will fall at the enemy\u0027s location, dealing Electric DMG to enemies within range. This DMG is considered Aftershock DMG.","m":["Thunder Smite: 188.1%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Azure Flash - Boundary","d":"When Special Attack: Thunder Smite DMG is triggered: If EX Special Attack: Sundering Bolt or Special Attack: Azure Flash is currently being used, then Special Attack: Azure Flash - Boundary will automatically trigger when the current skill ends, unleashing a flurry of slashes that deal multiple instances of Electric DMG. This skill counts as an Aftershock. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["249.4%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Sundering Bolt","d":"With enough Energy, hold to activate: Combines her twin swords and throws them forward for a high-speed slash, dealing massive Electric DMG. When the skill hits an enemy, it will fully charge Silver Star. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["379.6%","Energy Cost: 60%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Strobe","d":"Press to activate. A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Torrent","d":"Press during a dodge to activate: Perform a horizontal slash forward, then follow up with a thrust attack, dealing Electric DMG.","m":["82.5%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Ground Flash Counter","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Perform consecutive slashes at enemies in front, dealing Electric DMG. On hit, gain the Voltage Overload state for 15s. Repeated triggers refresh the duration. While in the Voltage Overload state, dodge performance is enhanced. Additionally, when using Basic Attack/Dash Attack/Dodge Counter, if the enemy target has White Thunder, pressing will immediately cancel the current skill and launch Special Attack: Azure Flash. While in this state, if the enemy does not have White Thunder, press to directly launch EX Special Attack: Sundering Bolt. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["250.6%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Leaping Thunderstrike","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Leap forward, then quickly dive and perform a cross slash, dealing massive Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["563.8%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Voidstrike","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate. Perform a powerful series of slashes at a large area in front, followed by a lightning strike, dealing massive Electric DMG. When the skill hits an enemy, it will fully charge Silver Star. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1734.9%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Cloud Flash","d":"When the on-field character is launched, press to activate. Repeatedly slash enemies in front, dealing Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["108.2%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Counter Surge","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Conducting Blow","d":"Press after an Defensive Assist to activate: Dash forward and unleash a series of slashes at enemies ahead, dealing Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["407.1%"]}],"build":{"w":["Severed Innocence","Cordis Germina","The Brimstone","Heartstring Nocturne"],"a":["Shadow Harmony, Branch \u0026 Blade Song","Shadow Harmony, Woodpecker Electro","Shadow Harmony, Astral Voice","Shadow Harmony, Thunder Metal"],"core":7,"st":[["CRIT Rate",68],["CRIT DMG",186],["ATK",3012]]},"how":"Please note, that we have omitted the automatic triggers of Special: White Thunder and Special: Thunder Smite for increased clarity. ORPHIE-TRIGGER TEAM ROTATION: The rotation below is a simple basic S0 Anby rotation when playing with Orphie and Trigger. Requires at least 60 energy and around 60% of Silver Star Mark filled. While this rotation is effective there are optimizations that can be added to increase S0 Anby\u0027s damage further. Trigger Stun with S0 Anby Chain Attack with Trigger (to apply King Of The Summit) Chain Attack Cancel Chain Special Attack: Azure Flash Special Attack: Azure Flash Special Attack: Azure Flash Special Attack: Azure Flash - Boundary Ultimate Special Attack: Azure Flash Special Attack: Azure Flash Special Attack: Azure Flash Special Attack: Azure Flash - Boundary Switch to Orphie Ultimate (Orphie) Quick Assist EX Special Special Attack: Azure Flash Special Attack: Azure Flash Special Attack: Azure Flash Special Attack: Azure Flash - Boundary Double EX Rotation Requires at least 120 energy. While this rotation is effective there are optimizations that can be added to increase S0 Anby\u0027s damage further. Trigger Stun with S0 Anby Chain Attack with Trigger (to apply King Of The Summit) Chain Attack Cancel Chain Ultimate Special Attack: Azure Flash Special Attack: Azure Flash Special Attack: Azure Flash Special Attack: Azure Flash - Boundary EX Special Special Attack: Azure Flash Special Attack: Azure Flash Special Attack: Azure Flash Special Attack: Azure Flash - Boundary EX Special Special Attack: Azure Flash Special Attack: Azure Flash Special Attack: Azure Flash Special Attack: Azure Flash - Boundary DOUBLE CHAIN OPTIMIZED ROTATION The timing for this combo is extremely tight and hard to pull off. This combo will require manual chain and a bit of practice to get down right. Requires 120 Energy and a full Silver Star Mark before Stun. Special Attack: Azure Flash Special Attack: Azure Flash Special Attack: Azure Flash Special Attack: Azure Flash - Boundary (swap-cancel) Trigger Stun with Stunner (ideally with their EX Special to apply King Of The Summit) Chain Attack Cancel Chain Special Attack: Azure Flash (optional; only if 1 Silver Star Mark is present) EX Special (swap-cancel) Trigger Stun with with another character Chain Attack Special Attack: Azure Flash Special Attack: Azure Flash Special Attack: Azure Flash Special Attack: Azure Flash - Boundary Azure Flash - Boundary Ultimate Special Attack: Azure Flash Special Attack: Azure Flash Special Attack: Azure Flash Special Attack: Azure Flash - Boundary EX Special Special Attac","pros":"One of the better Electric DPS Agents in the game; Good baseline performance with strong potential for optimization via optimal Stun combos and Perfect Dodging; Has several different teammate choices that can all perform relatively closely to one another;","cons":"Performance is highly reliant on the ability to execute Dodge Counters; may struggle against enemies that are less aggressive/give less opportunities for this; Likes having at least one inactive Aftershock Agent such as Trigger and Orphie to perform optimally, ideally both at once (Ju Fufu is also an alternative however); Severe lack of viable F2P W-Engine choices, performance can drop sharply without premium options available.","teams":[{"m":"Anby: Soldier 0 + Orphie y Magus + Trigger + Mercury","c":"","r":"Rank 16"},{"m":"Anby: Soldier 0 + Trigger + Astra Yao + Plugboo","c":"","r":"Rank 53"},{"m":"Seed + Anby: Soldier 0 + Trigger + Mercury","c":"","r":"Rank 119"}]},"Ju Fufu":{"slug":"ju-fufu","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Tiger Seven Forms - Flaming Claw","d":"Press to activate: Slash forward up to four times, dealing Physical DMG and Fire DMG. During the 3rd hit, repeatedly press to maintain the combo and keep striking the enemy. During the 3rd hit, hold or pause before pressing to chain into the 4th hit. During the 3rd hit, Anti-Interrupt Level is increased, and DMG received is reduced by 40%.","m":["1st-Hit: 42.5%","2nd-Hit: 45.2%","3rd-Hit: 31.5%","4th-Hit: 218.4%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Hu Wei","d":"During combat, Hu Wei will automatically attack enemies, dealing Fire DMG. Upon hitting an enemy, gain 20 points of Might, triggering up to once per use of a skill. The maximum for Might is 200.","m":["92.4%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Tiger Seven Forms - Mountain-Descending Tiger","d":"Press to activate. Perform a spinning slash forward, followed by a falling slash, dealing Fire DMG. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["66.1%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Tiger Seven Forms Alt - Mountain-Descending Savage Tiger","d":"With enough Energy, press to activate. Swing Hu Wei forward for a powerful strike, dealing massive Fire DMG. Upon activation, gain 3 points of Momentum and 80 points of Might. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["526.5%","Energy Cost: 60%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Tiger Seven Forms - Tigerwind","d":"Press to activate. A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Tiger Seven Forms - Tiger Charge","d":"Press during a dodge to activate: Perform a quick slash forward, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["36.8%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Tiger Seven Forms - Mountain King\u0027s Game","d":"After using Dash Attack: Tiger Seven Forms - Tiger Charge, hold to activate: Enter a high-speed spinning state. While in this state, use the stick/joystick to move and deal Physical DMG upon contact with enemies. After Ju Fufu gains Momentum from other skills, she will be surrounded by flames in the high-speed spinning state. Upon contact with enemies, 1 point of Momentum is consumed, changing the DMG to Fire DMG and granting 25 points of Might. The maximum for Momentum is 15. When dealing Fire DMG, if Might is above 100 points, 100 points of Might will be automatically consumed to trigger Chain Attack: Suppressing Tiger Cauldron. Releasing will have Ju Fufu exit the spinning state and throw Hu Wei to attack enemies. When switching to another character, Ju Fufu will remain in the spinning state and attempt to collide with the nearest enemy. While Ju Fufu is the currently active character, DMG taken during the skill is reduced by 40%, and Anti-Interrupt Level is increased. If not the active character, she becomes Invulnerable.","m":["Mountain King\u0027s Game: 18.4%","Mountain King\u0027s Game - Momentum: 19.2%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Tiger Seven Forms - Reignited Mountain","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Perform multiple slashes on enemies ahead, dealing Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["207.8%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Tiger Cauldron Collapse","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Swing Hu Wei to deliver a powerful strike to enemies in a small area ahead, dealing massive Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["668.1%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Suppressing Tiger Cauldron","d":"With at least 100 points of Might, after triggering a Chain Attack, automatically activate: Consume 100 Might to open Hu Wei and fire flames and popcorn at enemies, striking them in a small area ahead, dealing massive Fire DMG. If Momentum is available, and while not the active character, Fiery Spin will activate after the skill ends. This is an Aftershock. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["354.5%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Tiger Seven Forms - Raging Tiger Explosion","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate. Perform two downward attacks with Hu Wei, dealing massive Fire DMG. Upon activation, gain 6 points of Momentum and 100 points of Might. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1663.8%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Decisive Stomp","d":"When the active character is launched, press to activate. Slashes enemies in front, dealing Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["75.3%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Steadfast Crouching Tiger","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Feral Blazing Maw","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate: Slash forward at enemies, then use Hu Wei to follow up with a downward attack, dealing Fire DMG. Gain 1 point of Momentum upon activation at most once every 10s. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["407.2%"]}],"build":{"w":["Roaring Fur-nace","Hellfire Gears","Precious Fossilized Core","Steam Oven"],"a":["King of the Summit, Astral Voice","King of the Summit, Shockstar Disco","King of the Summit, Woodpecker Electro","King of the Summit, Hormone Punk"],"core":6.99,"st":[["CRIT Rate",56],["CRIT DMG",92],["ATK",3440]]},"how":"$undefined","pros":"Off-field Daze, damage, and buffing — all-in-one; Able to increase the Decibel cap and refund Decibels at no cost; Works in several teams and is the best choice for one of the best DPS currently, Yixuan. Even able to substitute for the high-demand Astra Yao in certain teams; Super easy to play. Just need to manage her resources, other than that works automatically off-field; Buffs are easy to upkeep permanently throughout a whole fight across your whole party; Low dependence on her Signature W-Engine, very budget-friendly; CUTE. Who\u0027s a good tiger?","cons":"Near-impossible to maximize her buffs without her Signature W-Engine. SERIOUSLY good Disc Drives are needed for that; Additionally difficult to ensure the 50% CRIT Rate requirement from King of the Summit while keeping good ATK for her CRIT DMG buff; To further add to her cost problem, all skills are important to level (save for her Dash Attack); While she is highly flexible in terms of teams, it\u0027s only to a certain extent of effectiveness — beyond Yixuan teams, there are always other Agents who outshine her by a good margin. Trigger, Lighter and Astra Yao are the best examples of this.","teams":[{"m":"Yixuan + Ju Fufu + Lucia + Belion","c":"","r":"Rank 11"},{"m":"Pyrois + Ju Fufu + Astra Yao + Snap","c":"","r":"Rank 88"},{"m":"Ye Shunguang + Ju Fufu + Zhao + Sprout","c":"","r":"Rank 101"}]},"Yixuan":{"slug":"yixuan","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Cirrus Strike","d":"Press to activate: Perform up to five attacks forward, dealing Auric Ink DMG. This skill\u0027s Anti-Interrupt Level increases during the 3rd and 4th hit.","m":["1st-Hit: 45.8%","2nd-Hit: 65.5%","3rd-Hit: 87.1%","4th-Hit: 104.8%","5th-Hit: 113.7%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Ink‐Veil Cloud Coalescence","d":"Hold to activate: Deploy a Grand Tai Chi Formation, dealing Auric Ink DMG. When the skill ends, automatically launch the 5th hit of Basic Attack: Cirrus Strike. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill, and DMG received is reduced by 40%.","m":["Ink‐Veil Cloud Coalescence: 234.7%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Auric Array","d":"With Auric Ink Point, activate Dodge: Nimbus Step, then tap , or with Auric Ink Point, hold to activate: Deploy an array, continuously dealing Auric Ink DMG. When the skill ends, it automatically triggers Basic Attack: Qingming Eruption. While channeling, continuously recover Adrenaline, recovering 7/s, for up to 3s. Character is invulnerable while using this skill, and enters the Vital View state.","m":["Auric Array: 305.2%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Qingming Eruption","d":"Automatically activates when Basic Attack: Auric Array reaches the max duration: Spreads her wings to launch an explosive attack, dealing massive Auric Ink DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["110.6%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Shadow-Ignition","d":"Press to activate. Swiftly retreat, then attack forward, dealing Auric Ink DMG. While retreating, a Perfect Dodge can be triggered, but cannot be followed up with a Dodge Counter. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["52.1%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Ink Manifestation","d":"With enough Adrenaline, press or hold to activate. Charge continuously, and release to launch an upward wing attack, dealing massive Auric Ink DMG; While charging, incoming attacks are automatically blocked and will activate the upward wing attack; If hit at the exact moment of activation, it triggers a Perfect Block effect, negating the DMG and increasing the skill\u0027s Interrupt Level to match a Heavy Defensive Assist, and recovering 10 Adrenaline; When an upward wing strike hits an enemy with a red flash or yellow flash, a Perfect Block can be triggered, negating the hit and increasing the skill\u0027s Interrupt Level to match a Heavy Defensive Assist, and recovering 10 Adrenaline; The Perfect Block effect can occur at most once every 0.5s; If charged until flashing or when triggering the Perfect Block effect, the upward wing attack can be followed by an additional Talisman Attack; After using this skill, press to launch [EX Special Attack: Celestial Cloud Blitz - Break]; After [EX Special Attack: Celestial Cloud Blitz - Break], and with enough Adrenaline, press to consume another 20 Adrenaline to launch [EX Special Attack: Qingming Eruption - Break]; After [EX Special Attack: Celestial Cloud Blitz - Break], with enough [Auric Ink Point], hold to quickly chain into [Basic Attack: Auric Array]; Character is invulnerable when activating this skill, and Anti-Interrupt Level is increased while charging.","m":["300.3%","Additional DMG on Full Charge: 149.6%","EX Special Attack: Celestial Cloud Blitz - Break: 370.6%","EX Special Attack: Qingming Eruption - Break: 426.4%","Energy Cost: 40%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Cloud-Shaper","d":"With enough Adrenaline, hold to activate. Continuously charge up, channeling energy around enemies to deal damage over time, up to a max of 2s, dealing massive Auric Ink DMG. Once fully charged or if interrupted, automatically trigger EX Special Attack: Ashen Ink Becomes Shadows. At the moment the skill is activated, a Perfect Dodge can be triggered, and then enter the Vital View state. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["During Charge: 671.8%","Initial Consumption: 20%","Consumption Per Second: 20%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Ashen Ink Becomes Shadows","d":"Triggers automatically during EX Special Attack: Cloud-Shaper: When the energy orb appears and collapses, it deals Auric Ink DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["When Energy Orb Appears/Contracts: 234.3%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Hidden Cloud Technique","d":"Press to activate. A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Skybreaker","d":"Press during a dodge to activate: Launch a dashing attack at enemies in front, dealing Auric Ink DMG.","m":["49.9%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Nimbus Step","d":"When dragging the stick/joystick, hold to activate. Enter a high‐speed Light as Air state. While in the Light as Air state, automatically collect from all resource pickup points within range. While in the Light as Air state, use the stick/joystick to steer. Release the stick/joystick to stop. Character is invulnerable at the moment this skill activates.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Banishing Blow","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Launch a series of attacks on enemies ahead, dealing Auric Ink DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["219.6%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Auric Ink Rush","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Rapidly dash forward and attack, followed by an explosive wing burst, dealing massive Auric Ink DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["533.1%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Qingming Skyshade","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate. Launch a barrage of wing attacks, then guide countless talismans to attack, dealing massive Auric Ink DMG; Upon activating this skill, Yixuan evenly redistributes the squad\u0027s HP; After using this skill, if Auric Ink Point is sufficient, hold to quickly chain into Basic Attack: Auric Array; Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1853.4%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Endless Talisman Suppression","d":"With enough Technique Points, press to activate. Spreads her wings, then guides countless talismans to attack, dealing massive Auric Ink DMG; With both enough Technique Points and Decibels, this skill triggers with priority; After using this skill, if Auric Ink Point is sufficient, hold to quickly chain into [Basic Attack: Auric Array]; Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1466.2%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Cloudstream Shadow","d":"When the active character is launched, press to activate. Launch a series of attacks on enemies ahead, dealing Auric Ink DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["101.2%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Clear Sky Surge","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Celestial Cloud Blitz","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate: Quickly dash forward and attack, dealing Auric Ink DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["297%"]}],"build":{"w":["Qingming Birdcage","Cauldron of Clarity","Puzzle Sphere","Steel Cushion"],"a":["Yunkui Tales, Branch \u0026 Blade Song","Yunkui Tales, Woodpecker Electro","Yunkui Tales, Chaotic Metal","Yunkui Tales, Shining Aria"],"core":7,"st":[["CRIT Rate",57],["CRIT DMG",163],["ATK",2133]]},"how":"Yixuan can be quite demanding of field time, as she wants to be actively hitting enemies for more Adrenaline generation and then wants to be spending said Adrenaline to build up to her Technique Points before every stun period, but not to the point where she has none for her burst. Her damage multipliers on EX Specials are very high, but which to use when is important to be mindful of. EX Special Attack: Cloud-Shaper is best reserved for the in-stun period, as for out of stun, using EX Special Attack: Ink Manifestation is the priority - ideally only when enemies are attacking so as to successfully counter them and get the partial Adrenaline refund. Then transition into Celestial Cloud Blitz - Break, and Qingming Eruption - Break for the highest damage:Adrenaline spend ratio. When there is no Adrenaline available, make use of her Dodge Counters for the 5 Adrenaline generation that she gets on Perfect Dodges from her Core Passive. It’s important to balance out Yixuan’s resource generation with other characters in the team. As her Additional Ability generates 5 Adrenaline when being swapped out via a Perfect Assist, make use of Evasive and Defensive Assists to still build Adrenaline, get Decibels and give your Stunners the opportunity to apply daze. As stun approaches, be mindful so as not to be low on Adrenaline, with at least 90 - 100 in stock being a good base, but the more the better. To get Yixuan’s best combo, one needs to master a “Chain Trigger Tech”. This involves getting a Chain Attack window to trigger halfway through a move that’d normally be swap locked, namely Ultimate: Endless Talisman Suppression. For it, hold Basic Attack to get EX Special Attack: Cloud-Shaper, then after a short while, release and then use the Ultimate. Doing so with the right timing will cause the EX Special Attack: Ashen Ink Becomes Shadow explosion to land after the Ultimate cutscene, allowing for Yixuan to be swapped out of during the Ultimate animation. That way, it’s possible to get other characters’ Chain Attacks without wasting any time. Too early and Yixuan won’t cast Ashen Ink, leading to no trigger, but too late and it will trigger before the Ultimate begins. Regardless of whether or not you are able to perform this tech, the combo shell remains the same: Cloud-Shaper Ultimate: Endless Talisman Suppression (Chain Trigger Tech) Chain Attack to a Stunner for King of the Summit Chain Attack to Yixuan Ultimate: Qingming Skyshade Auric Array (optional, do not use if Adrenaline is required for later in the run) Cloud-Shaper Cloud-Shaper If you aren’t able to perform t","pros":"Massive Sheer DMG potential, one of the highest in the game; HP Scaling Agent, which means really high HP to tank enemy attacks, on top of her Ultimate redistributing HP evenly between teammates to ensure survivability; Unique element with unique kit mechanics and several ways to optimize her playstyle — has a lot of depth to the way you can play her with many combos available, her playstyle is highly flexible; Easy to chase moving targets thanks to her enhanced movement capabilities; Her Ultimate animations though…","cons":"Reliant on specific key Agents who complement her kit perfectly — has trouble finding viable alternatives due to scaling primarily off of HP, wanting to stay on the field and ignoring DEF/PEN/Energy Regen-related stats; Enjoys being able to respond to enemy mechanics to trigger Perfect Blocks, Assists, and Dodges. The less aggressive the enemy is, the worse she becomes; How will Hoyoverse top off her Ultimate animations?","teams":[{"m":"Yixuan + Dialyn + Lucia + Belion","c":"","r":"Rank 7"},{"m":"Yixuan + Ju Fufu + Lucia + Belion","c":"","r":"Rank 11"},{"m":"Yixuan + Norma + Lucia + Belion","c":"","r":"Rank 36"}]},"Promeia":{"slug":"promeia","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Sweeping Edge","d":"Press to activate: Performs up to five attacks against enemies ahead, dealing Ice DMG. After landing the fifth hit\u0027s downward attack, and with sufficient Trial by Cold, keep holding or to chain into EX Special Attack: Execution - Merciless Judgment. Enters the Bound Absolution state after throwing the cape during the fourth hit.","m":["1st-Hit: 49.8%","2nd-Hit: 103.2%","3rd-Hit: 190.9%","4th-Hit: 204.7%","5th-Hit: 241.5%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Whirling Blade","d":"Hold to activate: Promeia leaps into the air and attacks, throwing her cape beside the enemy and entering the Bound Absolution state, dealing Ice DMG. Hitting enemies does not accumulate Corrosive Chill.","m":["175.5%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Bound Absolution","d":"When using certain skills, Promeia throws her cape to continuously slice enemies, dealing Ice DMG. Does not accumulate Corrosive Chill upon hit. While the cape remains out, Promeia can walk slowly. Press during this period to immediately follow up with the 5th hit of Basic Attack: Sweeping Edge. If attacked during this period, Promeia triggers a Perfect Dodge automatically. The dodge can trigger once every 20s.","m":[]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Execution - Cold Flash","d":"Press to activate. Launches a flying blade attack, dealing Ice DMG.","m":["127.8%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Execution - Glacial Death","d":"With enough Energy, press to activate. Performs a flying blade attack, throwing her cape beside the enemy and entering the Bound Absolution state, dealing Ice DMG. If attacked by an enemy shortly after using the move, automatically chains into EX Special Attack: Execution - Shrouded in Shadow. Upon use, Promeia gains the Absolute Order effect. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["79.3%","Energy Cost: 40%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Execution - Descending Frost","d":"While under the Absolute Order effect, press or while in the Bound Absolution state to activate: Leaps toward the enemy, retrieving the cape while performing a descending attack that deals Ice DMG. After landing, if Promeia possesses Trial by Cold, keep holding or to chain into EX Special Attack: Execution - Merciless Judgment. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["383.8%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Execution - Layered Frost","d":"After triggering EX Special Attack: Execution - Shrouded in Shadow, press or to activate: Quickly launches a flurry of attacks, then leaps toward the enemy, retrieving the cape while performing a more powerful downward attack that deals Ice DMG. After landing, if Promeia possesses Trial by Cold, keep holding or to chain into EX Special Attack: Execution - Merciless Judgment. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["608.2%","Blade Slash Total DMG Multiplier: 12.1%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Execution - Merciless Judgment","d":"With enough Trial by Cold and after performing the final hit of Basic Attack: Sweeping Edge, Special Attack: Execution - Descending Frost, or Special Attack: Execution - Layered Frost, keep holding or after landing to activate: Quickly leaps back while unleashing a more powerful finishing move, dealing Ice DMG. Hitting enemies does not accumulate Corrosive Chill. After using this skill, hold or , or press to immediately follow up with the 5th hit of Basic Attack: Sweeping Edge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["512.3%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Veiled Step","d":"Press to activate. A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Grim Reap","d":"Press during a dodge to activate: Delivers a quick attack forward, dealing Ice DMG.","m":["56.3%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Soaring Bat","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Unleashes consecutive attacks against the target, dealing Ice DMG. After using this skill, it can be immediately followed up with the 5th hit of Basic Attack: Sweeping Edge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["335.7%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Hanging Judgment","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Throws flying blades and hangs upside down above the enemy, unleashing a flurry of attacks and ending with a finishing move, dealing massive Ice DMG. When the heavy attack hits an enemy afflicted with Ice Anomaly, Ether Anomaly, Electric Anomaly, Fire Anomaly, Physical Anomaly, or Wind Anomaly, it triggers Abloom once, dealing 100% Attribute Anomaly DMG of the corresponding attribute. After using this skill, it can be immediately followed up with the 5th hit of Basic Attack: Sweeping Edge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["830.8%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Glaciating Impalement","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate: Launches a series of forward attacks, dealing massive Ice DMG. When the heavy attack hits an enemy afflicted with Ice Anomaly, Ether Anomaly, Electric Anomaly, Fire Anomaly, Physical Anomaly, or Wind Anomaly, it triggers Abloom once, dealing 250% Attribute Anomaly DMG of the corresponding attribute. After using this skill, it can be immediately followed up with the 5th hit of Basic Attack: Sweeping Edge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1538.4%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Ambushing Strike","d":"When the active character is launched, press to activate. Unleashes consecutive attacks against the target, dealing Ice DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["79.1%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Injunction","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Intercepting Strike","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate: Unleashes consecutive attacks against the target, dealing Ice DMG. After using this skill, it can be immediately followed up with the 5th hit of Basic Attack: Sweeping Edge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["469%"]}],"build":{"w":["Frostfall Sickle","Fusion Compiler","Weeping Gemini","Electro-Lip Gloss"],"a":["Notes From the Chained, Phaethon\u0027s Melody","Notes From the Chained, Flex","Notes From the Chained, Freedom Blues","Notes From the Chained, Hormone Punk"],"core":7,"st":[["CRIT Rate",12],["CRIT DMG",63],["ATK",2625]]},"how":"Promeia’s gameplan mostly amounts to: Stay on her as the active character and keep using her regular Basic Attack string to build Anomaly and her Corrosive Chill gauge. Use an EX early, so that she can activate her Additional Ability (and possibly W-Engine) buffs. Make use of as many Dodge Counters into Basic 5s as possible so as to quickly build resources. Use her Abloom EX to dish out as much damage as possible, making sure to have enough for critical burst periods (like Stun or when enemies are debuffed). Different team compositions will have different priorities. Those running Stunners may struggle to generate enough Corrosive Chill for every Stun, so making use of Assist Counters to balance her own gauge and Daze is important. Double Anomaly teams are going to be using Ablooms out-of-stun often, so try to make sure that they’re only being used on Anomalies applied by the most buffed/strongest Agents to not lose out on Abloom DMG from snapshotting weaker units. As she gets a large amount of Decibels, Ultimates are used frequently, but attempting to align them can be important for certain combos, as the high Ice Anomaly Build-up it provides can be a way to avoid having to spend time and/or Ablooms on a weak Anomaly after a Disorder, making for a fast way to re-apply Ice. It’s also a great skill to Freeze enemies (or break them out of it quickly!), which can be a big boon against certain enemies. The Frost Oath point it provides can also be used for fast Anomaly application when it matters. Be watchful of resources, as Promeia would much rather go into her Abloom EX through a regular EX start than her hold Basic. Given that her EXs are only really useful as a means to get her Ablooming, there isn’t much of a need to spend them outside of burst periods. Even the counter EX isn’t all that great to use, as Promeia would get far more resources from her Dodge Counters, so it can be safely avoided unless the high Build-up from her alternate enhanced Special is needed. These can then be used in combos to get her fast burst after other Agents’ Chain Attacks. While Promeia’s isn’t bad, it’s usually better to spend it on others for Anomaly (yielding more Disorders) or resources (e.g. Decibels, as Promeia often has plenty), but can still see use. As is the case for most Anomaly Agents, her exact combos are dependent on her gearing - like Anomaly Mastery W-Engines or those with Build-up Rate buffs - as well as her team as a whole. For reference though, here’s a sample combo with Vivian and Yuzuha, using all Signatures, on an Ice + Ether weak enemy: Promeia needs a","pros":"Very strong numbers generally, with high Anomaly build-up setting her up to do well with Wind and readily accessible burst making her good both in and out-of-stun. Her teamwide Abloom buffs gives her varied team options and has her function as both a main-DPS and pseudo-support, uplifting other units. Accessible build options, with competitive W-Engine alternatives and lack of saturation making stat picks and distribution less important than her peers. Aura farm, the character.","cons":"Few fights in which she’s useful for, with Ice Anomaly being heavily anti-shilled and half DEF bosses becoming more common. Reliant on teammates for resource generation (Disorder and Ablooms especially), leading to large performance swings depending on the comp. Said resources can be difficult to manage, with lopsided Decibel generation and her Corrosive Chill being especially scarce in comps where stuns come quickly. The coolest animations are the ones you’ll never use.","teams":[{"m":"nangong-yu + ukinami-yuzuha, sunna","c":"","r":""},{"m":"vivian + ukinami-yuzuha, sunna","c":"","r":""},{"m":"lycaon + ukinami-yuzuha, astra-yao, sunna, nicole-demara","c":"","r":""}]},"Alice":{"slug":"alice","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Celestial Overture","d":"Press to activate: Perform up to 5 slashes forward, dealing Physical DMG. When Alice triggers Assault through Attribute Anomaly Buildup, the 5th hit of her next Basic Attack is enhanced.","m":["1st-Hit: 55.1%","2nd-Hit: 88%","3rd-Hit: 66.1%","4th-Hit: 111.9%","5th-Hit: 130.3%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Starshine Waltz","d":"When Alice\u0027s Blade Etiquette reaches 1 bar, hold to activate: Hold to charge, expending up to 3 bars of Blade Etiquette. Release or when Blade Etiquette is below 1 bar, Alice performs a series of slashes in an area centered on the target enemy, with the number of hits determined by charge level, dealing massive Physical DMG. When the Finishing Move of a three-stage charged Basic Attack: Starshine Waltz hits, it triggers a special Assault effect: Polarized Assault. This deals DMG equal to 100.0% of the original Assault, ignoring Anomaly Buildup, and can interact with other Attribute Anomalies, including Physical, to trigger Disorder. Blade Etiquette does not accumulate when hitting an enemy. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["One-Staged Charged Attack: 118.9%","Two-Staged Charged Attack: 304.4%","Three-Staged Charged Attack: 965.7%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Piercing Dawn","d":"Press to activate. Hurl the blade to strike and pass through enemies ahead, dealing Physical DMG. Upon activating this skill, a Perfect Dodge can be triggered. After triggering a Perfect Dodge, press to follow up with the 5th hit of a Basic Attack. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["62.4%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Aurora Thrust - Northern Cross","d":"With enough energy, drag the stick/joystick forward and press to activate. A thrust attack that goes through enemies ahead, dealing massive Physical DMG. Activating the skill can trigger Perfect Dodge and restores 10 Blade Etiquette. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["460%","Energy Cost: 40%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Aurora Thrust - Southern Cross","d":"With enough energy, and without moving the stick/joystick or when dragging it backwards, press to activate. Back away with a slash, then thrust forward, dealing Physical DMG. Activating the skill can trigger Perfect Dodge and restores 10 Blade Etiquette. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["532%","Energy Cost: 40%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Jumpy Bunny","d":"Press to activate. A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Blade-Dancer\u0027s Gale","d":"Press during a dodge to activate: Slashes enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["75.3%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Ceremony of Swordlight","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Slash and kick enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["284%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Starfall Intermission","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Unleashes powerful consecutive slashes at enemies ahead, dealing massive Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["666.3%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Starfall Finale","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate. Unleashes powerful slashes at enemies in a large area ahead, dealing massive Physical DMG. Activating this skill restores 200 Blade Etiquette. Blade Etiquette does not accumulate when hitting an enemy. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["2262%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Intertwined Stab","d":"When the active character is launched, press to activate. Slash and kick enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["163.3%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Parry Guard","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Cross Riposte","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate: SCharge forward and slash enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["332.7%"]}],"build":{"w":["Practiced Perfection","Weeping Gemini","Sharpened Stinger","Fusion Compiler"],"a":["Fanged Metal, Phaethon\u0027s Melody","Fanged Metal, Freedom Blues","Fanged Metal, Chaos Jazz","Fanged Metal, Puffer Electro"],"core":7,"st":[["CRIT Rate",13],["CRIT DMG",65],["ATK",3024]]},"how":"Rotations Alice\u0027s gameplay and mechanics are including simple, stack up Blade Etiquette via her most efficient skills in order to execute maxed out charged Basic Attacks to deal massive amounts of AoE damage. The best path to acheive this is executing combos that branch to her Basic Attack 5, which is her strongest accessible ability for Anomaly Application and Blade Etiquette generation, this fact forms the backbone of her combos. Note this Basic 5 can be enhanced by triggering Assault at any point, but this does not affect her combos — in fact, it only makes them stronger.The skills Alice can use that allow her to follow up immediately with her Basic Attack 5 are as follows: Both EX Specials; Quick Assist; Dodge Counter; Assist Follow-Up; Chain Attack; Special (when a Perfect Dodge is triggered from it). All of these attacks, save for her Special (unless Fusion Compiler is her W-Engine), serve practical use in her rotations — just make sure to use Basic Attack 5 after each and every single one of them.It is also worth noting that both of her EX Specials can and should be used to trigger Perfect Dodges whenever possible to restore extra Blade Etiquette for Alice. Additionally, her Charged Basic Attack has a lengthy animation very similar to Miyabi\u0027s, hence it\u0027s similarly worthwhile to Swap Cancel out of it in order to maximize team damage output.One last tip — if you really wish to optimize, Alice\u0027s Enhanced Basic Attack 5 and EX Specials also have lengthy animations. As a result, it\u0027s worthwhile to Swap Cancel them as well, but it\u0027s not as important as her Charged Basic Attack. Incorporate what you\u0027re comfortable with in her rotations in order to deal optimal damage.Some staple combos can look like this: Standard out of Stun combo Quick Assist Basic Attack 5 EX Special (optionally Swap Cancel) Basic Attack 5 EX Special (optionally Swap Cancel) Basic Attack 5 Charged Basic Attack Level 3 (Swap Cancel) The above combo has so many invincibility frames it\u0027s nearly impossible to get hit while executing it. Note that it\u0027s possible to start this combo off with a Dodge Counter or Special (with Perfect Dodge) without spending any extra resources. Ultimately, take the rotation described above as a concept, much less a must-execute sequence of attacks. Max Resource Combo Unlike other characters Alices access to her main resource Blade Etiquette is inconsistant due to a portion of it coming from anomaly/disorder triggers which vary based on team, gameplay and enemies. Because of this only treat the following burst rotations as examples.This combo is particularly u","pros":"High, super easy-to-access Physical Anomaly damage with tons of invincibility on her attacks; Flexible team options - has many viable alternatives; Good Disk Drive flexibility, will be very easy to build for people who already built Jane/Piper; Basically a physical version of Miyabi, familiar playstyle and similar strengths (even though she doesn\u0027t quite pack as much of a punch).","cons":"High reliance on her Signature W-Engine to really be above Jane and Piper\u0027s damage level; Will be easily spooked by most enemies in battle, which is totally affecting her combat performance (it\u0027s not). Sorry Alice, but we have to put you through this…","teams":[{"m":"Remielle + Alice + Velina + Ariel","c":"","r":"Rank 27"},{"m":"Remielle + Alice + Jane Doe + Ariel","c":"","r":"Rank 69"},{"m":"Alice + Jane Doe + Yuzuha + Miss Esme","c":"","r":"Rank 76"}]},"Evelyn":{"slug":"evelyn","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Razor Wire","d":"Press to activate: Launch up to five attacks ahead, dealing Physical DMG and Fire DMG. When the 5th hit lands against an enemy, Evelyn will use her Lunalux Garrote to bind the primary target and enter Binding Seal.","m":["1st-Hit: 51.2%","2nd-Hit: 62.1%","3rd-Hit: 78.2%","4th-Hit: 186.7%","5th-Hit: 223.4%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Passive: Bind","d":"When Evelyn uses her skills to deal DMG to enemies, she will accumulate Burning Embers. When Evelyn consumes Burning Embers to activate Garrote or consumes Decibels to perform an Ultimate, she gains 1 Burning Tether Point. Once Evelyn has 3 Burning Tether Points, her next use of Garrote will consume all Burning Tether Points to instead use a lower Interrupt Level version of Chain Attack: Lunalux - Snare.","m":[]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Garrote - First Form","d":"When Burning Embers is at 50% or higher, hold or to activate: Consume 50% Burning Embers to use Lunalux Garrote to perform a slashing attack, dealing Fire DMG. During skill activation, Anti-Interrupt level increases, and DMG taken is reduced by 40%. After using this skill, gain 1 Burning Tether Point.","m":["226.4%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Garrote - Second Form","d":"When Burning Embers is 50% or higher, after using Basic Attack: Garrote - First Form, continue to hold or to activate: Consume 50% Burning Embers to use Lunalux Garrote to perform a follow-up attack, dealing Fire DMG. During skill activation, Anti-Interrupt level increases, and DMG taken is reduced by 40%. After using this skill, gain 1 Burning Tether Point.","m":["245.2%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Locked Position","d":"Before entering Binding Seal, press to activate. Use Lunalux Garrote to pull the enemy and charge forward with a kick, dealing Fire DMG. When the attack hits the enemy, Evelyn will use Lunalux Garrote to bind the primary target and enter Binding Seal. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["1st-Hit: 52.3%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Binding Sunder - First Form","d":"After entering Binding Seal, press or hold to activate: Centered on the target affected by Binding Seal, tether surrounding enemies and detonate an explosion, dealing Fire DMG. Binding Seal will end after detonation. Dodge enemy attacks upon activating the skill, and if a Perfect Dodge is triggered, gain an additional 25% Burning Embers. After tethering surrounding enemies, press to cancel detonation and immediately follow up with the Basic Attack\u0027s 3rd hit. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["Bind DMG: 40.4%","Explosion DMG: 34%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Binding Sunder - Final Form","d":"After entering Binding Seal and with enough Energy, press or hold to activate: Centered on the target affected by Binding Seal, tether surrounding enemies and detonate an explosion, dealing massive Fire DMG. Binding Seal will end after detonation. Dodge enemy attacks upon activating the skill, and if a Perfect Dodge is triggered, gain an additional 25% Burning Embers. After pulling in surrounding enemies, press to cancel detonation and immediately follow up with the Basic Attack\u0027s 3rd hit. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Bind DMG: 541.2%","Explosion DMG: 59.6%","Energy Cost: 60%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Arc Step","d":"Press to activate. A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Piercing Ambush","d":"Press during a dodge to activate: Deliver a kick to the enemy in front, causing Physical DMG.","m":["60.5%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Strangling Reversal","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Use Lunalux Garrote to slash surrounding enemies, dealing Fire DMG; When the attack hits an enemy, Evelyn will use Lunalux Garrote to bind the primary target and enter Binding Seal. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["210.2%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Lunalux - Snare\"","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Evelyn slashes in front with multiple Lunalux Garrotes and detonates an explosion, dealing massive Fire DMG to enemies in the area. When the attack hits an enemy, Evelyn uses Lunalux Garrote to bind the primary target and enters Binding Seal. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["829.3%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Lunalux Garrote - Timbre","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate. Evelyn slashes in front with multiple Lunalux Garrotes and detonates an explosion, dealing massive Fire DMG to enemies in the area. Upon activating this skill, Evelyn removes her jacket and enters the Dance of Awakened Fire state, which lasts for the entire battle. While in the Dance of Awakened Fire state, when Evelyn consumes Burning Tether Points to activate Chain Attack: Lunalux - Snare, she will retain 1 point of Burning Tether Point. When the attack hits an enemy, Evelyn uses Lunalux Garrote to bind the primary target, entering Binding Seal. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. After using this skill, gain 1 Burning Tether Point.","m":["1988.5%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Lunalux Garrote - Shadow","d":"While under the Dance of Awakened Fire state, and when Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate. Evelyn slashes in front with multiple Lunalux Garrotes and detonates an explosion, dealing massive Fire DMG to enemies in the area. When the attack hits an enemy, Evelyn uses Lunalux Garrote to bind the primary target and enters Binding Seal. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. After using this skill, gain 1 Burning Tether Point.","m":["1988.5%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Fierce Blade","d":"When the on-field character is launched, press to activate. Use Lunalux Garrote to slash surrounding enemies, dealing Fire DMG. When the attack hits an enemy, Evelyn will use Lunalux Garrote to bind the primary target and enter Binding Seal. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["77.1%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Silent Protection","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Course Disruption","d":"Press after an Defensive Assist to activate: Evelyn slashes with Lunalux Garrote, then triggers an explosion ahead, dealing Fire DMG. When the attack hits an enemy, Evelyn will use Lunalux Garrote to bind the primary target and enter Binding Seal. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["291.6%"]}],"build":{"w":["Heartstring Nocturne","Marcato Desire","The Brimstone","Cordis Germina"],"a":["Woodpecker Electro, Branch \u0026 Blade Song","Astral Voice, Branch \u0026 Blade Song","Puffer Electro, Branch \u0026 Blade Song","Hormone Punk, Branch \u0026 Blade Song"],"core":7,"st":[["CRIT Rate",75],["CRIT DMG",165],["ATK",3049]]},"how":"Evelyn is a character who likes to on-field, not because she does much damage while doing so, but because she needs it to generate her resources. Being stocked on both 3 Burning Tether Points and 16 Burning Embers prior to a stun is often required for her most damaging combos and should be considered a priority. On paper it’s simple: use her Special Attack: Locked Position to apply binding seal, then follow with Special Attack: Binding Sunder - First Form. This allows her to bypass the weak, Physical DMG 1st and 2nd hits of her Basic Attack string and get onto the stronger and higher Burning Ember generating moves faster. From there, simply continue to use her Basic Attack string until the 5th hit, then again cast Special Attack: Binding Sunder - First Form and repeat. Be mindful so as to not overcap Burning Embers and use Evelyn’s enhanced Basic Attack: Garrote to convert them to Burning Tether Points every so often. It’s not uncommon to just about hit the Energy threshold for EX Special Attack: Binding Sunder - Final Form, so make sure to not waste any of its build-up. In practice, it’s unlikely that enemies will stand still and allow for uninterrupted use of all these Basic Attacks. This is not a negative however, as it provides an opportunity to gain additional Burning Embers through the Perfect Dodge properties of Evelyn’s Special and EX Special. The more aggressive the enemy, the faster Burning Embers can be built, so do capitalise on attacks to maximise its generation. Depending on how quickly her resources are built, it may allow for one out of stun Burning Tether Points Chain Attack to be used. This can do some decent damage but it’s primary purpose would be to generate Decibels, as Evelyn is more than capable of sustaining Ultimate use in every stun bar certain routes (e.g. 5 stuns on element neutral). Despite Evelyn’s demanding field presence, this does not detract much from her teams’ abilities to stun quickly, as it provides opportunities to Defensive Assist onto Stunners for daze build and Decibel generation. As her Assist Follow-Up is not particularly strong, this is an effective use of Assist Points, however do be mindful as it can make Decibel build more reliant on using out of stun Chain Attacks. Once stun arrives, that’s where Evelyn shines. She has some of the highest combo damage multipliers in the game, getting a truly absurd amount of Chain Attacks out in a short period. Her best combos however, are conditional on having specific teammates that can extend the stun duration (Lighter or Dialyn) as well as Astra, who is able to provid","pros":"Not only has a great \u0027floor\u0027 when it comes to her damage output but also a great \u0027ceiling\u0027 for those who want to master her harder rotations, Can group enemies, which is rare for a DPS, Her playstyle is very rewarding for those who like combo-based gameplay.","cons":"W-Engine options outside of her Signature are pretty underwhelming, Her best teammates are both limited characters (Astra Yao and Lighter) and the free alternatives are, well, worse.","teams":[{"m":"Evelyn + Norma + Astra Yao + Snap","c":"","r":"Rank 83"},{"m":"Evelyn + Dialyn + Astra Yao + Snap","c":"","r":"Rank 91"},{"m":"Evelyn + Lighter + Astra Yao + Snap","c":"","r":"Rank 103"}]},"Pan Yinhu":{"slug":"pan-yinhu","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Unyielding Strikes","d":"Press to activate: Launches up to four consecutive melee attacks, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["1st-Hit: 49.7%","2nd-Hit: 49.8%","3rd-Hit: 109.4%","4th-Hit: 211.3%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Sonic Pressure-Point Strike","d":"Press to activate. Delivers a forward melee technique while tossing firecrackers, dealing Physical DMG. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["62.5%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Touch of Death","d":"With Break Force, press to activate. Special Attack: Touch of Death attacks centered on the enemy, dealing Physical DMG. The skill can be chained up to three times. Each use of Special Attack: Touch of Death consumes 1 point of Break Force. When Pan Yinhu is the active Agent, DMG received during the skill is reduced by 60% and Anti-Interrupt Level is increased. If he isn\u0027t the active Agent, he becomes Invulnerable.","m":["384.1%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Mountainous Pulse Strike","d":"With enough Energy, press to activate. EX Special Attack: Mountainous Pulse Strike unleashes a powerful strike forward, dealing Physical DMG. Gain 3 points of Break Force on activation. Upon hitting an enemy, it triggers the Quick Assist of the previous character in the squad. Agents who enter the field via this Quick Assist will gain the Sheer Force bonus from the Core Passive. After switching out, Pan Yinhu will stay on the field and automatically launch Special Attack: Touch of Death until his Break Force runs out, where he then leaves the field. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1st-Hit: 97.3%","2nd-Hit: 97.3%","3rd-Hit: 97.3%","Energy Cost: 60%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Light as a Swallow","d":"Press to activate. A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Sizzling Oil Supreme","d":"Press during a dodge to activate: Perform a quick forward melee attack, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["83.4%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Moving Mountains and Seas","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Perform a melee attack on enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["219.2%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Anointed with Wok Steam","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Hop onto the Iron Wok and spin rapidly to ram into enemies, dealing massive Physical DMG to all enemies on the way.","m":["632.3%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: A Feast Fit for an Emperor!","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate. Perform a technique that compresses qi into fried rice and catapults it at foes, dealing massive Physical DMG and healing the whole squad for some HP, while also applying a 8s heal over time on Agents, recovering certain HP/s. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1627.9%","Heal (Flat): 160%","HoT (HP%): 0.9%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Lift Your Gaze to Good Fortune","d":"When the active character is launched, press to activate. Perform a melee attack on enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["91.7%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Intimidating Presence","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. This skill excels at parrying enemy attacks and reduces the consumption of Assist Points when the character is under intense attacks. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Ride the Momentum","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate: Perform a melee attack on enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["337.4%"]}],"build":{"w":["Tremor Trigram Vessel","Tusks of Fury","Peacekeeper - Specialized","Reel Projector"],"a":["Astral Voice, Swing Jazz","Bunny in Wonderland, Swing Jazz","Astral Voice, Moonlight Lullaby","Bunny in Wonderland, Moonlight Lullaby"],"core":7,"st":[["CRIT Rate",28],["CRIT DMG",77],["ATK",3048]]},"how":"Rotations Pan Yinhu\u0027s rotations are extremely simple in design. He only wants to activate a few of his key abilities when available at specific intervals. His gameplay can be summed up to the following steps: Use EX Special to buff the Sheer Force of the previous character in the squad by triggering a Quick Assist (ideally a Rupture damage dealer) every 25s; Use 1 Touch of Death to increase the DMG taken by enemies every 10s (can be done 3 times with EX Special); Use Ultimate if teammates need healing or when readily available. With Yixuan as his DPS to support, ensure you execute Defensive Assists to switch into Pan Yinhu to feed Adrenaline to Yixuan and generate extra Daze.Additional Note: Make sure Pan Yinhu is always the party member following the DPS he is supporting, so that he can Quick Assist into them with his EX Special and provide his Sheer Force boost properly.","pros":"Extremely simple plug-and-play Support Agent — anyone can pick him up. Basically the equivalent of Lucy for Sheer Force-scaling Agents, with very low field time and effective buffs; The only Sheer Force buffer at the time of his release, a unique and valuable role; Rare presence of healing in his kit which helps with party survivability; Very low-cost Agent who needs little resources investment-wise aside from his ATK requirement; Scales well with Mindscapes while retaining his functionality at a baseline.","cons":"Only usable with Rupture Agents — very specialized character (excels in his niche but doesn\u0027t have the generalist potential of Agents like Nicole/Lucy); Must be placed before the DPS Agent in the party which can make some team options awkward (with characters like Trigger); Has a scarce amount of effective W-Engine options.","teams":[{"m":"Yixuan + Lucia + Pan Yinhu + Belion","c":"","r":"Rank 66"},{"m":"Billy - Starlight + Dialyn + Pan Yinhu + Birkblick","c":"","r":"Rank 230"},{"m":"Yixuan + Ju Fufu + Pan Yinhu + Belion","c":"","r":"Rank 280"}]},"Harumasa":{"slug":"harumasa","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Cloud Piercer","d":"Press or hold to activate: Launch up to five piercing attacks ahead, dealing Physical DMG and Electric DMG. When the 5th hit of the Basic Attack hits an enemy, it generates 2 Electro Quivers. After activating a Chain Attack, the next time Harumasa activates the 5th hit of Basic Attack: Cloud Piercer and hits an enemy with it, it generates 6 Electro Quivers.","m":["1st-Hit: 42.4%","2nd-Hit: 39.8%","3rd-Hit: 70.9%","4th-Hit: 90.1%","5th-Hit: 132.9%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Cloud Piercer - Drift","d":"During Basic Attack: Cloud Piercer, drag the stick/joystick and press to activate: Shoot a ranged piercing attack and reposition towards the corresponding drag direction, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["69.5%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Falling Feather","d":"After the 5th hit of Basic Attack: Cloud Piercer, a Special Attack, an EX Special Attack, or a Chain Attack, hold to activate: Immediately shoot Falling Feather at enemies ahead, dealing Electric DMG. Hold to aim at a target and release to activate: After drawing the bowstring and aiming, shoot Falling Feather at the target, dealing Electric DMG.","m":["105.4%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Ha-Oto no Ya","d":"When the 5th hit of Basic Attack: Cloud Piercer/EX Special Attack/Chain Attack hits an enemy or the ground, it can generate 2/6/6 Electro Quivers. If there are no Electro Quivers on the field when any squad member applies an Attribute Anomaly to an enemy, generate 6 Electro Quivers. This effect can trigger once every 12s. There can be up to 6 Electro Quivers present at a time. If there are any Electro Quivers present when Harumasa fires and hits enemies with Falling Feather, the Electro Quivers will activate and fire Ha-Oto no Ya at the enemies hit by Falling Feather, dealing Electric DMG. Ha-Oto no Ya will apply Electro Prison to enemies hit, stacking up to 8 times and lasting 10s, repeated triggers reset the duration. While a target has at least 2 stacks of Electro Prison, they will be X-Marked.","m":["15.9%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Nowhere to Hide","d":"Press to activate. Launch an arrow forward, dealing Electric DMG. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["52.3%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Nowhere to Run","d":"With enough energy, press to activate: Launch daggers and an enhanced arrow ahead, dealing massive Electric DMG. When the enhanced arrow hits an enemy or the ground, it generates 6 Electro Quivers. Character is invulnerable while using this skill","m":["449.3%","Energy Cost: 60%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Quick Flash","d":"Press to activate. A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Hiten no Tsuru","d":"Press during a dodge to activate: Launch multiple piercing attacks ahead, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["80.7%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Hidden Edge","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Pierces enemies in front, dealing Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["219.6%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Hiten no Tsuru - Slash","d":"While there are X-Marked enemies on the field, Harumasa will enter the Awakened state, switching Dash Attack: Hiten no Tsuru for Dash Attack: Hiten no Tsuru - Slash. While in the Awakened state, press during a dodge to activate: Rush forwards to the closest X-Marked enemy and execute a powerful slash, dealing Electric DMG. When the slash hits the target, it consumes 2 stacks of Electro Prison. With less than 2 stacks of Electro Prison, X-Marked will be removed from the enemy. Before X-Marked is removed, repeatedly press to repeatedly use Dash Attack: Hiten no Tsuru - Slash. While no X-Marked enemies exist on the field, Harumasa leaves the Awakened state. While in the Awakened state, press after Basic Attack: Falling Featherto quickly follow up with Dash Attack: Hiten no Tsuru - Slash. During skill activation, Anti-Interrupt level increases, and DMG taken is reduced by 40%.","m":["1st-Hit: 162.3%","2nd-Hit: 166.6%","3rd-Hit: 189.6%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Kai - Hanare","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Unleash a piercing attack on enemies in a large area ahead then fire an enhanced arrow, dealing massive Electric DMG. When the arrow hits the ground, it generates 6 Electro Quivers. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["517.6%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Zanshin","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate. Unleash a piercing attack on enemies in a large area ahead, dealing massive Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1953.9%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Braced Bow","d":"When the on-field character is launched, press to activate. Unleash a piercing attack at enemies ahead, dealing Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["84.3%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Yugamae","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Yugamae - Slash","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate: Unleash a series of slashes at enemies ahead, dealing Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["307.1%"]}],"build":{"w":["Zanshin Herb Case","The Brimstone","Cordis Germina","Severed Innocence"],"a":["Shadow Harmony, Branch \u0026 Blade Song","Shadow Harmony, Puffer Electro","Shadow Harmony, Astral Voice","Shadow Harmony, Woodpecker Electro"],"core":7,"st":[["CRIT Rate",52],["CRIT DMG",186],["ATK",3287]]},"how":"Harumasa’s difficulty comes not from the complexity of his kit, but how to best route fights with him and in having the skill to perfectly time attacks to maximise his damage. There is no clear cut way to play him, as each encounter demands its own adjustments, where trying to get Anomalies to trigger at specific points is a significant value add. If using Thunder Metal, this is doubly important, as Shock timings are needed not only for Quiver generation, but for Combat ATK buffs too. To start with, using Cloud Piercer 3 times before a fight begins is ideal, as this allows one to pre-build 6 Electro Quivers. From there, the route to stun can change depending on the team, with some teams (like those with Trigger or mono-Shock) demanding some field time, but most standard comps having Harumasa sit out until stun arrives, with only the occasional Defensive Assist and Assist Follow-Up for Decibel generation and Electric Anomaly build-up. Stun should arrive in less than 60 seconds from the first Quiver being set-up and ideally Anomaly should be at around 3/4s full, so that it can align with certain points of his combo (varies based on enemy Anomaly limit and weaknesses). A standard Anomaly-timed combo would be: Nicole EX Special Attack: Stuffed Sugarcoated Bullet Harumasa Quick Assist: Braced Bow EX Special Attack: Nowhere to Run - Patrol Dash Attack: Hiten no Tsuru - Slash 1 Dash Attack: Hiten no Tsuru - Slash 2 Dash Attack: Hiten no Tsuru - Slash 3 Dash Attack: Hiten no Tsuru - Slash 2 Basic Attack: Falling Feather Dash Attack: Hiten no Tsuru - Slash 1 Dash Attack: Hiten no Tsuru - Slash 2 Dash Attack: Hiten no Tsuru - Slash 3 Nicole Ultimate: Ether Grenade Harumasa Chain Attack: Kai - Hanare (Shock Anomaly) Cancel Dash Attack: Hiten no Tsuru - Slash 1 Dash Attack: Hiten no Tsuru - Slash 2 Dash Attack: Hiten no Tsuru - Slash 3 EX Special Attack: Nowhere to Run - Patrol Ultimate: Zanshin Nicole Chain Attack: Ether Shellacking Zanshin - Scattered Blossoms Harumasa Quick Assist: Braced Bow Dash Attack: Hiten no Tsuru - Slash 1 Dash Attack: Hiten no Tsuru - Slash 2 Dash Attack: Hiten no Tsuru - Slash 3 Dash Attack: Hiten no Tsuru - Slash 2 Basic Attack: Falling Feather Dash Attack: Hiten no Tsuru - Slash 1 Dash Attack: Hiten no Tsuru - Slash 2 Dash Attack: Hiten no Tsuru - Slash 3 Basic Attack: Falling Feather Dash Attack: Hiten no Tsuru - Slash 1 Basic Attack: Cloud Piercer 4 Basic Attack: Cloud Piercer 5 The final Basic Attacks would be landing out of stun, and are used only to set-up 6 Electro Quivers in advance of the next combo cycle. The Shock Anomaly can","pros":"High skill ceiling character that thoroughly rewards player skill expression. Variety of team options, working well in pure stun burst/hypercarry teams, as well as non-standard comps (like with Seed or mono-Shock) depending on investment. Was handed out for free to all players. Mastering him is the epitome of ZZZ bragging rights.","cons":"Demanding execution requirements, with an unforgiving skill floor that can be somewhat hostile to beginners. Needs proper route planning and mapping to perform at his best, with Anomaly alignment being required for the best combos and builds. Pre-stacking of Quivers before fights begin is tedious and often mandatory for the highest level of play. May not live long enough to see EoS.","teams":[{"m":"Harumasa + Dialyn + Astra Yao + Birkblick","c":"","r":"Rank 177"},{"m":"Harumasa + Seed + Trigger + Plugboo","c":"","r":"Rank 230"},{"m":"Harumasa + Dialyn + Yuzuha + Plugboo","c":"","r":"Rank 230"}]},"Anby":{"slug":"anby-demara","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Turbo Volt","d":"Press to activate. Unleashes up to 4 slashes. The first 3 hits deal Physical DMG the 4th hit deals Electric DMG.","m":["1st-Hit: 31.2%","2nd-Hit: 33.7%","3rd-Hit: 113.6%","4th-Hit: 239.1%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Thunderbolt","d":"After unleashing the 3rd hit of the Basic Attack, hold down or pause for a short while, and then press to activate. Unleashes a downward strike that deals Electric DMG. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["328.6%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Fork Lightning","d":"Press to activate. Unleashes an upward slash that deals Electric DMG. This attack launches faster when used after the 3rd-hit of the Basic Attack or Basic Attack: Thunderbolt. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["93.4%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Lightning Bolt","d":"With enough energy, press to activate. Unleashes a powerful upward slash that deals Electric DMG. This attack launches faster when used after the 3rd hit of her Basic Attack or Basic Attack: Thunderbolt. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["583%","Energy Cost: 60%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Slide","d":"Press to dodge. A rapid dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Taser Blast","d":"Press during a dodge to activate. Slashes all nearby enemies, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["56.7%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Thunderclap","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Slashes enemies in front, dealing Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["180.2%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Electro Engine","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate. Unleashes a powerful upwards slash at enemies in a small area, dealing massive Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["542.4%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Overdrive Engine","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate. Unleashes a powerful upward slash at enemies in a small area followed by several falling attacks, dealing massive Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1512.6%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Thunderfall","d":"When the on-field character is launched, press to activate. Slashes enemies in front, dealing Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["61.7%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Flash","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, inflicting massive Daze. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Lightning Whirl","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate. Perform a spinning slash against enemies in front, dealing Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["335.2%"]}],"build":{"w":["Demara Battery Mark II"],"a":["Woodpecker Electro, Branch \u0026 Blade Song","Proto Punk, Woodpecker Electro, Flex"],"core":7,"st":[["CRIT Rate",65],["CRIT DMG",134],["ATK",2468]]},"how":"","pros":"Very easy combos to learn and execute with high daze potential and a simplistic onfielder playstyle; High Energy generation built into her kit, even able to funnel flat Energy to other Electric characters; Becomes stronger the more aggressive the enemy is, thanks to her Dodge Counter, while remaining usable at a baseline; Surprisingly acceptable personal damage by Stun character standards, especially at M6; She’s free!","cons":"Has little to no AoE potential unless enemies are on top of each other; Provides very little value to other Agents as she has no extra buffs/debuffs like other Stun Agents do; Overshadowed in any team by one or more options, which makes her very easily replaceable.","teams":[{"m":"Anby + Nicole + Astra Yao + Amillion","c":"","r":"Rank 388"},{"m":"Harumasa + Anby + Rina + Plugboo","c":"","r":"Rank 310"},{"m":"Pyrois + Anby + Nicole + Amillion","c":"","r":"Rank 365"}]},"Yanagi":{"slug":"yanagi","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Tsukuyomi Kagura","d":"Yanagi has two stances: Jougen and Kagen. Press to activate: Execute up to five forward slashes based on the current stance, causing Physical DMG and Electric DMG. During combat, Yanagi gains the corresponding stance buff based on her current stance: Jougen stance buff: Electric DMG increases by 10%. Anti-Interrupt Level increases during Basic Attacks. Kagen stance buff: PEN Ratio increases by 10%. Interrupt Level increases for Basic Attacks. For 8s after switching stances, Yanagi retains the bonus from the previous stance.","m":["Jougen 1st-Hit: 56.6%","Jougen 2nd-Hit: 99.7%","Jougen 3rd-Hit: 113.1%","Jougen 4th-Hit: 126.6%","Jougen 5th-Hit: 236.9%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Ruten","d":"Press to activate. Perform a forward slash, dealing Electric DMG, and switch the current stance. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill. If activated after the 3rd, 4th, or 5th hit of a Basic Attack, it activates Swift Ruten, speeding up the slashes while switching her current stance. Block enemy attacks while Swift Ruten is active. Upon activating Swift Ruten, Yanagi can immediately follow up with the 3rd hit of the current stance\u0027s Basic Attack.","m":["117.4%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Gekka Ruten","d":"With enough energy, press to activate: Charge up power for a quick forward thrust, followed by a downward attack, dealing massive Electric DMG. Upon executing the thrust, Yanagi switches stances and enters the Shinrabanshou state, lasting 15s. For the duration of this state, when following up with a subsequent Basic Attack from the 5th hit of a Basic Attack or other skills, the combo will begin directly from the 3rd hit of the Basic Attack. If the downward attack hits an enemy suffering an Anomaly, it triggers a special Disorder effect, Polarity Disorder, dealing 15% of the original Disorder effect\u0027s DMG to the target, plus an additional percentage of Yanagi\u0027s Anomaly Proficiency. Polarity Disorder will not remove the target\u0027s Anomaly.","m":["Thrust Attack: 163.8%","Downward Attack: 377.8%","Energy Cost: 40%","Additional DMG: 725%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Wandering Breeze","d":"Press to activate. A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Fleeting Flight","d":"Press during a dodge to activate: Slashes enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["50.4%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Rapid Retaliation","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Slashes enemies in front, dealing Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. After using this skill, you can immediately follow up with the 3rd hit of the current stance\u0027s Basic Attack.","m":["231.6%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Celestial Harmony","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Switch stances and unleash a powerful slash on enemies in front, dealing massive Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. After using this skill, you can immediately follow up with the 3rd hit of the current stance\u0027s Basic Attack.","m":["593.1%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Raiei Tenge","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate. Yanagi unleashes her potential and delivers a powerful slash to a large area of enemies in front in a very short time, followed by an additional lightning strike, dealing massive Electric DMG. When the lightning strike hits an enemy affected by an Attribute Anomaly, it triggers a special Disorder effect called Polarity Disorder. This deals DMG equal to 15% of the original Disorder effect plus an additional percentage of Yanagi\u0027s Anomaly Proficiency. Polarity Disorder will not remove the target\u0027s Anomaly. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. After using this skill, Yanagi can immediately follow up with the 3rd hit of the current stance\u0027s Basic Attack.","m":["1511.8%","Additional DMG: 730%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Blade of Elegance","d":"When the on-field character is launched, press to activate. Slashes enemies in front, dealing Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. After using this skill, you can immediately follow up with the 3rd hit of the current stance\u0027s Basic Attack.","m":["93.6%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Radiant Reversal","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, inflicting massive Daze. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Weeping Willow Stab","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate: Switch stances, and quickly deliver multiple slashes to enemies in front, dealing Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. After using this skill, you can immediately follow up with the 3rd hit of the current stance\u0027s Basic Attack.","m":["407.1%"]}],"build":{"w":["Timeweaver","Weeping Gemini","Fusion Compiler","Electro-Lip Gloss"],"a":["Chaos Jazz, Freedom Blues","Chaos Jazz, Feathered Fate","Freedom Blues, Chaos Jazz","Thunder Metal, Chaos Jazz"],"core":7,"st":[["CRIT Rate",13],["CRIT DMG",65],["ATK",2936]]},"how":"","pros":"Boosts Disorder damage, inflicts Disorder on her own regardless of Anomaly Buildup; Able to apply Anomaly effectively in quick, short bursts but also in a more sustained on-field playstyle — very flexible gameplay-wise; Doesn\u0027t mind lower investments as much as other characters due to being able to be used as a disorder bot within a Miyabi team, has good F2P W-Engine choices and having most skills unlevelled is okay; Has lots of team options available by extension of her playstyle fiexibility.","cons":"Lots of buffs to keep track of with short uptimes; Performance will vastly vary depending on available second and third slot teammates — significantly enjoys her best choices comparatively to alternatives.","teams":[{"m":"Miyabi + Yanagi + Yuzuha + Agent Gulliver","c":"","r":"Rank 35"},{"m":"Miyabi + Yanagi + Astra Yao + Agent Gulliver","c":"","r":"Rank 59"},{"m":"Remielle + Velina + Yanagi + Ariel","c":"","r":"Rank 74"}]},"Orphie (Magus)":{"slug":"orphie-and-magus","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: High-Pressure Flamethrower","d":"Press to activate: Unleashes up to 5 attacks in front, followed by a powerful flame blade strike, dealing Physical DMG and Fire DMG.","m":["1st-Hit: 14.5%","2nd-Hit: 44.4%","3rd-Hit: 41.5%","4th-Hit: 86.7%","5th-Hit: 1818.6%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Blazing Chamber","d":"Press to activate. Thrust forward and perform a tail attack, dealing Fire DMG. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["36.5%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Corrosive Flash","d":"Automatically triggers during ally attacks: Unleashes 4 laser Aftershock attacks, dealing Fire DMG. Triggers once per 5s. Upon activating this skill, restore 20 Bottled Heat. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["495%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Watch Your Step","d":"With enough Energy, press to activate: Perform a sweeping laser attack forward, dealing Fire DMG. After using this skill, immediately follow up with the powerful fire blade from the Basic Attack. Upon activating this skill, restore 20 Bottled Heat. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["280.9%","Energy Cost: 30%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Crimson Vortex","d":"When off-field with 60 or more Energy, automatically triggers during ally attacks: Performs a sweeping laser attack in an area around, dealing Fire DMG. Upon activating this skill, restore 20 Bottled Heat. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["678.4%","Energy Cost: 30%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Heat Charge","d":"When Bottled Heat is greater than or equal to 100, hold to activate: Consume 100 Bottled Heat to continuously fire a laser forward, dealing Fire DMG. When firing begins, triggers Quick Assist. After continuous firing for a period, firepower increases, greatly boosting the skill\u0027s Interrupt Level. When attacked during firing, will parry enemy attacks and immediately increase firepower. When maximum firing duration is reached, automatically activates EX Special Attack: Fiery Eruption. During the low firepower phase, Anti-Interrupt Level increases and DMG taken is reduced by 40%, while character is invulnerable during the high firepower phase.","m":["Laser Maximum: 389.4%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Fiery Eruption","d":"Automatically activates after EX Special Attack: Heat Charge reaches maximum firing time: Performs a spinning attack forward, then fires a laser ahead dealing Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["259.6%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Flickering Flames","d":"Press to activate. A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Rush Command","d":"Press during a dodge to activate: Perform a quick forward attack, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["62.3%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Counter Strike Opportunity","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Launch a series of attacks on enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG and Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["257.8%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Overheated Barrel","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Perform a spinning attack forward, then fire a laser ahead, dealing Fire DMG. Upon activating this skill, restore 20 points of Bottled Heat. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["626.3%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Dance With Fire","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate. Perform a spinning attack forward, then fire a laser ahead, dealing Fire DMG. When leaping into the air, a Quick Assist will be triggered. If the Quick Assist is activated, Orphie \u0026 Magus will extend the laser firing duration. Upon activating this skill, recover 20 Bottled Heat. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["698.7%","Extended Duration Total: 465.8%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Searing Slash","d":"When the active character is launched, press to activate. Unleash a series of attacks on enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG and Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["113.7%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Blazing Gunblade","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Boiling Pierce","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate: Unleash multiple attacks against enemies in front, dealing Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["360.9%"]}],"build":{"w":["Bellicose Blaze","Gilded Blossom","Marcato Desire","Heartstring Nocturne"],"a":["Shadow Harmony, Moonlight Lullaby","Shadow Harmony, Swing Jazz","Shadow Harmony, Branch \u0026 Blade Song","Shadow Harmony, Woodpecker Electro"],"core":7,"st":[["CRIT Rate",41],["CRIT DMG",145],["ATK",2744]]},"how":"","pros":"Good on-field and inactive damage potential, paired with buffing capabilities; Low skill floor and a high skill ceiling — lots of room for optimization while retaining good baseline performance; Easy to build, low-cost character in general from skill levels, to W-Engines, to Disk Drives; Top-tier animations.","cons":"Has a lot of extended inactive animations, during which she cannot swap back to input any other actions, can be annoying for team combos; Limited powerful synergies on release, locking strong performance behind pairing her with very specific characters. Low primary DPS potential, greatly overshadowed by her secondary DPS role (even if she can theoretically achieve mid-tier primary DPS performance).","teams":[{"m":"Anby: Soldier 0 + Orphie y Magus + Trigger + Mercury","c":"","r":"Rank 16"},{"m":"Seed + Orphie y Magus + Trigger + Mercury","c":"","r":"Rank 88"},{"m":"Anby: Soldier 0 + Orphie y Magus + Astra Yao + Mercury","c":"","r":"Rank 146"}]},"Nicole":{"slug":"nicole-demara","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Cunning Combo","d":"Press to activate. Unleashes up to 3 strikes, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["1st-Hit: 65.9%","2nd-Hit: 71.3%","3rd-Hit: 304.3%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Do As I Please","d":"After using a Special Attack, EX Special Attack, Chain Attack, or Ultimate, Nicole can reload, and her Basic Attack and Dash Attack are enhanced, increasing the power of her bullets.","m":["1st-Hit: 88.1%","2nd-Hit: 100.9%","3rd-Hit: 452.3%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Sugarcoated Bullet","d":"Press to activate. Unleashes a ranged strike against enemies in front, dealing Ether DMG. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill. Automatically reloads after the attack to enhance Basic Attack and Dash Attack up to 8 times.","m":["52.6%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Stuffed Sugarcoated Bullet","d":"With enough energy, press to activate. A powerful ranged strike, generating an energy field that pulls enemies towards its center to deal Ether DMG. Hold down to charge up this attack, during which a small energy field is generated at the muzzle as Energy is consumed, dealing bonus DMG to enemies nearby. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. A Quick Assist is triggered when this skill hits an enemy. Automatically reloads after the attack to enhance Basic Attack and Dash Attack up to 8 times.","m":["Charged Attack: 215.2%","Bombard: 215.1%","Energy Field: 387%","Charger Attack Energy Cost (per sec): 20%","Bombard Energy Cost: 60%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Speed Demon","d":"Press to activate. A rapid dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. Drag the to dodge, then hold to reload while dodging, enhancing Basic Attacks and Dash Attacks up to 8 times.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Jack in the Box","d":"When dragging the during a dodge, press : Dashes in the target direction and strikes nearby enemies, dealing Physical DMG. When not dragging the during a dodge, press : Vaults backward and launches a ranged strike against enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG. Automatically reloads after the attack to enhance her Basic Attack and Dash Attack, up to 8 times.","m":["Forward Dash: 158.2%","Backward Vault: 60%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Diverted Bombard","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Dodge backwards and send a ranged strike at enemies in front, dealing Ether DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. Automatically reloads after the attack to enhance Basic Attack and Dash Attack up to 8 times.","m":["182.4%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Ether Shellacking","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select a character to activate: Unleashes a powerful ranged strike at enemies in a small area, generating an energy field that pulls enemies towards its center to deal Ether DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. A Quick Assist is triggered when this skill hits an enemy. Automatically reloads after the attack to enhance Basic Attack and Dash Attack up to 8 times.","m":["Bombard: 209.6%","Energy Field: 283%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Ether Grenade","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate: Unleashes a powerful ranged strike at enemies in a small area, generating an energy field that pulls enemies towards its center to deal Ether DMG. When using this skill, other squad members recover 10 Energy. The next character to switch in gains an additional 20 energy. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. A Quick Assist is triggered when this skill hits an enemy. Automatically reloads after the attack to enhance Basic Attack and Dash Attack up to 8 times.","m":["Bombard: 646.8%","Energy Field: 873.2%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Emergency Bombard","d":"When the on-field character is launched, press to activate. Dodge backwards and send ranged strikes at enemies in front, dealing Ether DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. Automatically reloads after the attack to enhance Basic Attack and Dash Attack up to 8 times.","m":["63.4%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: The Hare Strikes Back","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Window of Opportunity","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate. Charge forward and bombard enemies, dealing Ether DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["377.1%"]}],"build":{"w":["The Vault","Kaboom the Cannon","Weeping Cradle","Unfettered Game Ball"],"a":["Moonlight Lullaby, Swing Jazz","Moonlight Lullaby, Phaethon\u0027s Melody","Swing Jazz, Chaotic Metal","Astral Voice, Swing Jazz"],"core":6.89,"st":[["CRIT Rate",32],["CRIT DMG",86],["ATK",2144]]},"how":"Nicole’s game plan is all about maximising her debuffs for critical periods. Besides that, how she plays tends to ride on the team comp and encounter. To start with, ensuring that her debuffs are up throughout all of a damage dealer’s stun burst is the most important skill to master early. If using The Vault as a W-Engine, the additional Energy Regen it provides means that it’s possible for Nicole to get multiple EX Special casts in a single stun period. Each team will have a unique combo, but as a good template, opening with her EX Special and then weaving in a Chain Attack, Ultimate and/or a second EX Special mid-stun serves to both ensure uptime of Drive Discs (be it Moonlight Lullaby or Astral Voice via Quick Assists) and maintain her debuffs. Merely tapping her EX Special is enough for most comps, but in certain teams where Anomalies are required, it can be useful to hold down her EX Special at melee range to maximise Anomaly application, but be careful to not do so at the cost of damage elsewhere and fit it in while the main damage dealer is taken up in their own attack animations. Optimising Nicole out of stun is where things get very difficult and what lands her the “Expert” tag. Different characters have different points in which they are taken up in skills but can be safely swapped out of; Zhu Yuan during her triple Shotshell finisher, Miyabi on a level 3 Shimotsuki, Evelyn as she casts her points Chain Attack, Alice on a level 3 Starshine Waltz, etc. Use these as opportunities to swap to Nicole and do Basic Attacks, Dash Attacks, or EX Specials to refresh her debuff and - if using her EX - apply Anomaly and build Decibels on top. While it may be tempting to try and shoot for 100% uptime of her debuff, it’s not realistic to do so and often comes with a hefty opportunity cost. There’s no need to have her debuff applied on attacks that do little damage after all, so learning when and where to prioritise swapping to Nicole is part of her skill expression. It’s worth noting that DEF Shred and PEN Ratio negatively affect the impact they have on enemies when paired together due to how damage is calculated - avoid pairing Nicole and Rina in a Double Support team setup for example, or building PEN Ratio on your Disc Drives/W-Engines if Nicole is present in the team. Even without exploiting Nicole’s Additional Ability reserved to Ether teams (which only adds to her value in those), she remains one of the most versatile Support Agents, and while she doesn’t function with Rupture Agents as they completely ignore her DEF Shred capabilities, with any Attack","pros":"Amazing DEF Shred debuff that amplifies your party’s DMG by a ton. Additionally provides CRIT Rate at M6 and Ether DMG with her Additional Ability; Even has a DMG% debuff on her Signature W-Engine. All in all one of the strongest supportive potentials in the game by a long shot; Able to gather enemies in an Energy Field which is practical for Shiyu Defense etc.; Low field time, can swap in and out really easily, even in the middle of a stun combo. Also able to trigger Quick Assists efficiently; She’s free! There are very few cons to this character. She’s good with almost everyone. She requires minimal investment. Build Nicole.","cons":"Really low DEF Shred uptime, requires constant management, may even require her to intervene in the midst of a Stun window. DEF Shred is not only completely antisynergistic with Rupture Agents but also makes PEN Ratio less valuable. Keep this in mind when building a team including Nicole.","teams":[{"m":"Miyabi + Nicole + Astra Yao + Resonaboo","c":"","r":"Rank 97"},{"m":"Pyrois + Nicole + Astra Yao + Snap","c":"","r":"Rank 101"},{"m":"Claret + Trigger + Nicole + Plugboo","c":"","r":"Rank 153"}]},"Astra Yao":{"slug":"astra-yao","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: \"Capriccio\"","d":"Press to activate: Perform up to three attacks forward, dealing Ether DMG. During the 3rd-hit, hold to charge, drawing enemies in and expanding the attack range for a stronger attack. After using other skills, hold to initiate the 3rd-hit directly.","m":["1st-Hit: 43.8%","2nd-Hit: 59.1%","3rd-Hit Min: 120.9%","3rd-Hit Max: 270.7%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Interlude","d":"While in the Idyllic Cadenza state, press to activate: Release Tremolo forward to attack, dealing Ether DMG. A Quick Assist will be triggered when this skill hits an enemy.","m":["1st-Hit: 55%","2nd-Hit: 55%","3rd-Hit: 55%","4th-Hit: 55%","5th-Hit: 55%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Chorus","d":"While in the Idyllic Cadenza state, press during a Perfect Dodge to activate: Launch multiple Tremolo attacks at enemies in front, dealing massive Ether DMG. A Quick Assist will be triggered when this skill hits an enemy. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["55%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Finale","d":"While in the Idyllic Cadenza state, press to activate: Release Tremolo forward to attack, dealing Ether DMG and exit the Idyllic Cadenza state. Upon activation of the skill, it grants the buff from Core Passive: \"Graceful Andante\". With enough Energy, consumes Energy to follow up with 1 Tremolo and 3 Tone Clusters. This Tremolo attack released is considered an EX Special Attack.","m":["55%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: \"Windchimes \u0026 Oaths\"","d":"Press to activate. Quickly move, then release Tremolo, dealing Ether DMG, and enter the Idyllic Cadenza state. During activation, dragging the stick/joystick enables movement in the direction held. Hold to charge during activation, drawing enemies in, and follow up with 1 to 4 Tremolos depending on the charge duration. A Quick Assist will be triggered when this skill hits an enemy. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Minimum: 55%","Maximum: 55%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Idyllic Cadenza","d":"After entering the Idyllic Cadenza state, Astra Yao increases all squad members\u0027 DMG and CRIT DMG. While in the Idyllic Cadenza state, Astra Yao cannot move, but pressing will activate Basic Attack: Interlude, and pressing will activate a dodge. After triggering a Perfect Dodge, press to activate Basic Attack: Chorus. While in this state, Astra Yao\u0027s Anti-Interrupt Level is increased, and the DMG she takes is reduced by 40%. After switching to another character, Astra Yao will remain on the field and become Invulnerable. When switching back to her, she will automatically follow up with Special Attack: Windchimes \u0026 Oaths. During this state, hold to activate Basic Attack: Finale, or hold to exit the Idyllic Cadenza state.","m":["Squad DMG Increase: 9%","Squad CRIT DMG Increase: 8.5%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Chord","d":"For every 25 Energy, Astra Yao will have 1 Chord. While in the Idyllic Cadenza state, when Astra Yao has Chords, a Quick Assist can be triggered in the following situations: When the controlled character\u0027s attack hits an enemy, once per 3s. When the controlled character\u0027s heavy attack hits an enemy, once per 1s. When other characters in the squad switch in through a Quick Assist, Chain Attack, Defensive Assist, or Evasive Assist, Astra Yao will consume 25 Energy and release 1 Tremolo to attack. This Tremolo attack released is considered an EX Special Attack. After triggering a Quick Assist, quickly press to switch characters and trigger a Precise Assist, causing Astra Yao to follow up with 3 Tone Clusters to attack. When other squad members switch in through a Chain Attack, Defensive Assist, or Evasive Assist, it will automatically trigger a Precise Assist.","m":["Follow-Up Tremolo: 46%","Follow-Up Tone Cluster: 24%","Energy Cost: 25%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: \"Mini Waltz\"","d":"Press to activate. A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: \"Lunar Eclipse Melody\"","d":"Press during a dodge to activate: Attack ahead, dealing Ether DMG. When triggered, dragging thestick/joystick allows movement in the corresponding direction.","m":["80.7%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: \"Umbrella Waltz\"","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Attack enemies in front, dealing Ether DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["110%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: \"Tipsy Concerto\"","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Use song to channel energy into a blast, dealing massive Ether DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. After the skill, Astra Yao enters the Idyllic Cadenza state.","m":["671.8%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: \"Fantasian Sonata\"","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate. Use song to channel energy into a blast, dealing massive Ether DMG, and restoring some HP to all squad members. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. After the skill, Astra Yao enters the Idyllic Cadenza state. After the skill, the next two Quick Assists will be replaced by Chain Attacks.","m":["1959.8%","HP Recovery: 200%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: \"One Luminous Sky\"","d":"When the on-field character is launched, press to activate. Attack enemies in front, dealing Ether DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["55%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Evasive Assist: \"Two Hearts\"","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Dodges the enemy\u0027s attack and activates Vital View. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: \"Three Lifetimes of Fate\"","d":"Press after an Evasive Assist to activate: Release an energy beam forward, dealing Ether DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["304.6%"]}],"build":{"w":["Elegant Vanity","Kaboom the Cannon","Bashful Demon","The Vault"],"a":["Astral Voice, Swing Jazz","Astral Voice, Moonlight Lullaby","Moonlight Lullaby, Swing Jazz","Moonlight Lullaby, Astral Voice"],"core":6.99,"st":[["CRIT Rate",22],["CRIT DMG",81],["ATK",3421]]},"how":"At first glance, Astra is a very simple character: use her Special, Quick Assist out, then be done with it. However, there are many ways to optimise her, as she can be surprisingly complex. Sustaining her Core Passive: Graceful Andante’s buff is easy when alternating between two Agents, however this often isn’t the case for many teams in which Astra is a good pick for. Any team with a damage dealer that likes on-fielding, such as with Ellen, Evelyn, Soldier 0 - Anby, Seed, etc. may often come into a scenario where one is Quick Assisting out to a Stunner or secondary support, but not remain on them long enough for Astra to regenerate her Energy for another Quick Assist. Therefore, it’s important to keep an eye out for her buff uptime, as it can frequently drop in critical periods - like in stun bursts - if special attention isn’t given to her Energy levels. Besides standard buff management, Astra can struggle in generating Decibels in fights. Although she is able to trigger Anomalies while being inactive, her personal build-up is awful (both of Decibels and Anomaly), making her overly reliant on shared Decibel generation. To remedy this, making use of her Basic Attack: Finale to exit Idyllic Cadenza is a way to open up Astra to be picked for Evasive Assists. It only uses up 1 Assist Point (so assuming a team of 2 Assist Point cost characters, it does not sacrifice the total number of Perfect Assists) and can help with building Decibels to better align her Ultimates. Do remember to get her back in Idyllic Cadenza right after, as while her Core Passive’s ATK buff is independent of it, her DMG and CRIT DMG bonuses are not. In combos, Astra can also allow for double Chain Attacks in a single character from her Ultimate alone. Normally, this is not possible, as once her Ultimate is used, a Quick Assist prompt will yield a Chain Attack to the following character - normally the main damage dealer - but after that, the next Quick Assist prompt will take one to the second character. This will happen regardless of Energy too, owing to her Ultimate forcing the Idyllic Cadenza state and its unique property that forces Quick Assist prompts when any squad member lands a Chain Attack or Ultimate until all charges are used up. The trick lies in the fact that these Quick Assist prompts can only come up while Astra is in Idyllic Cadenza or after hardcasting her Special. Which means that it’s possible to: Astra Ultimate Basic Attack: Finale to exit Idyllic Cadenza Quick Assist → Chain Attack to main damage dealer Swap back to Astra and hardcast her Special Quick Assist → Ch","pros":"Universal support that can be played in almost any team composition. Buffs affect the whole team, offering even greater power to double damage teams than other supports. Provides Healing to teammates, which is useful for content where sustain is relevant. Allows incredibly frequent use of quick assists and the use of chain attacks outside of stun windows. Provides an incredible array of buffs, including one of the highest attack buffs in the game.","cons":"Effectively locks you into a 2 active Agent playstyledue to her low field time playstyle which while competitive wont be for everyone.","teams":[{"m":"Cissia + Seed + Astra Yao + Plugboo","c":"","r":"Rank 20"},{"m":"Sigrid + Norma + Astra Yao + Ultra Jake","c":"","r":"Rank 21"},{"m":"Ye Shunguang + Astra Yao + Zhao + Sprout","c":"","r":"Rank 22"}]},"Phoenix":{"slug":"phoenix","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Sever Life","d":"Press to activate: Performs up to 4 attacks forward, dealing Fire DMG. The 3rd and 4th Basic Attacks are considered Combustion Attacks.","m":["1st-Hit: 15.6%","2nd-Hit: 67.7%","3rd-Hit: 178.1%","4th-Hit: 389.2%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Purifying Flame","d":"With enough Pyre, consume 90 Pyre and hold to activate: Phoenix throws her weapon, dealing massive Fire DMG to enemies in an area ahead. When the Finishing Move hits an enemy affected by Ice Anomaly, Ether Anomaly, Electric Anomaly, Fire Anomaly, Physical Anomaly, or Wind Anomaly, it triggers 1 instance of Abloom, dealing Anomaly DMG of the corresponding attribute with a 245% multiplier. When this instance of Abloom triggers a critical hit, its CRIT DMG is increased by an additional 40%. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["547.3%","Abloom Multiplier: 225%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Meltdown","d":"If Special Attack: Fire Sweep does not trigger a Perfect Block, press to activate: Charge forward, dealing Fire DMG. Considered a Combustion Attack. During this skill, press Icon_Normal to follow up with the 3rd hit of a Basic Attack.","m":["178.1%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Drifting Sway","d":"Press to activate: A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Lunge","d":"Press during a dodge to activate: Dashes forward and slashes, dealing Fire DMG.","m":["104%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Twin Passage of Karmic Fire","d":"After triggering a Perfect Dodge, press to activate: Dash forward and unleash a quick slash, dealing Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. Press to follow up with the 3rd hit of a Basic Attack.","m":["296.2%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Emergency Aid","d":"When the active character is launched, press to activate: Dash forward and unleash a quick slash, dealing Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. Press to follow up with the 3rd hit of a Basic Attack.","m":["95.4%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Patient Turned Doctor","d":"When the on-field character is about to be attacked, press to activate: Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Regeneration Therapy","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate: Throws her weapon at the enemy, then recalls it and performs a slash, dealing Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. Press to follow up with the 3rd hit of a Basic Attack.","m":["426.5%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Fire Sweep","d":"Press to activate: After retreating back, quickly launch an upward slash forward, dealing Fire DMG. During the retreat, DMG taken is reduced by 40%. If attacked at the instant the upward slash begins, or if the slash hits an enemy flashing red or yellow, a Perfect Block is triggered, negating that instance of DMG. Press to immediately follow up with the 3rd hit of a Basic Attack. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["45.6%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Blazing Slash","d":"With Ascension, consume 1 point of Ascension and press to activate: After retreating, quickly perform a powerful upward slash, dealing massive Fire DMG. Hold while retreating to continue charging. While charging, release to perform a powerful upward slash, dealing massive Fire DMG. When chained into from a Combustion Attack, skip the retreat and immediately perform the upward slash. DMG taken while retreating and charging is reduced by 40%. Receiving an attack just as the upward slash begins or hitting an enemy flashing red or yellow triggers a Perfect Block. This skill counts as a Combustion Attack. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. Press to follow up with the 3rd hit of a Basic Attack.","m":["380.5%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Dazzling Flare","d":"With enough Energy, press to activate: Quickly spin around, dealing massive Fire DMG to enemies. Receiving an attack at the moment the spin begins or hitting an enemy flashing red or yellow triggers a Perfect Block. This skill is considered a Combustion Attack. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. Press Icon_Normal to follow up with the 3rd hit of a Basic Attack.","m":["457.6%","Energy Cost: 40%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Falling Sun","d":"After using EX Special Attack: Dazzling Flare, and with enough Energy, press or hold to activate: Rises into the air and throws her weapon, dealing massive Fire DMG to enemies. Gain 1 point of Ascension when the skill is activated. Up to 1 point of Ascension can be held. Receiving an attack at the moment she starts rising or hitting an enemy flashing red or yellow triggers a Perfect Block. This skill is considered a Combustion Attack. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. Press to follow up with the 3rd hit of a Basic Attack.","m":["623%","Energy Cost: 40%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Last-Minute Salvation","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Unleash multiple attacks forward, dealing Fire DMG. Considered a Combustion Attack. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. Press to follow up with the 3rd hit of a Basic Attack.","m":["882.7%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Perpetual Resurrection","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate: Fly into the air, then dive at the enemy, consuming all of Phoenix\u0027s HP to trigger an explosion, dealing massive Fire DMG, then enter the Wither state, and trigger the next character\u0027s Quick Assist. Considered a Combustion Attack. Active attacks cannot be performed while in the Wither state. A short while after using this skill, Soul-Searching Blaze is automatically activated after a short period. Press to quickly activate Soul-Searching Blaze. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1813.9%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Soul-Searching Blaze","d":"Triggered when Phoenix is in the Wither state, the next time she enters the field through a normal switch, Quick Assist, or Defensive Assist: Phoenix is wreathed in flames, dealing Fire DMG to nearby enemies, which is also considered Ultimate DMG, and exiting the Wither state. She recovers all HP consumed by Ultimate: Perpetual Resurrection, plus an additional 10% of her Max HP. When the Finishing Move hits an enemy affected by Ice Anomaly, Ether Anomaly, Electric Anomaly, Fire Anomaly, Physical Anomaly, or Wind Anomaly, it triggers 1 instance of Abloom, resolving the corresponding Attribute Anomaly at a 327% multiplier. When this Abloom effect triggers a critical hit, its CRIT DMG is increased by an additional 40%. When Phoenix enters the field via Chain Attack: Last-Minute Salvation or Ultimate: Perpetual Resurrection while in the Wither state, the HP recovery and Abloom effects described above are also triggered. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. Press Icon_Normal to follow up with the 3rd hit of a Basic Attack.","m":["95.5%","Abloom Multiplier: 300%"]}],"build":{"w":["Plume of Rebirth","Weeping Gemini","Angel in the Shell","Fusion Compiler"],"a":["Freedom Blues, Phaethon\u0027s Melody","Chaos Jazz, Phaethon\u0027s Melody","Feathered Fate, Phaethon\u0027s Melody","Phaethon\u0027s Melody, Freedom Blues"],"core":6.93,"st":[["CRIT Rate",12],["CRIT DMG",64],["ATK",2598]]},"how":"Phoenix has multiple resources but they all tie into one another, leading to a relatively simple flowchart: Use her Basic 3 and 4. Then cast her Special to make use of the Combustion attack shortcut, and loop into the alternate Basic, then Basics 3 and 4 again. As needed, cycle through her EX Specials for additional Anomaly build-up, making use of the free alternate EX as it comes. When there’s enough Pyre available, make use of her enhanced Basic Attack for its high Anomaly build-up and the Abloom trigger. If Ultimate is ready, use it + the Soul-Searching Blaze follow-up for high Anomaly build-up and an Abloom. The Quick Assist triggered by the Ultimate can be used during Soul-Searching Blaze if looking to swap out of Phoenix. Many of her skills also have rather long animations, like her Basic 4 and enhanced Basic Attack. On teams with Remielle, or other Anomaly Agents that may have field-time demands, this is an opportunity to swap out of Phoenix to use their skills. As Phoenix’s CRIT DMG does not apply to Disorders, her teams should ideally have a Wind Anomaly Agent to enable Vortex. Optimising the number of Vortexes then becomes the primary goal, trying to avoid overcapping on Anomaly build-up to get more triggers.","pros":"Allows Anomaly DMG to CRIT, being a unique multiplier that applies to all sorts of effects (Ablooms, Vortex, Luminizes, etc). Resurrection effect can be very useful in certain modes (like Operation Bagel) and makes her forgiving to use. A significant step-up in performance compared to Anomaly drivers released before her to Vortex teams. Immune to death-","cons":"CRIT passive only applies to Anomalies, not Disorders, which limits her team-building options. Lack of Anomaly Mastery F2P W-Engines means she needs Signature or limited alternatives to max out her passive. Demands a full premium line-up, as she has one of the biggest drops in performance between her top team and anything else. -but not to pain…","teams":[{"m":"velina + remielle, ukinami-yuzuha","c":"","r":""}]},"Lucia":{"slug":"lucia","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Orbital Combo","d":"Press to activate: Perform up to five forward strikes, dealing Ether DMG. The fifth attack is a Whim, conjuring an Ethereal figure that inflicts Ether DMG on enemies in a circular area ahead. When in combat and not in the Dream state, Lucia gains 40 Dream Points upon using this Whim.","m":["1st-Hit: 40.9%","2nd-Hit: 27.8%","3rd-Hit: 83.5%","4th-Hit: 80.1%","Whim: 172.9%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Symphony of the Reaper - Storm","d":"Press to activate. This Special Attack is a Whim. When activated, it recreates an Ethereal figure that slashes forward in a line, dealing Ether DMG. When in combat and not in the Dream state, Lucia gains 20 Dream Points upon using this Whim. This effect can trigger once every 5s.","m":["Whim: 45.9%","Harmony: 183.4%","Aftershock: 550%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Symphony of the Reaper - Daybreak","d":"With enough Energy, press to activate: This EX Special Attack is a Harmony. When activated, it summons an Ethereal figure that delivers a powerful forward slash in a line, dealing Ether DMG. When Lucia uses any Harmony, all squad members gain the Darkbreaker state. While in Darkbreaker state, Sheer Force increases by 12. Every 200 points of Lucia\u0027s initial Max HP grants an additional amount of Sheer Force. The Darkbreaker state can increase Sheer Force by up to a maximum of X, lasting 20s and repeated triggers reset the duration. When Lucia\u0027s initial Max HP reaches 24,000, the above bonus effect reaches its maximum value. When any Harmony deals DMG, Lucia increases the final attack\u0027s DMG by an additional % of her Max HP. If she activates this EX Special Attack while in the Dream state and under the effect of Ether Veil: Wellspring, Ether Veil: Wellspring duration is extended by 16s. After activating her EX Special Attack, Lucia can immediately follow up with the 5th hit of her Basic Attack. If not in the Dream state, Lucia gains 60 Dream Points upon using this Harmony. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["638.1%","Energy Cost: 60%","Sheer Force: 5.2%","Max Additional Sheer Force Increase: 636%","Harmony Additional DMG Multiplier: 37%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Fading Silhouette","d":"Press to activate. A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Refraction","d":"Press during a dodge to activate: Deliver a quick strike forward, dealing Ether DMG.","m":["86.3%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Stardust Echo","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. This Dodge Counter is a Whim. When activated, summons an Ethereal figure that delivers a downward attack in a circular area ahead, dealing Ether DMG. If not in the Dream state, Lucia gains 20 Dream Points upon using this Whim. This effect can trigger once every 5s. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Whim: 248.3%","Harmony: 385.8%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Stage of Brilliance","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: This Chain Attack is a Harmony. When activated, it summons an Ethereal figure that pulls in enemies in a circular area ahead and deals Ether DMG. If not in the Dream state, Lucia gains 40 Dream Points upon using this Harmony. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["616.7%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Charge, Great Armor!","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate. This Ultimate is a Harmony. When activated, Lucia summons an Ethereal figure and rides it forward in a charge. Holding a directional button allows her to steer and extend the charge, up to 3s. During the charge, Anti-Interrupt Level is increased, DMG taken is reduced by 40%, and when Lucia takes fatal DMG, she remains in battle with HP not dropping below 1. When the charge ends, Lucia unleashes a powerful strike in a large area around her, dealing Ether DMG. A Quick Assist is triggered when this skill hits an enemy, and after the skill is used, it leaves behind a Starlight Convergence. Starlight Convergence lasts 8s. While inside Starlight Convergence, the currently active character gains HP regeneration equal to % of Lucia\u0027s Max HP per second. This effect ends 4s after leaving the Starlight Convergence or immediately when switching out. After activation, if Lucia is in the Dream state and Ether Veil: Wellspring is active, Ether Veil: Wellspring duration is extended by 32s. If not in the Dream state, Lucia gains 100 Dream Points upon using this Harmony. If she is in the Dream state when activating this Harmony, she will gain 100 Dream Points and re-enter Dream state the next time she exits it. This effect cannot be stacked. Character is invulnerable while performing the powerful strike.","m":["Charge Single-Hit: 93%","Ultimate: 1902.7%","Percent HP Recovered Per Second: 1.1%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Crushing Mist","d":"When the active character is launched, press to activate. This Quick Assist is a Whim. When activated, it summons an Ethereal figure that delivers a downward attack in a circular area ahead, dealing Ether DMG. If not in the Dream state, Lucia gains 20 Dream Points upon using this Whim. This effect can trigger once every 5s. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Whim: 106.4%","Harmony: 243.9%","Aftershock: 550%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Voice of Illusory Dreams","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Harmony of Painted Dreams","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate: This Assist Follow-Up is a Harmony. When activated, it summons an Ethereal figure that delivers a downward attack in a circular area ahead, dealing Ether DMG. If not in the Dream state, Lucia gains 40 Dream Points upon using this Harmony. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["327.7%"]}],"build":{"w":["Dreamlit Hearth","Kaboom the Cannon","Weeping Cradle","The Vault"],"a":["Moonlight Lullaby, Yunkui Tales","Moonlight Lullaby, Swing Jazz","Moonlight Lullaby, Bunny in Wonderland","Moonlight Lullaby, King of the Summit"],"core":6.99,"st":[["CRIT Rate",19],["CRIT DMG",75],["ATK",2022]]},"how":"$undefined","pros":"The best buffer for Rupture teams bar none. A level above everyone else; Signature W-Engine is not necessary to perform; Rather easy to use at a baseline, while still maintaining some room for optimization; Provides a decent chunk of healing for added comfort; Quite literally the goat","cons":"Has little to no uses outside of Rupture teams; Expensive in terms of skill levels to maximize damage; While her Signature W-Engine is not necessary, it is a noticeable upgrade and makes her much easier to build - but it is also only usable by her.","teams":[{"m":"Yixuan + Dialyn + Lucia + Belion","c":"","r":"Rank 7"},{"m":"Yixuan + Ju Fufu + Lucia + Belion","c":"","r":"Rank 11"},{"m":"Billy - Starlight + Dialyn + Lucia + Birkblick","c":"","r":"Rank 17"}]},"Rina":{"slug":"rina","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Whack the Dimwit","d":"Press to activate. Order Drusilla and Anastella to attack up to 4 times, dealing Physical DMG and Electric DMG. Performing other actions with Rina during Drusilla and Anastella\u0027s attacks will not interrupt Rina\u0027s Basic Attack combo count.","m":["1st-Hit: 44%","2nd-Hit: 111.4%","3rd-Hit: 117.1%","4th-Hit: 183.9%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Shoo the Fool","d":"Hold or to activate. Calls back Drusilla and Anastella to swing them around for a ranged attack, dealing Electric DMG. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["315.1%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Beat the Blockhead","d":"Press to activate. Order Anastella to execute a downward smash, dealing Electric DMG Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["61.3%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Dimwit Disappearing Trick","d":"With enough energy, press to activate: Commands Drusilla and Anastella to unleash a continuous downward smash attack, dealing massive Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. After using this skill, a Quick Assist is triggered.","m":["546%","Energy Cost: 60%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Dress Adjustment","d":"Press to dodge. A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Sudden Surprise","d":"Press during a dodge to activate. Order Drusilla and Anastella to execute a piercing attack, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["105%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Bangboo Callback","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Order Drusilla and Anastella to spin forward and trigger an explosion, dealing Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["227.6%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Code of Conduct","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Order Drusilla and Anastella to push forward and generate a ball-shaped electrical field that deals massive Electric DMG. During this skill, Drusilla and Anastella are unable to perform Basic Attacks, Dash Attacks, Special Attacks, and EX Special Attacks, but can be recalled to Rina\u0027s side through Basic Attack: Shoo the Fool. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. A Quick Assist is triggered when this skill hits an enemy.","m":["1013%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: The Queen\u0027s Attendant","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate: Commands Drusilla and Anastella to spin forward, dealing massive Electric DMG. During this skill, Drusilla and Anastella are unable to respond to Basic Attack, Dash Attack, Special Attack, or EX Special Attack commands, but can be recalled to Rina\u0027s side through Basic Attack: Shoo the Fool. Upon activating this skill, other squad members recover 10 Energy. The next character to switch in recovers an additional 20 Energy. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. After using this skill, a Quick Assist is triggered.","m":["2116.7%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Duple Meter Allemande","d":"When the character on field is launched, press to activate. Order Drusilla and Anastella to spin forward and trigger an explosion, dealing Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["122.6%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Evasive Assist: Tripple Meter Courante","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Dodges the enemy\u0027s attack and activates Vital View. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Quadruple Meter Gavotte","d":"Press after an Evasive Assist to trigger. Commands Drusilla and Anastella to continuously advance while generating a vortex of electricity, dealing Electric DMG. While using this skill, you can quickly chain into EX Special Attack: Dimwit Disappearing Trick. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["349.4%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Morning Cleanup","d":"After Rina uses an EX Special Attack, Chain Attack, or Ultimate, she enters the Spotless state for 13s. During this time, Drusilla or Anastella attacks an enemy once every 2.5s, dealing Physical DMG and Electric DMG, and grants 1 stack of Fright, up to a maximum of 6 stacks. After using the skill, Drusilla and Anastella\u0027s exit timer resets.","m":["1st-Hit: 52.5%","2nd-Hit: 52.5%","3rd-Hit: 52.5%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Midnight Cleanup","d":"When reaches 6 stacks, the next Basic Attack: Morning Cleanup performed by Drusilla or Anastella consumes all Fright stacks and is replaced with Basic Attack: Midnight Cleanup, dealing Electric DMG After using the skill, Drusilla and Anastella\u0027s exit timer resets.","m":["210%"]}],"build":{"w":["Weeping Cradle","Slice of Time","Kaboom the Cannon","Unfettered Game Ball"],"a":["Moonlight Lullaby, Puffer Electro","Swing Jazz, Puffer Electro","Astral Voice, Puffer Electro","Astral Voice, Swing Jazz"],"core":6.87,"st":[["CRIT Rate",24],["CRIT DMG",77],["ATK",2191]]},"how":"Rina has an exceptionally simple gameplan: keep her Bangboos out for as much as possible to have her Core Passive buff up and be sure to enter the Spotless state as stun begins, since the 18ish seconds that the Bangboos will be out in the field for is enough to cover most stun durations. There are optimisations that can be done. If the route allows for it, use her regular Basic or Dash Attack to deploy her Bangboos out to the field. Rina may occasionally have the time to use her EX Special for the Spotless state out-of-stun and still recover Energy in time for it, which can help with general uptime. As Stun is about to begin, use her EX Special or Ultimate to enter the Spotless state, activate Moonlight Lullaby, and if applicable, maintain Weeping Cradle’s buff for the burst. Since Weeping Cradle lasts 3s, there’s a 2.5s gap between it and the Bangboos leaving, so having Rina use her skills as late as possible is best, to ensure that as much of the stun duration is covered by the buff effect. Once done, the cycle repeats, with skill expression manifesting in attempts to maintain as much uptime of the buff as possible in the out-of-stun period.","pros":"Standard Agent that’s easy to get and can work as a competitive support pick for most Attackers. Has especially good compatibility with many of the better Support W-Engines, having easier maintenance than many of her peers. PEN Ratio from her buffs is a mostly unsaturated stat that can be further enhanced by building Agents with a matching D5. 2 years since her release, and she’s still the record holder.","cons":"Even after her Potential Awakening, she is still reliant on M1 to get full value out of her buff, as she doesn’t have enough resources to maintain it at all times. Her Signature is important to get full value out of her PEN Ratio buff, and can feel reliant on its dupes to keep up with other limited Supports. Anti-synergises with DEF Shred, making her be a less effective Agent in some team comps. Hard to tell if her cooking is food or a Lovecraftian eldritch abomination.","teams":[{"m":"Claret + Roxy + Rina + Plugboo","c":"","r":"Rank 9"},{"m":"Claret + Koleda + Rina + Plugboo","c":"","r":"Rank 12"},{"m":"Claret + Norma + Rina + Ultra Jake","c":"","r":"Rank 13"}]},"Jane Doe":{"slug":"jane-doe","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Dancing Blades","d":"Press to activate: Unleashes up to six consecutive attacks ahead, dealing Physical DMG. The sixth Basic Attack is also treated as a Dash Attack, and Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["1st-Hit: 36.1%","2nd-Hit: 62.3%","3rd-Hit: 83.5%","4th-Hit: 163.4%","5th-Hit: 98.8%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Passion","d":"When Jane triggers Perfect Dodge, Defensive Assist, or performs a move that deals DMG to the enemy, she accumulates Passion Stream. Upon reaching the maximum Passion Stream, Jane enters the Passion state. While in the Passion state, Jane\u0027s Physical Anomaly Buildup Rate is increased by 25%. Additionally, if Jane\u0027s Anomaly Proficiency exceeds 120, each extra point raises her ATK by 2, up to a maximum of 600. In the Passion state, Jane\u0027s skills that deal damage consume Passion Stream. Activating a Perfect Dodge or Defensive Assist regenerates Passion Stream. Jane exits the Passion state when all of her Passion Stream is consumed.","m":[]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Salchow Jump","d":"Entering the Passion state grants Jane one use of Basic Attack: Salchow Jump. When available, hold to activate: Launch rapid consecutive attacks forward, followed by a Finishing Move, dealing Physical DMG. Hold the button during the consecutive attacks to greatly extend the skill duration. Release to trigger the Finishing Move early. Anti-Interrupt level is increased during the consecutive attacks, and Jane takes 40% reduced DMG. Jane is invulnerable during the Finishing Move, which can also trigger a Perfect Dodge upon activation. If a Perfect Dodge is triggered, the Finishing Move restores more Passion Stream on hit. Using and damaging an enemy with Basic Attack: Salchow Jump while in the Passion state generates Passion Stream.","m":["Consecutive Attack: 482.1%","Finishing Move: 161.3%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Aerial Sweep","d":"Press to activate. Leaps into the air to launch consecutive kicks forward, then sweeps across, dealing Physical DMG. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["57.8%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Aerial Sweep - Clearout","d":"With enough Energy, press to activate: Leaps into the air to launch multiple consecutive kicks forward, then sweeps across, dealing massive Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill, which also counts as a Dash Attack.","m":["574.7%","Energy Cost: 60%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Phantom","d":"Press to activate. A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. Jane has an extra dodge. Before she enters the Passion state, she alternates between the two dodges. After entering the Passion state, Jane can pass through enemies in front when dodging.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Edge Jump","d":"Press during a dodge to activate. If after the first dodge, launch an upward slash in front, dealing Physical DMG. If after the second dodge, perform a consecutive slashes in front, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["1st-Dodge: 71.5%","2nd-Dodge: 71.5%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Phantom Thrust","d":"While in the Passion state, press during a dodge to activate: Launch three quick rushing slashes in front, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["104.5%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Swift Shadow","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. If after the first dodge, unleash multiple slashes at enemies in front, followed by a downward thrust, dealing Physical DMG. If after the second dodge, leap up and deliver three consecutive attacks to enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1st-Dodge: 341.2%","2nd-Dodge: 341.2%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Swift Shadow Dance","d":"While in the Passion state, press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Slash enemies in front quickly multiple times, dealing Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["387%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Flowers of Sin","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Weaves between and slashes enemies in a large area in front, dealing massive Physical DMG. Jane directly enters the Passion state upon activating the skill, and gains max Passion Stream. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["632.6%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Final Curtain","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate. Weaves between and slashes enemies with a powerful attack in a large area in front, followed by a Finishing Move, dealing massive Physical DMG. Jane directly enters the Passion state upon activating the skill, and gains max Passion Stream. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1470.6%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Dark Thorn","d":"When the on-field character is launched, press to activate. Unleash multiple slashes at enemies in front, followed by a downward thrust, dealing Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["119.2%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Lutz Jump","d":"While in the Passion state, when the on-field character is launched, press to activate: Slash enemies in front quickly multiple times, dealing Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["137.5%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Last Defense","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, inflicting massive Daze. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Gale Sweep","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate. Leap up and swiftly slash the enemy, then execute a wide sweeping slash across a large area in front, dealing Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["345.5%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Aerial Sweep - Onslaught","d":"While in the Passion state and with enough Energy, press to activate: Leaps into the air to launch multiple consecutive kicks forward, then sweeps across, dealing massive Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill, which also counts as a Dash Attack.","m":["595.1%","Energy Cost: 60%"]}],"build":{"w":["Sharpened Stinger","Practiced Perfection","Weeping Gemini","Rainforest Gourmet"],"a":["Fanged Metal, Freedom Blues","Fanged Metal, Phaethon\u0027s Melody","Fanged Metal, Chaos Jazz","Fanged Metal, Feathered Fate"],"core":7,"st":[["CRIT Rate",13],["CRIT DMG",66],["ATK",2623]]},"how":"Jane has 2 distinct playstyles: an on-field main DPS one and a supportive one. When playing her as an on-fielder, getting as many Dodge Counters as possible is the priority. The combination of high Anomaly build-up and the bonus to Passion Stream gets her into Passion State quickly, and then once in it, it’s one of the ways that she can maintain it in spite of attacks constantly draining it. Getting Salchow Jump’s Perfect Dodge bonus is especially important if running low, as it can generate a significant amount of the gauge between its regular spinning hits, Perfect Dodge and the extra gain on the Finishing Move. Although Jane’s EX is very strong, it’s better reserved to the Passion State, and ideally for in-stun combos, as without Dodge Counters to boost her build-up, it’s one of her primary ways of applying Anomaly quickly. Getting as many Assaults (and Vortexes) in stun is how she gets the most damage. Jane’s supportive playstyle is often the way to go when pairing her with Physical Anomaly Agents. In these, Jane may not be on-field as often, but it’s important that she gets at least one strike in on enemies every 10 seconds to maintain the Gnawed state, ensuring that Assaults CRIT and its duration is at a high 15 seconds. Her approach in these comps would be to get an early Passion State, then maintain it with occasional Defensive Assists and swap-ins for Dodge Counters while other Agents go through longer animations in their attacks. She can be especially useful to trigger Anomalies midway through skills, like if run with Alice when she does a Starshine Waltz. Given the strength of Jane’s Chain Attacks, it can still be worth using over that of other Anomaly Agents depending on the circumstance, especially as the restoration of her Passion State helps ensure that she’s always at max self-buffs to avoid diluting Physical Anomalies. Regardless of how she’s played, Jane is a valuable Physical Anomaly Agent, and her ability to give CRITs to Assaults is incredibly powerful, especially at M2+.","pros":"Low skill floor with high skill ceiling, with 3 Dodges and a simple game plan, but rewarding for those who maintain her Passion State. Her ability to make all Assaults from her team\u0027s CRIT give her absurdly good synergy with Physical and Wind Anomaly Agents. Has some of the best early vertical in the game, with her M2 being one of the greatest uplifts of any Agent. Gaps every other character in Random Play Store Membership Value.","cons":"Managing Passion State is highly dependent on enemy aggression, as is her Anomaly Build-up when low on resources… …which isn’t helped by the fact Physical has higher Anomaly threshold requirements, and late finishers on her Basics mean it’s easy to overcap on build-up. Even after Potential Unlock, her Signature W-Engine can be frustrating to upkeep in many comps that have other Agents be demanding of field-time. Why is -insert future Physical Anomaly Agent/mechanic/multiplier- gimped? Jane, that’s why.","teams":[{"m":"Remielle + Jane Doe + Velina + Ariel","c":"","r":"Rank 8"},{"m":"Jane Doe + Velina + Yuzuha + Ultra Jake","c":"","r":"Rank 43"},{"m":"Remielle + Jane Doe + Burnice + Ariel","c":"","r":"Rank 50"}]},"Dialyn":{"slug":"dialyn","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Happy to Be of Service","d":"Press to activate: Unleashes up to four attacks, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["1st-Hit: 25.6%","2nd-Hit: 51.3%","3rd-Hit: 64.8%","4th-Hit: 99.5%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Rock, Paper, Scissors","d":"After EX Special Attack: Rock or EX Special Attack: Scissors, press to activate: Performs up to two attacks, dealing Physical DMG. During skill activation, Anti-Interrupt level increases, and DMG taken is reduced by 40%.","m":["1st-Hit: 89.5%","2nd-Hit: 113.9%","3rd-Hit: 103.1%","4th-Hit: 100.3%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Get Lost!","d":"With Customer Complaint, hold to activate. Delivers a forward martial salute attack. On activation, it consumes 1 Customer Complaint and deals Physical DMG. On activation, the previous character\u0027s Quick Assist is triggered. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["549.7%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Welcome Gesture","d":"Press to activate. Throws dual rings to slash enemies, dealing Physical DMG. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["54.2%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Rock","d":"With enough Energy, press to activate: Launches a fist attack, dealing Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["404%","Energy Cost: 25%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Scissors","d":"With enough Energy, press to activate: Launches a scissors attack, dealing Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["524.9%","Energy Cost: 25%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Paper!","d":"With enough Energy, press to activate: Launches a paper attack, dealing Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["701.7%","Energy Cost: 25%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Line Busy","d":"Press to activate. A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Sudden Call","d":"Press during a dodge to activate: Launches a dashing attack at enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["60.5%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Number Unavailable","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Launches consecutive attacks against enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG. After using this skill, can immediately follow up with the 4th hit of Basic Attack: Happy to Be of Service. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["267.3%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Welcome Mat","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Launches consecutive kicks against enemies in front, dealing massive Physical DMG. After using this skill, can immediately follow up with the 4th hit of Basic Attack: Happy to Be of Service. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["620.4%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Service Stopped for Number Dialed","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate: Rushes forward and performs a finger flick attack, dealing massive Physical DMG. After using this skill, can immediately follow up with the 4th hit of Basic Attack: Happy to Be of Service. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1622.5%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Forward Call","d":"When the active character is launched, press to activate. Launches consecutive attacks against enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG. After using this skill, can immediately follow up with the 4th hit of Basic Attack: Happy to Be of Service. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["121%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. This skill excels at parrying enemy attacks and reduces the consumption of Assist Points when the character is under intense attacks. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Back-to-Back Calls","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate: Performs a rapid dash followed by a slash attack, dealing Physical DMG. After using this skill, can immediately follow up with the 4th hit of Basic Attack: Happy to Be of Service. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["376.4%"]}],"build":{"w":["Yesterday Calls","Hellfire Gears","Steam Oven","Precious Fossilized Core"],"a":["King of the Summit, Woodpecker Electro","King of the Summit, Moonlight Lullaby","King of the Summit, Swing Jazz","King of the Summit, Shockstar Disco"],"core":6.99,"st":[["CRIT Rate",96],["CRIT DMG",96],["ATK",2374]]},"how":"Dialyn is a very flexible Agent: she can be played mostly on-field or off-field, so long as you are able to sustain the Energy generation she needs to build Positive Reviews for every stun. In simple terms, all that one needs to do is make sure to cast at least one full string of her regular EX Special, so Rock, Scissors and Paper. Landing Paper is very important, as that is how her Stun DMG Multiplier increase and duration extension are applied. The earlier she uses an EX Special, the better, as that applies her Overwhelmingly Positive 40% DMG Bonus buff to the whole team. As you can stagger her EX Special casts 8 seconds apart, it\u0027s perfectly fine to use an EX Special despite not having the full 75 Energy required for all 3 consecutively, as long as enough can be built before the timer runs out after each cast. Once all buffs are up and debuffs are applied, you would split your focus between building enough resources on your main damage dealer (such as Zhu Yuan shotshells, Evelyn Burning Embers, Yixuan Technique Points, etc.) and making sure that Dialyn gets 90 Positive Reviews in time for stun. With her Signature W-Engine, she can be mostly kept off-field for its Energy Regeneration bonus and brought in occasionally for EX Specials. Without it, you may need to make use of her alternate Basics between EX Specials to have enough resources. Once Stun begins, make sure to use one of the attacks that can trigger the Ultimate conversion to use up her Positive Reviews and go into a stun burst combo. The easiest way to achieve this is usually do: Trigger a Chain Attack with any character Chain Attack on Dialyn Chain Attack to your damage dealer (this is upgraded/converted into an Ultimate) The more optimal way of initiating stuns though, is through: Hold Basic for EX Special: Get Lost! Chain Attack to your damage dealer (this is upgraded/converted to an Ultimate) Chain Attack on a second character Chain Attack on your main damage dealer As Ultimates don\u0027t count as Chain Attacks, this allows for you to get both an Ultimate conversion and still get your damage dealer\u0027s Chain Attack off! After the stun ends, it\u0027s rinse and repeat. Don\u0027t take too long between EX Specials to maintain her 40% DMG Bonus, apply her debuffs with Paper, and keep a close eye on Dialyn\u0027s resources so that you have enough Positive Reviews before every stun.","pros":"Her Ultimate conversion mechanic is meta-defining, being absurdly strong in its value offering. Allows for better combo routes on many teams owing to her stun duration extension. Well-rounded buff offering, making her less susceptible to stat saturation. Some of the highest Daze build in the entire game, being a competitive option even against Physical resistant enemies. Enables the use of Puffer Electro 4-piece for most Attackers, making them easier to build and play. Will help you pick up your phone.","cons":"Does not gain much Daze from most weapons, being reliant on her Signature W-Engine for the best routes. Steep CRIT Rate requirements mean she can be demanding regarding Drive Disc substat counts. Forwards to voicemail way too quickly.","teams":[{"m":"Ye Shunguang + Dialyn + Sunna + Sprout","c":"","r":"Rank 4"},{"m":"Ye Shunguang + Dialyn + Zhao + Sprout","c":"","r":"Rank 5"},{"m":"Yixuan + Dialyn + Lucia + Belion","c":"","r":"Rank 7"}]},"Yuzuha":{"slug":"ukinami-yuzuha","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Tanuki Claws","d":"Press to activate: Unleashes up to 5 strikes ahead, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["1st-Hit: 37.7%","2nd-Hit: 57.7%","3rd-Hit: 66%","4th-Hit: 98.1%","5th-Hit: 164.1%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Tanuki Cloak","d":"Hold to activate: Enter a defensive stance for up to 1.5 seconds. If hit during this time, parry the attack and inflict massive Daze against the attacking enemy. Successfully parrying an attack grants 1 Sugar Points. Character is invulnerable when successfully parrying.","m":["0%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Hard Candy Shot","d":"When Yuzuha has Sugar Points, landing a hit with other active characters\u0027 attacks will have Yuzuha continuously twirl her umbrella and attack centered around the target before launching a powerful shell, dealing Physical DMG. When this attack lands a heavy attack, Yuzuha consumes 1 Sugar Point. Basic Attack: Hard Candy Shot is considered an Aftershock. Basic Attack: Hard Candy Shot can be triggered once every 8s. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["132%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Sugarburst Sparkles","d":"Enemies under the effect of Sweet Scare will be attacked by a Basic Attack: Sugarburst Sparkles once every 1s. Basic Attack: Sugarburst Sparkles initially deals Physical DMG. Basic Attack: Sugarburst Sparkles does not contribute its accumulated Attribute Anomaly Buildup toward Anomaly DMG calculation. Basic Attack: Sugarburst Sparkles Anomaly Buildup Rate increases.","m":["27.5%","Anomaly Buildup Rate Increase: 8.5%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Sugarburst Sparkles - Max","d":"Enemies affected by Sweet Scare will be attacked by a Basic Attack: Sugarburst Sparkles - Max when hit with a heavy attack from Basic Attack: Hard Candy Shot or Assist Follow-Up: Stuffed Hard Candy Shot. Basic Attack: Sugarburst Sparkles - Max initially deals Physical DMG. Basic Attack: Sugarburst Sparkles - Max does not contribute its accumulated Attribute Anomaly Buildup toward Anomaly DMG calculation. Basic Attack: Sugarburst Sparkles - Max Anomaly Buildup Rate increases.","m":["308%","Anomaly Buildup Rate Increase: 8.5%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Tanuki Helper","d":"When Yuzuha is off-field, tanuki Kama assists the active character in attacking enemies, dealing Physical DMG. When Yuzuha performs Basic Attack: Tanuki Cloak, tanuki Kama joins her in attacking the enemy, dealing Physical DMG. Tanuki Kama inherits Yuzuha\u0027s initial ATK.","m":["Tanuki Kama \u0026 Yuzuha Coordinated Attack: 110%","Tanuki Kama Auto-Attack: 110%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Gummy Bombardment","d":"Press to activate. Fire a cannon shot forward, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["50.5%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Cavity Alert","d":"With enough Energy, press to activate. Throw a bomb at the enemy, dealing Physical DMG; Upon hitting an enemy with a heavy attack, it inflicts the [Sweet Scare] state; Gain 2 [Sugar Points] upon activation; A [Quick Assist] is triggered when this skill hits an enemy; Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["421%","Energy Cost: 60%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Cavity Alert, Right Now!","d":"After using [Dodge Counter: Time for Payback~], [Quick Assist: Dessert Time], [Assist Follow-Up: We Have Cookies], or [Assist Follow-Up: Stuffed Hard Candy Shot], or when a [Perfect Dodge] is triggered, press to activate. Quickly throw a bomb at the enemy, dealing Physical DMG; On hitting an enemy with a heavy attack, it inflicts the [Sweet Scare] state; Gain 2 [Sugar Points] upon activation; A [Quick Assist] is triggered when this skill hits an enemy; Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["241.4%","Energy Cost: 60%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Sweet Scare","d":"The Sweet Scare state lasts for specified duration, repeated triggers reset the duration. When an enemy affected by Sweet Scare is first hit by an active character using an attack of their attribute, Flavor Match is triggered against that enemy, changing the attribute of Basic Attack: Sugarburst Sparkles and Basic Attack: Sugarburst Sparkles - Max against that enemy to match that of the character who triggered Flavor Match. When Sweet Scare is triggered again on an enemy, their existing Flavor Match state is removed. The process can be repeated to change the attribute of Basic Attack: Sugarburst Sparkles and Basic Attack: Sugarburst Sparkles - Max again.","m":["Duration: 18%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Did I Scare You?","d":"Press to activate. A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: You\u0027re Outta Luck!","d":"Press during a dodge to activate: Rapidly strikes enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["69.8%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Time for Payback~","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Deliver a quick strike forward, dealing Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["276.9%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Prank Assault","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Unleash a powerful strike on enemies in a small area ahead, dealing massive Physical DMG; Gain 1 Sugar Points when used; A Quick Assist is triggered when this skill hits an enemy; Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["598.7%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Surrender or Suffer the Mischief","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate. Unleash a powerful strike on enemies in a large area around the character, dealing massive Physical DMG; Enemies hit with a heavy attack are inflicted with the Sweet Scare state; Upon activating this skill, other squad members gain Energy; Upon activating this skill, gain 2 Sugar Points; A Quick Assist is triggered when this skill hits an enemy; Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1443.2%","Other Squad Members\u0027 Energy Gain: 8.5%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Dessert Time","d":"When the active character is launched, press to activate. Strike enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["112.9%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Replenish Your Fun","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. Upon a successful parry, gain 1 Sugar Points; Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: We Have Cookies","d":"After triggering a Defensive Assist or successfully parrying an enemy attack with Basic Attack: Tanuki Cloak, press activate: Strike enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["294.3%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Stuffed Hard Candy Shot","d":"After triggering a Defensive Assist or successfully parrying an enemy attack with Basic Attack: Tanuki Cloak, press at the right moment to activate: Following a continuous spinning umbrella attack, fire a powerful projectile that deals Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["463.6%"]}],"build":{"w":["Metanukimorphosis","Kaboom the Cannon","Weeping Cradle","Thoughtbop"],"a":["Moonlight Lullaby, Phaethon\u0027s Melody","Astral Voice, Phaethon\u0027s Melody","Swing Jazz, Phaethon\u0027s Melody","Phaethon\u0027s Melody, Swing Jazz, Flex"],"core":7,"st":[["CRIT Rate",15],["CRIT DMG",69],["ATK",3062]]},"how":"Rotations For more information on Yuzuha\u0027s kit and how to exploit her best, we strongly recommend reading our Review which goes in full detail on her mechanics. Fundamentally speaking, Yuzuha is an extremely simple character to use, who mostly operates from off-field, occasionally swapping in at least once every 40s to keep 100% uptime on her buffs. However, keep in mind swapping her in to trigger Quick Assists may be more frequent when using Astral Voice to ensure uptime on the Disk Drive set effect as well. Yuzuha has 2 main combos, both starting with a Defensive Assist or Parry which are extremely easy to trigger in various situations: Starting with Parry This combo is best if Yuzuha cannot readily trigger a Perfect Assist and needs to be switched on-field, anticipating an enemy attack in the process. Basic Attack: Tanuki Cloak (trigger Parry) Assist Follow-Up: Stuffed Hard Candy Shot EX Special: Cavity Alert, Right Now! OR Ultimate Quick Assist is activated (switch out). Starting with Perfect Assist This combo is best to execute when an enemy uses an attack that can be reacted with using a Defensive Assist, and Yuzuha needs to step in to refresh her buff count/use her Ultimate (keep in mind choosing to Perfect Dodge with your on-field DPS Agent may be preferred in certain teams while Yuzuha\u0027s buff is still up — combos must always be considered within a team context). Defensive Assist: Replenish your Fun Assist Follow-Up: Stuffed Hard Candy Shot EX Special: Cavity Alert, Right Now! OR Ultimate Quick Assist is activated (switch out). Remember Yuzuha\u0027s Assist Follow-Up can\u0027t be mashed — it needs to be activated at a specific timing to be most efficient. Additionally, please keep in mind that with Yuzuha, Chain Attacks are appreciated to generate extra Sugar Points as well as contribute to team Decibel generation at the same time. Whenever a Stun is triggered, ensure Yuzuha gets her Chain Attack (hence full team Chain Attacks will be privileged, without the Bangboo of course).","pros":"The biggest buffs to Anomaly Agents out of any Support while retaining good personal damage and Daze, and even restoring Energy; Super easy to operate - mostly functions off-field, and features a simple parry mechanic; Low reliance on her Signature W-Engine, almost at full performance with F2P-friendly options; Not just good in Anomaly teams — most often the second-best Support choice even outside of Anomaly compositions, only behind Astra Yao; 10/10 character design - addicted to sugar, she\u0027s just like me for real.","cons":"All skills are worth levelling except for Dodge — costly in terms of skill materials; The quality of character designs is making nearly every banner impossible to skip, and this needs to stop (it doesn\u0027t).","teams":[{"m":"Miyabi + Nangong Yu + Yuzuha + Biggest Fan","c":"","r":"Rank 2"},{"m":"Miyabi + Vivian + Yuzuha + Robin","c":"","r":"Rank 19"},{"m":"Promeia + Nangong Yu + Yuzuha + Biggest Fan","c":"","r":"Rank 26"}]},"Caesar":{"slug":"caesar","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Rampaging Slash","d":"Press to activate: Unleashes up to 6 slashes ahead, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["1st-Hit: 47.2%","2nd-Hit: 40.9%","3rd-Hit: 148.3%","3rd-Hit (ALT): 118.4%","4th-Hit: 78.8%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Dead End","d":"When there are sufficient Assist Points, hold to activate: Consume 1 Assist Point to toss the shield and attack nearby enemies in all directions, dealing Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["126.3%","Assist Point Cost: 1%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Shockwave Shield Bash","d":"Press to activate. Strike forward with the shield, dealing Physical DMG. If Caesar is hit by an enemy at the beginning of the skill activation, it will trigger a Perfect Block, negating the damage once and automatically following up with a Special Attack: Roaring Thrust. After using the skill, Caesar enters a guard stance, reducing incoming damage by 40%. When attacked by an enemy Caesar blocks with the shield and gets slightly knocked back. Press or to trigger Retaliation, activating Special Attack: Roaring Thrust or EX Special Attack: Overpowered Shield Bash. When Retaliation is triggered, Caesar is invulnerable while using the skill.","m":["53.3%","[Perfect Block]: 0%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Roaring Thrust","d":"After activating Special Attack: Shockwave Shield Bash, press to activate: Thrusts forward, dealing Physical DMG. If Perfect Block or Retaliation is not triggered, the Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill. Character is invulnerable while using this skill when Perfect Block or Retaliationis triggered.","m":["58.8%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Parry Counter","d":"With enough energy, press to activate: Strikes forward with the shield, followed by a powerful thrust, dealing massive Physical DMG. If Caesar is hit by an enemy at the beginning of the skill activation or a Interrupt is triggered with the shield strike, it will trigger Perfect Block, negating incoming damage once and countering with a shield bash. After triggering Perfect Block, press to activate EX Special Attack: Overpowered Shield Bash without consuming energy. After using the skill, Caesar enters a guard stance, reducing incoming damage by 40%. When attacked by an enemy, Caesar blocks the attack and is slightly knocked back. Press or to trigger Retaliation and activate Special Attack: Roaring Thrust or EX Special Attack: Overpowered Shield Bash. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["387.2%","[Perfect Block]: 0%","[Perfect Block] Counter: 387.2%","Energy Cost per second: 40%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Overpowered Shield Bash","d":"After activating EX Special Attack: Parry Counter, with enough energy, press to activate: Strikes forward with the shield, dealing massive Physical DMG. If Caesar is hit by an enemy at the beginning of the skill activation or a Interrupt is triggered with a shield strike, it will trigger Perfect Block, negating incoming damage once and recovering the Energy used to activate the skill. When the skill is activated through Perfect Block or Retaliation, Perfect Block cannot be triggered again. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["425.7%","[Perfect Block]: 0%","Activation Energy Cost: 20%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Stance Switch","d":"When Caesar triggers a Perfect Block, Retaliation, or Defensive Assist, her impact is increased for 3s.","m":["Impact Increase: 9%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Adrift","d":"Press to activate. A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Hog Rush","d":"While dodging, press to activate. Strikes forward with the shield, dealing Physical DMG. During skill activation, damage taken is reduced by 40%. When attacked by an enemy Caesar blocks with the shield and gets slightly knocked back. Press or to trigger Retaliation and activate Special Attack: Roaring Thrust or EX Special Attack: Overpowered Shield Bash.","m":["62.3%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Eye For an Eye","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Slashes enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["193.5%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Road Rage Slam","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Unleashes a powerful downward strike at enemies ahead, dealing massive Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["638.8%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Savage Smash","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate. Tosses the shield forward, unleashing a powerful spinning attack on enemies in front, followed by a downward strike, dealing massive Physical DMG. When hitting shielded enemies, the Daze dealt is increased. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["2012.3%","Daze Increase: 45%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Lane Change","d":"When the on-field character is launched, press to activate. Slashes enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["64.2%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Aegis Shield","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, inflicting massive Daze. This skill excels at parrying enemy attacks and reduces the consumption of Assist Points when the character is under intense attacks. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Aiding Blade","d":"After activating Defensive Assist, press to activate: Tosses the shield forward, unleashing a powerful spinning attack on enemies in front, followed by a slash that deals Physical DMG. After activating the skill, press or or to trigger a Retaliation, activating Special Attack: Roaring Thrust or EX Special Attack: Overpowered Shield Bash. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["407.2%"]}],"build":{"w":["Tusks of Fury","Reel Projector","Precious Fossilized Core","Tremor Trigram Vessel"],"a":["Proto Punk, Shockstar Disco","Bunny in Wonderland, Shockstar Disco","Bunny in Wonderland, King of the Summit","Proto Punk, Swing Jazz"],"core":6.92,"st":[["CRIT Rate",46],["CRIT DMG",107],["ATK",2170]]},"how":"Caesar’s goal in battle is to maintain her Core Passive and Additional Ability at all times while inflicting as much Daze as possible in as little field time as possible. Fortunately, all of this can be achieved easily via two simple combos. Note that whenever Caesar\u0027s Ultimate is available and the enemy is out of Stun, that is the best time to use her Ultimate (include it after all of the other actions in the combos below have been performed before switching out). It\u0027s also possible to use Caesar\u0027s Ultimate in the middle of a Stun window if she is built for high damage, but in most teams it will be preferable to spend that time dealing damage with your DPS Agents while Caesar provides extra Daze with her Ultimate. Defensive Assist Core Combo: Enemy Attacks while Caesar is not on field, Quick-Swap to Caesar, Defensive Assist: Aegis Shield (Activates Additional Ability: Battle Spirit), Assist Follow-Up: Aiding Blade (Gain Retaliation), EX Special Attack: Overpowered Shield Bash (Activates Core Ability: Radiant Aegis), Swap Back to Main Field Character of choice. This combo is her strongest - as it activates both her Core Passive and Additional Ability, takes minimal field time, deals tremendous Daze per second at cost of 1 Assist Point and 20 Energy, making it consistent and economical to execute in most scenarios. This combo is suitable when playing her as a Support or as a Stunner alongside teammates who are more hungry for field time.Alternatively if the enemy isn’t attacking or you wish to make use of Defensive Assist on other characters the following combo can be used: Non-Defensive Assist Combo: EX Special Attack: Parry Counter (Activates Core Ability: Radiant Aegis) EX Special Attack: Overpowered Shield Bash Basic Attack: Dead End (Activates Additional Ability: Battle Spirit) This combo can be utilized anytime and doesn\u0027t rely on enemies attacking into a Defensive Assist making it useful in a pinch and for teams that prefer triggering Defensive Assist on other characters. However, unlike the Defensive Assist combo, this combo is much easier to time and land a Perfect Block with, and if done, you can skip using Basic Attack - Dead End as the Perfect Block will apply the Additional Ability instead, saving an Assist Point and field time.If Caesar is approaching maximum Energy it’s recommended you execute a quick Double EX Special Attack combo for extra Daze to ensure you don’t waste resources as long as it doesn’t interrupt your team\u0027s game plan. EX Special Attack: Parry Counter EX Special Attack: Overpowered Shield Bash At all times whenever possible","pros":"Huge refreshable Shield that grants Interruption Resistance on the active Agent; That same Shield gives a flat 1000 ATK buff to the equipper; Applies a DMG Taken debuff upon using certain abilities with her Additional Ability which is easy to activate and maintain; Great Daze potential for a Support — contributes well to stunning enemies more often; Highly flexible, functions in several teams as a general buffer, shielder \u0026 hybrid stunner; Has one of the best EP songs in the franchise (objectively speaking of course).","cons":"Highly reliant on executing Perfect Assists to apply Daze and her DMG Taken debuff. Will require players to learn boss patterns \u0026 timings to make the full use of her kit; Really bad W-Engine options due to all of her utility scaling off of Impact, often choosing to run W-Engines from the Stun class solely for their Impact boost; Her Shield only buffs the active Agent. This is severely impactful as lots of Agents operate from off-field and she cannot give the ATK buff to them. By extension, can’t apply the ATK buff to any Swap Cancelled abilities. This severely impacts her value in the meta as a damage buffer, not to mention recent Stun Agents also started providing strong party-wide buffs as well while simply inflicting higher Daze than Caesar.","teams":[{"m":"Ye Shunguang + Caesar + Zhao + Sprout","c":"","r":"Rank 136"},{"m":"Yixuan + Lucia + Caesar + Resonaboo","c":"","r":"Rank 230"},{"m":"Ye Shunguang + Dialyn + Caesar + Sprout","c":"","r":"Rank 280"}]},"Seed":{"slug":"seed","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Chrysanthemum Wheel Dance","d":"Press to activate: Perform up to 4 attacks forward, dealing Physical DMG for the first two hits and Electric DMG for the third and fourth hits. When attacked between the retreat of the 3rd hit to before the 4th hit, triggers an automatic dodge.","m":["1st-Hit: 46.5%","2nd-Hit: 124.1%","3rd-Hit: 71.8%","4th-Hit: 358.6%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Falling Petals - Slaughter","d":"After the 4th hit of a Basic Attack, Dodge Counter, Quick Assist, or Assist Follow-Up, hold or press to activate: Summon the mech to perform a charged punch attack, dealing massive Electric DMG. When Steel Charge reaches 120, gain one chance to quickly activate Basic Attack: Falling Petals - Slaughter by holding . This effect expires when Steel Charge is less than 120 or after using the method above to activate Basic Attack: Falling Petals - Slaughter once. Does not accumulate Steel Charge on hit. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["166.6%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Falling Petals - Downfall","d":"Seed has Steel Charge, which she can accumulate by hitting enemies with her skills. Steel Charge has a maximum value of 150, and an initial value of 60. Upon reaching 120 Steel Charge and triggering Basic Attack: Falling Petals - Slaughter or Ultimate: Clockwork Garden - Bloom!, press or hold to consume 60 Steel Charge and unleash Basic Attack: Falling Petals - Downfall First Form, then automatically consume 60 Steel Charge to follow up with Basic Attack: Falling Petals - Downfall Second Form. Pilots the mech to fire sweeping shots and perform a jumping smash, dealing massive Electric DMG. Does not accumulate Steel Charge on hit. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Downfall First Form: 528.3%","Downfall Second Form: 989.4%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Withered in Frost","d":"Press to activate. Throw a steel wheel that traces a curved path, dealing Electric DMG.","m":["47.7%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Raining Iron Petals","d":"With enough Energy, press to activate. Enter flight mode, where Seed can move in four directions, and unleash a continuous barrage of missiles, dealing massive Electric DMG. Hold to extend the barrage duration while continuously consuming Energy. During flight, release to trigger EX Special Attack: Raining Iron Petals - Away. Upon consuming 60 Energy points in one flight, automatically trigger Basic Attack: Falling Petals - Slaughter. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["683.4%","Initial Cost: 10%","Barrage Cost: 5%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Raining Iron Petals - Away","d":"During EX Special Attack: Raining Iron Petals, release to activate: Unleash rapid cannon fire, dealing Electric DMG Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["18.4%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Running on Petals","d":"Press to activate. A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Magnetic Wheel Dance","d":"Press during a dodge to activate: Throw steel wheels forward, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["64.2%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Blossom Burst","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Unleash a barrage of lasers at enemies in front, dealing Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["320.1%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Tempest of Frosty Petals","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Summons her mech for protection, then launches cannon shots and a barrage of missiles, dealing massive Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["734.2%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Clockwork Garden - Bloom!","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate. Seed will pilot the mech personally, raining down missiles and a meteor shower of rockets, then performing a jumping smash, dealing massive Electric DMG. After using this skill, accumulate 60 Steel Charge. Does not accumulate Steel Charge on hit. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["3249.7%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Barrage of Raining Flowers","d":"When the active character is launched, press to activate. Unleash a barrage of lasers at enemies in front, dealing Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["154%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Sprouting Barrier","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Crimson Core Burst","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate: Unleash continuous floating turret attacks at enemies ahead, dealing Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["456%"]}],"build":{"w":["Cordis Germina","Marcato Desire","The Brimstone","Heartstring Nocturne"],"a":["Dawn\u0027s Bloom, Woodpecker Electro","Dawn\u0027s Bloom, Branch \u0026 Blade Song","Astral Voice, Branch \u0026 Blade Song","Dawn\u0027s Bloom, Puffer Electro"],"core":7,"st":[["CRIT Rate",77],["CRIT DMG",166],["ATK",3026]]},"how":"Balancing Seed’s field time with that of her Vanguard can be quite difficult, with the amount of time spent on each varying between teams. For most Attack Agents, prioritising Seed tends to be the better option. Try to remain on her and get as many Basic Attacks and Dodge Counters as you can, with emphasis being placed on her regular Basic 4. This is the most efficient way of generating Steel Charge, and with proper management, it is possible to get multiple uses of her Basic Attack: Falling Petals - Downfall (at least 1, often 2) while still building back enough by the time enemies are about to be stunned. Use her EX Special every so often - and especially before Downfalls - as they will be needed to refresh her Dawn’s Bloom 4-piece effect in the out-of-stun period. While doing so, don’t forget to occasionally swap back to the Vanguard for an EX Special cast, both to help supplement Seed’s Steel Charge generation and so as to not drop the Onslaught and Besiege buffs. This buff ticks down even before a fight has begun, so keep a watchful eye on it. The Energy generation she provides to the Vanguard should make it easy to maintain, and given the long animations from Downfall, it’s the perfect opportunity to swap out. In some situations however, such as if run against Electric Resistant enemies or being used for her buffs (e.g. running with Evelyn vs Pompey), then Seed can sit in the back and be played as a quickswap Agent, coming in during the main damage dealer’s downtime to help supplement their Energy and to expend her own Energy on EX Specials to refresh Direct Strike and get enough Steel Charge for a Downfall cast here and there. Other highly demanding on-field damage dealers, like Soldier 0 - Anby, can also work well with this playstyle, where Seed instead can make use of her high damage multipliers for burst in stun as opposed to cycling through multiple Downfalls out of stun. On the topic of stun, Seed’s ideal combo needs 120 Steel Charge and her Ultimate, being: EX Special (Full Channel) before Stun begins, to refresh Dawn’s Bloom 4-piece and help build up to 120 Steel Charge Basic Attack: Falling Petals - Slaughter Basic Attack: Falling Petals - Downfall Swap to the Vanguard and use an EX Special (60 Energy) Stunner Chain Attack, to refresh King of the Summit Seed Chain Attack Cancel Ultimate Basic Attack: Falling Petals - Downfall Swap to the Vanguard and use their Ultimate and/or generic burst The above combo does not need Manual Chain, as the Cancel can be moved up to after Slaughter instead. If using Manual Chain, then it is also possible to","pros":"Plenty of invincibility frames and free dodge mechanics - difficult to get interrupted during combos. Introduces a new team archetype of Dual Attack-Class DPS. Makes niche characters more usable than ever before (e.g Nekomata \u0026 Billy), granting her many potential team partners. Kit contains elements of the Support and DPS, granting her a unique position among the Attack Class.","cons":"Lacking a true dedicated partner at the time of her release - she must take other Attack Agents from their best teams to form her own. Combos aren\u0027t mechanically difficult, but require proper resource management to be effective Must be run alongside another Attack Agent.","teams":[{"m":"Cissia + Seed + Astra Yao + Plugboo","c":"","r":"Rank 20"},{"m":"Cissia + Seed + Trigger + Plugboo","c":"","r":"Rank 30"},{"m":"Seed + Orphie y Magus + Trigger + Mercury","c":"","r":"Rank 88"}]},"Billy ★ Starlight":{"slug":"billy-starlight","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Knight\u0027s Technique","d":"Press to activate: Performs up to four attacks forward, dealing Physical DMG. During the 4th hit, press to use Special Attack: Drive Suppression, reducing HP consumption by 50%. Restores a small amount of HP on hit.","m":["1st-Hit DMG: 50.3%","2nd-Hit DMG: 68%","3rd-Hit DMG: 54.5%","4th-Hit DMG: 206%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Full-Throttle Starlight","d":"With enough Determination, hold to activate: Charges forward on the motorcycle, then fires a laser beam, dealing massive Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1043.2%","Determination Cost: 100%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Drive Suppression","d":"When HP is above 25%, press to activate: Consumes HP equal to 16% of Max HP to summon a motorcycle and swiftly crash into enemies, continuously dealing Physical DMG. If attacked by an enemy as the active character shortly upon activating this skill, triggers a block, negating the attack and restoring 5 Determination. After triggering a block, immediately chains into EX Special Attack: Cool Wheelie. After the skill continues for a while, it automatically chains into EX Special Attack: Cool Wheelie. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["52%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Run Wild","d":"Triggers automatically when Dodge: Through the Galaxy is interrupted: Kicks his motorcycle at enemies, dealing Physical DMG. After using this skill, it can be chained into Dodge Counter: Duel King. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["72.1%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Cool Wheelie","d":"Triggers automatically when Special Attack: Drive Suppression reaches its maximum duration or a block is triggered: Lifts the motorcycle to attack enemies, dealing Physical DMG. On hit, restores an additional 8 Determination. After using this skill, with enough Adrenaline, press or hold to chain into EX Special Attack: Rocking Footwork. After the skill animation ends, automatically chains into Special Attack: Run Wild. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["389.7%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: High-Traction Wheels","d":"With enough Adrenaline, hold to activate: Slams down with the motorcycle, dealing Physical DMG. Restores 30% of Max HP upon activating this skill. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["929.9%","Adrenaline Cost: 60%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Rocking Footwork","d":"After activating EX Special Attack: Cool Wheelie and with enough Adrenaline, press or hold to activate: Uses the motorcycle and hand cannon for a combined attack, dealing Physical DMG. Upon activating this skill, restore 15% of Max HP. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["959%","Adrenaline Cost: 60%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Close Call!","d":"Press to activate: A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Through the Galaxy","d":"During Special Attack: Drive Suppression, drag the / or hold to activate: Drifts with the motorcycle, enabling Perfect Dodges for a brief duration. If a Perfect Dodge is successfully triggered, it immediately chains into Dodge Counter: Afterfire Spin. During this skill, continue dragging the / or holding to continue drifting. During this skill, the duration of Special Attack: Drive Suppression will continue, and upon reaching the maximum duration, it automatically chains into EX Special Attack: Cool Wheelie. If the skill ends early, it automatically chains into Special Attack: Run Wild. Character is briefly invulnerable and Anti-Interrupt Level increases during this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Starlight Retribution","d":"Press during a dodge to activate: Performs a quick forward slash, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["45.1%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Duel King","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate: Fires a blast from his arm cannon, dealing Physical DMG. If this skill is triggered via a Perfect Dodge, hitting an enemy restores 10% of Max HP, and it can be chained into the 4th hit of Basic Attack: Knight\u0027s Technique. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["119.5%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Afterfire Spin","d":"During Dodge: Through the Galaxy, trigger a Perfect Dodge to activate: Spins with the bike to deal Physical DMG to surrounding enemies. After using this skill, it automatically chains into EX Special Attack: Cool Wheelie. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["198.7%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Starlight - Power of Bonds","d":"When the active character is launched, press to activate: Fires a blast from his arm cannon ahead, dealing Physical DMG. When HP is above 25%, this skill is replaced with Special Attack: Drive Suppression. This effect can trigger once every 5s. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["92%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Hero\u0027s Entrance","d":"When the on-field character is about to be attacked, press to activate: Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Villain\u0027s Exit","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate: Kicks the motorcycle at the target, dealing massive Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["229.6%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Knight\u0027s Swagger","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Launches a series of attacks forward, dealing massive Physical DMG. Upon activating this skill, gains 15 Determination. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["662.9%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Starlight Knight Flying Kick","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate: Leaps into the air and delivers a flying kick at the target, dealing massive Physical DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1592.1%"]}],"build":{"w":["Starlight Rider Faceplate","Cauldron of Clarity","Qingming Birdcage","Grill O\u0027Wisp"],"a":["Yunkui Tales, Branch \u0026 Blade Song","Yunkui Tales, Woodpecker Electro","Yunkui Tales, Fanged Metal","Yunkui Tales, White Water Ballad"],"core":7,"st":[["CRIT Rate",65],["CRIT DMG",146],["ATK",2054]]},"how":"Billy’s general gameplan can be summed up as: Look to get as many uses of the Cool Wheelie EX out of stun as possible for everything, be it damage, resources or buffs. Do the above ideally through parries on Drive Suppression or with the alternate Dodge Counter for even better results. As Drive Suppression consumes HP, make use of the regular Basic string and regular Dodge Counters to heal, with an occasional Special use after B4 to reduce its HP cost. Have as much Determination and Adrenaline filled when going into stun, then unload his enhanced Basic, Adrenaline EXs, Chains and Ultimates for the most damage. On top of the above, making use of Defensive Assists to pad out Determination alongside Decibels, as well as being aware of enemy invulnerability phases and Billy’s HP so as to not drop key buffs can be important. A standard combo for Billy would be: Basic Attack: High-Throttle Starlight Swap to another character to trigger a Chain Attack Chain to Billy EX Special: High-Traction Wheels Swap to another character to trigger a Chain Attack Chain to Billy Ultimate EX Special: High-Traction Wheels Basic Attack: High-Throttle Starlight The 2nd enhanced Basic’s exhaust beam would land out of stun, but the first part - which does more damage - should land in full. It’s unlikely that Billy will have all his resources up on every stun, in which case, being flexible with his skill use works best. While High-Traction Wheels is the default Adrenaline EX to fall back on, if there aren’t enough Decibels for an Ultimate, or not enough Adrenaline to fit in 2 EXs, using a Cool Wheelie for damage after his second Chain Attack, then cancelling its recovery with Ultimate can be better. Alternatively, linking into the alternate Adrenaline EX Rocking Footwork can be better if there won’t be time or Determination to get another enhanced Basic. Since Billy takes a long time to cast his enhanced Basic, it’s a good opportunity to swap to other characters to refresh buffs and debuffs - like a Support for Moonlight Lullaby or a Stunner for King of the Summit - and get back to him via a Quick Assist conversion to Drive Suppression to cut out recovery animations. Although he has the standard features of a Rupture unit, Billy has a varied kit that allows him to adapt to different situations, and it\u0027s in learning how to balance out his skill that one can master his gameplay.","pros":"Has both high burst in stun combos and decent out of stun damage via Cool Wheelie, making him uniquely suited to some encounters (e.g. Thrall). High stat saturation from his Core Passive means that his substat distribution is far more forgiving than that of other Rupture Agents. Wide variety of moves, with multiple EXs, Dodge Counters and mobility skills that keep him feeling fresh. Raidā Kikku!","cons":"Massively reliant on a few key teammates, with some of the biggest performance drops out of any Agent yet when not in his best team. Spread out damage across multiple skills, making him expensive to invest in. Reeeeeeeeally long animations, which can feel clunky and cumbersome at times, having strict combo requirements. The closest we’ll ever get to playable Pompey, and yet doesn’t even have Scarlet Engine as a Core Unlock material.","teams":[{"m":"dialyn + lucia","c":"","r":""},{"m":"qingyi, ju-fufu, trigger + lucia","c":"","r":""},{"m":"anby-demara, koleda + pan-yinhu","c":"","r":""}]},"Lucy":{"slug":"lucy","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Lady\u0027s Bat","d":"Press to activate. Strike forward up to 4 times, dealing Physical DMG and Fire DMG. When Lucy uses her fourth Basic Attack, the currently on-field guard boars will launch Guard Boars: Spinning Swing! together.","m":["1st-Hit: 56.6%","2nd-Hit: 77.8%","3rd-Hit: 188.9%","4th-Hit: 272.6%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Guard Boars: To Arms!","d":"In combat, the guard boars will randomly use a baseball bat, boxing gloves, or a slingshot to automatically attack enemies, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["Baseball Bat: 92.5%","Boxing Gloves: 127.5%","Slingshot: 175%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Guard Boars: Spinning Swing!","d":"When Lucy uses the fourth Basic Attack, or when she gains the Cheer On! status, the guard boars will whirl their baseball bats in a continuous motion, dealing Physical DMG to nearby enemies. If the attack cannot be executed immediately, the guard boars will remember the required number of times to execute it.","m":["Spinning Swing: 250%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Solid Hit!","d":"Press to activate: Recall a guard boar and launch it as a Line Drive. The guard boar will cause an explosion upon hitting enemies, or walls, dealing Fire DMG. Hold to activate: Recall a guard boar and launch it as a Fly Ball. The guard boar will cause an explosion upon landing, dealing Fire DMG.","m":["Line Drive: 61.7%","Fly Ball: 69.2%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Home Run!","d":"When enough energy, press to activate. Recall a guard boar and launch it as a Line Drive. The guard boar will cause an explosion upon hitting enemies, or walls, dealing massive Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. When enough energy, hold to activate: Recall a guard boar and launch it as a Fly Ball. The guard boar will cause an explosion upon landing, dealing massive Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. When the skill hits an enemy, it triggers a Quick Assist.","m":["Line Drive: 508.4%","Fly Ball: 536.4%","Energy Cost: 60%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Foul Ball!","d":"Press to dodge. A rapid dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Fearless Boar!","d":"Press during a dodge to activate. Rapidly strikes enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["78.4%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Returning Tusk!","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Strike enemies in front, dealing Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["308%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Grand Slam!","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate. Lucy jumps up and sends a guard boar at enemies in front in a large area, dealing massive Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. When the skill hits an enemy, it triggers a Quick Assist.","m":["161.1%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Walk-Off Home Run!","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate. Launch all guard boards sequentially, dealing massive Fire DMG in a large area to enemies ahead. While using this skill, other squad members recover 10 energy, and the next character to switch in gains an additional 20 energy. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. When the skill hits an enemy, it triggers a Quick Assist.","m":["572.8%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Hit By Pitch!","d":"When the on-field character is launched, press to activate. Strikes enemies in front, dealing Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["160%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Safe on Base!","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Scored a Run!","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate. Strikes enemies in front, dealing Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["349.1%"]}],"build":{"w":["Kaboom the Cannon","Weeping Cradle"],"a":["Moonlight Lullaby, Swing Jazz","Swing Jazz, Hormone Punk","Astral Voice, Swing Jazz","Moonlight Lullaby, Puffer Electro"],"core":7,"st":[["CRIT Rate",44],["CRIT DMG",97],["ATK",2424]]},"how":"$undefined","pros":"Does off-field damage and Daze thanks to her Guard Boars — decent personal damage overall by pure Support standards; Grants the whole squad (along with Bangboos and Guard Boars) a 600 flat ATK buff which is really easy to maintain; Super easy to play, takes minimal field time and only needs to execute 1 ability to access all of her buffs; The embodiment of a generalist character, usable everywhere, with everyone, to an acceptable extent.","cons":"ATK buff is really good with easy maintenance, but falls short of other options that are more technical like Nicole or simply harder to acquire like Astra Yao; Guard Boars sometimes just won’t attack an enemy who’s too fast for them to keep up — Lucy’s age in spite of her small stature seems to affect even her pets…","teams":[{"m":"Ye Shunguang + Lucy + Zhao + Sprout","c":"","r":"Rank 280"},{"m":"Burnice + Velina + Lucy + Ultra Jake","c":"","r":"Rank 388"},{"m":"Phoenix + Velina + Lucy + Rocketboo","c":"","r":"Rank 388"}]},"Zhu Yuan":{"slug":"zhu-yuan","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Don\u0027t Move!","d":"[Assault Mode] Press to activate: Unleash a flurry of martial arts, bullets, and Ether Buckshots in a series of up to 5 attacks, dealing Physical DMG and Ether DMG. When the 4th or 5th hits strike an enemy, obtain 1 Enhanced Shotshell. A max of 1 can be obtained per skill use. While using this skill, drag the stick/joystick and press to activate Dash Attack: Firepower Offensive and readjust to face the selected direction. While under Assault Mode, hold to switch to Suppressive Mode.","m":["1st-Hit: 43.1%","2nd-Hit: 126.4%","3rd-Hit: 137.3%","4th-Hit: 151%","5th-Hit: 162.2%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Please Do Not Resist","d":"[Suppressive Mode] Hold to activate. Unleash up to 3 Shotshell piercing attacks, dealing Physical DMG. If Zhu Yuan has Enhanced Shotshells upon firing, 1 Enhanced Shotshell will be consumed, dealing massive Ether DMG. While using this skill, drag the stick/joystick to activate her Dash Attack: Overwhelming Firepower and readjust to face the selected direction. While in Suppressive Mode, release to return to Assault Mode.","m":["1st-Hit (Physical): 53.7%","2nd-Hit (Physical): 53.7%","3rd-Hit (Physical): 160.9%","1st-Hit (Ether): 135.9%","2nd-Hit (Ether): 135.9%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Buckshot Blast","d":"Press to activate: Shoots Ether Buckshots that deal Ether DMG. This can be repeated 3 times by repeatedly pressing . Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["18.4%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Full Barrage","d":"With enough energy, press to activate: Shoots a series of Ether Buckshots, that explode and deal massive Ether DMG. Upon activation, gain 3 Enhanced Shotshells. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["587.4%","Energy Cost: 60%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Tactical Detour","d":"Press to activate:. A rapid dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Firepower Offensive","d":"[Assault Mode] Press during a dodge to activate: Uses handgun to attack, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["55.1%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Fire Blast ","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Shoots enemies in front with an Ether Buckshot, dealing Ether DMG. Gain 1 Enhanced Shotshell on skill use. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["176.8%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Overwhelming Firepower","d":"Suppressive Mode Drag the joystick/joystickduring Basic Attack: Please Do Not Resist to activate: Unleashes a Shotshell piercing attack, dealing Physical DMG. If Zhu Yuan has Enhanced Shotshells when firing, 1 Enhanced Shotshell will be consumed, dealing massive Ether DMG.","m":["Physical: 53.7%","Ether: 135.9%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Eradication Mode","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Uses Modified Master Firearm to execute a saturated attack, firing lasers and seeking missiles to deal massive Ether DMG. Upon activation, gain 3 Enhanced Shotshells. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["587.5%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Max Eradication Mode","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate. Uses Modified Master Firearm to execute a saturated attack, firing lasers and seeking missiles to deal massive Ether DMG. Upon activation, gain 3 Enhanced Shotshells. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1977.6%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Covering Shot","d":"When the on-field character is launched, press to activate. Shoots enemies in front with an Ether Buckshot, dealing Ether DMG. Gain 1 Enhanced Shotshell on skill use. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["51.4%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Evasive Assist: Guarded Backup","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Dodges the enemy\u0027s attack and activates the Vital View. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Defensive Counter","d":"Press after an Evasive Assist to activate. Attack with a combination of martial arts and shotshells, dealing Physical DMG and Ether DMG. Upon activation, gain 3 Enhanced Shotshells. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["355.8%"]}],"build":{"w":["Riot Suppressor Mark VI","The Brimstone","Cordis Germina","Marcato Desire"],"a":["The Sky Ablaze, Branch \u0026 Blade Song","Chaotic Metal, Woodpecker Electro","The Sky Ablaze, Astral Voice","The Sky Ablaze, Woodpecker Electro"],"core":7,"st":[["CRIT Rate",50],["CRIT DMG",198],["ATK",3349]]},"how":"Zhu Yuan doesn’t like being on-field all that much, with Assault Mode attacks doing little damage and building few resources, but she can take on the role if necessary, as her Suppressive Mode Shotshell attacks can be very strong. The primary goal is to have enough Shotshells and Energy ready before every stun. With her Evasive Assist into Assist Follow-Up using up only 1 Assist Point and building 3 Shotshells, it’s an effective way to build them quickly without taking up too much time. This isn’t always ideal, however, as many Stunners don’t work well with on-fielding, it’s fine to have Zhu Yuan be the active character and then make use of her Dodge Counters and, if possible, Assist Counter to a Stunner to get both Shotshells and daze application. Zhu Yuan can get away with having 5-6 Shotshells and a little under 3/4s of her Energy before stuns, if being run with a Support that can provide Quick Assists. Manual Chain is mandatory for her best combos. Most moves will have Heavy Attacks that trigger Chain at inopportune times, as making use of Chain Attacks for Shotshell generation is important to get the most damage out. Thankfully, it’s very easy to use, as one needs to be holding down Basic Attack for Zhu Yuan’s Suppressive Mode Basic Attacks anyways. A combo with Nicole as an example: EX Special (5 → 8 Shotshells) Swap to Nicole for her EX Special Stun Begins Quick Assist to Zhu Yuan (8 → 9 Shotshells) Dash Attack Suppressive Mode B1 (9 → 8 Shotshells) Suppressive Mode B2 (8 → 7 Shotshells) Suppressive Mode Dash Attack (7 → 6 Shotshells) Suppressive mode B3 (6 → 3 Shotshells) Swap to Nicole for her Ultimate Zhu Yuan Chain Attack (3 → 6 Shotshells) Cancel Suppressive Mode B1 (6 → 5 Shotshells) Suppressive Mode B2 (5 → 4 Shotshells) Suppressive mode B3 (4 → 1 Shotshells) EX Special (1 → 4 Shotshells) Ultimate (4 → 7 Shotshells) Nicole Chain Attack Quick Assist to Zhu Yuan (7 → 8 Shotshells) Dash Attack Suppressive Mode B1 (8 → 7 Shotshells) Suppressive Mode B2 (7 → 6 Shotshells) Suppressive mode B3 (6 → 3 Shotshells) Suppressive Mode Dash Attack (3 → 2 Shotshells) Suppressive mode B3 (2 → 0 Shotshells) This allows for 19 Shotshells total while maintaining full Nicole uptime. Dash Attack is used to skip the flip that Zhu Yuan does when entering Suppressive Mode, as Dash Attack shortcuts into it. If using Dialyn, then even more damage can be done with fewer Shotshell requirements: Nicole EX Special Swap to Dialyn for her Hold Basic EX Special (Get Lost!) Stun Begins Zhu Yuan Ultimate (Dialyn Conversion, 3 → 6 Shotshells) Nicole Chain Attack Zhu Yuan Chai","pros":"One of the more F2P-friendly characters with strong generalist team options and highly accessible W-Engines; Core playstyle is easy to understand and has high mobility, but still leaves lots of room for optimization; Belongs in teams with Double Support and Stun + Support units with fairly equal performance, only reinforcing her accessibility.","cons":"Zhu Yuan is a combo-based character who can take lots of practice to pick up and play perfectly, presenting a major learning curve; Nowadays, significantly outclassed in the Ether DMG department at higher investments by characters like Yixuan.","teams":[{"m":"Zhu Yuan + Norma + Sunna + Resonaboo","c":"","r":"Rank 230"},{"m":"Zhu Yuan + Dialyn + Sunna + Birkblick","c":"","r":"Rank 280"},{"m":"Zhu Yuan + Norma + Nicole + Snap","c":"","r":"Rank 388"}]},"Soldier 11":{"slug":"soldier-11","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Warmup Sparks","d":"Press to activate. Unleashes up to 4 slashes, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["1st-Hit: 34.4%","2nd-Hit: 41.2%","3rd-Hit: 102.8%","4th-Hit: 213.4%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Fire Suppression","d":"Press at the right moment to activate: Launches a stronger slash, dealing Fire DMG. When Fire Suppression is guaranteed to trigger, pressing when the attack is about to end speeds up the transition into the next hit of Basic Attack. When Fire Suppression is guaranteed to trigger, the 5th hit of the Basic Attack string unlocks. Activating a Chain Attack or Ultimate powers up her next Basic Attack 5th hit. A strengthened Basic Attack 5th hit will consume all remaining guaranteed Fire Suppression activations to deal additional Fire DMG per activation spent. After triggering a Perfect Dodge, the current Basic Attack hit count is retained for 5s. After performing a Dodge Counter, pressing resumes the Basic Attack from the retained hit count.","m":["1st-Hit: 55.1%","2nd-Hit: 57.2%","3rd-Hit: 132%","4th-Hit: 340.7%","5th-Hit: 441.7%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Fire Assault","d":"Hold to activate: Basic Attack: Fire Charge Release while Basic Attack: Fire Charge is activated to launch Basic Attack: Fire Assault. If attacked by an enemy during Basic Attack: Fire Assault or the moment Basic Attack: Fire Charge is activated, a Block Counter can be triggered, negating that instance of DMG and granting 3 guaranteed triggers of Fire Suppression. Press to follow up with the 3rd hit of a Basic Attack, up to 8 times. While charging, tilting the stick/joystick launches Basic Attack: Blazing Rush.","m":["Basic Attack: Fire Assault: 94.1%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Raging Fire","d":"Press to activate. Slashes enemies nearby, dealing Fire DMG. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["52.6%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Fervent Fire","d":"With enough energy, press to activate. Executes a powerful slash against enemies nearby, dealing massive Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. After using this skill, Soldier 11\u0027s Basic Attacks and Dash Attacks are guaranteed to trigger Fire Suppression for up to 30s or 8 times. After using this skill, press to immediately follow up with the 4th hit of a Basic Attack. Soldier 11 enters the Alert Stance after using this skill. While in Alert Stance, if hit during a Basic Attack, triggers Basic Attack: Fire Charge to block the attack, followed by Basic Attack: Fire Assault. After Basic Attack: Fire Assault is performed, press to resume Basic Attack from the retained Basic Attack hit count.","m":["675%","Energy Cost: 80%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Tempered Fire","d":"Press to dodge. A rapid dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Blazing Fire","d":"Press during a dodge to activate. Slashes enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["68.3%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Fire Suppression","d":"Press during a dodge to activate. Slashes enemies in front, dealing Fire DMG.","m":["78.8%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Backdraft","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Executes a powerful slash against enemies in front, dealing massive Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["262%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Uplifting Flame","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate. Slashes enemies in a small area ahead, then executes a powerful upwards slash, dealing massive Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. After using this skill, Soldier 11\u0027s Basic Attacks and Dash Attacks are guaranteed to trigger Fire Suppression for up to 30s or 8 times. After using this skill, press to immediately follow up with the 4th hit of a Basic Attack. Soldier 11 enters the Alert Stance after using this skill. While in Alert Stance, if hit during a Basic Attack, triggers Basic Attack: Fire Charge to block the attack, followed by Basic Attack: Fire Assault. After Basic Attack: Fire Assault is performed, press to resume Basic Attack from the retained Basic Attack hit count.","m":["632.5%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Bellowing Flame","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate. Slashes enemies nearby, dealing massive Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. After using this skill, Soldier 11\u0027s Basic Attacks and Dash Attacks are guaranteed to trigger Fire Suppression for up to 30s or 8 times. After using this skill, press to immediately follow up with the 4th hit of a Basic Attack. Soldier 11 enters the Alert Stance after using this skill. While in Alert Stance, if hit during a Basic Attack, triggers Basic Attack: Fire Charge to block the attack, followed by Basic Attack: Fire Assault. After Basic Attack: Fire Assault is performed, press to resume Basic Attack from the retained Basic Attack hit count.","m":["2103%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Covering Fire","d":"When the on-field character is launched, press to activate. Slashes enemies in front, dealing Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["120.8%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Hold the Line","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, inflicting massive Daze. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Reignition","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate. Charge and cross slash enemies in front, dealing Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["383.7%"]}],"build":{"w":["The Brimstone","Heartstring Nocturne","Cordis Germina","Severed Innocence"],"a":["Inferno Metal, Puffer Electro","Woodpecker Electro, Puffer Electro","Inferno Metal, Woodpecker Electro","Woodpecker Electro, Branch \u0026 Blade Song"],"core":7,"st":[["CRIT Rate",76],["CRIT DMG",137],["ATK",3205]]},"how":"When in the out-of-stun state, Soldier 11’s relies on your ability to perfectly time attacks to get Fire Suppression Basic Attack strings out, with Burst of Firepower being used to counter enemy attacks for the free 3 Fire Suppression stacks and shortcut to B3, ensuring that B5 can be used. As Energy builds, use EX Specials for the 8 Fire Suppression stacks that it gives and instead of using Burst of Firepower, make use of the B5 → B3 shortcut and Perfect Dodges into Dodge Counters to preserve Basic Attack sequences until stacks have been used (which should amount to 3 B5s in total). Don’t get bogged down in only doing Soldier 11 Basic Attacks though, as it’s still important to maintain buff uptime with supportive units and build Daze with Stunners. As Soldier 11 doesn’t have many resources to manage, the more stuns she gets in a fight the better. Once Stun arrives, she has the following combo shell: Chain Attack (or Ultimate, with Dialyn’s conversion) B4 EB5 Swap to another character to trigger Chain Soldier 11 Chain Attack B4 EB5 Ultimate B4 EB5 EX Special B4 B5 B3, and so on, until Stun expires. After which it’s back to timing Fire Suppressions out-of-stun, parrying with Burst of Firepower and getting the occasional EX Special for B5, B3, B4, B5 looping. Do take care to build enough Decibels on Soldier 11 for frequent Ultimates, feeding her Defensive Assists and Assist Follow-Ups where required, but otherwise what needs to be done is simple. Just gotta practice those perfect timings!","pros":"Strong damage dealer with perfectly timed attacks that are on par with some Limited S-Rank Agents. Low resource management needs allows for both constant on-field presence and frequent, bursty stun rotations. Standard Banner unit that’s effectively free. Could eat something well over 2,000,000 on the scoville scale and be fine.","cons":"Relies on perfectly timed attacks to do well, demanding a high skill floor. Highly dependent on specific units (Dialyn, Lighter, etc.) and Limited S-Rank W-Engines to be truly competitive. Can sometimes struggle with Drive Disc set maintenance. Will find more ways than you thought possible to botch your name.","teams":[{"m":"Soldier 11 + Norma + Astra Yao + Rocketboo","c":"","r":"Rank 119"},{"m":"Soldier 11 + Norma + Sunna + Rocketboo","c":"","r":"Rank 161"},{"m":"Soldier 11 + Norma + Rina + Ultra Jake","c":"","r":"Rank 202"}]},"Qingyi":{"slug":"qingyi","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Penultimate","d":"Press to activate: Launch up to four attacks forward, dealing Physical and Electric DMG. During the 3rd-hit, repeatedly press to continue the attack, continuously striking the enemy. Using Dodge during this period will not interrupt Qingyis Basic Attack combo count. During the 3rd hit, stop pressing to interrupt the continuous attack, transitioning automatically to the 4th hit. If the continuous attack lasts for a certain time, the 4th hit will be enhanced. Anti-Interrupt Level is increased and DMG received is reduced by 40% during the 3rd and 4th hit.","m":["1st-Hit: 47.2%","1st-Hit (Alt): 110.3%","2nd-Hit: 122.1%","3rd-Hit: 17.6%","4th-Hit: 106.4%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Enchanted Blossoms","d":"Hold to activate: Launches a forward rush attack, dealing Electric DMG. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["85.6%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Flash Connect","d":"When Qingyi deals Electric DMG with a skill, she accumulates Flash Connect Voltage. When Flash Connect Voltage reaches 75%, she will enter the Flash Connect state. When using her Basic Attack: Enchanted Moonlit Blossoms, Qingyi will consume all Flash Connect Voltage and exit the Flash Connect state. For every 1% of Flash Connect Voltage consumed over 75%, her Damage and Daze inflicted by this skill will be increased by 1%/0.5%. Basic Attack: Enchanted Moonlit Blossoms itself does not accumulate Flash Connect Voltage.","m":[]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Enchanted Moonlit Blossoms","d":"During the Flash Connect state, hold to activate: Launch five consecutive forward rush attacks, then execute a Finishing Move that inflicts massive Electric DMG. Release during the move to trigger the Finishing Move early. Activate the Finishing Move just before the character is attacked to trigger Perfect Dodge. Anti-Interrupt level is increased during the rush attack and DMG received is reduced by 40%. Qingyi is invulnerable during the Finishing Move.","m":["Rush Attack: 448.7%","Finishing Strike: 394.4%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Sunlit Glory","d":"Press to activate. Quickly strikes upward, followed by a downward smash, dealing Electric DMG. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["62.4%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Moonlit Begonia","d":"When Qingyi has enough energy, press to activate: Quickly strikes upward and leaps into the air, turning around to launch a series of strikes, then follows up with a powerful downward smash, dealing massive Electric DMG. Hold to consume additional energy to increase the combo hits of the series of strikes. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. After executing the move, you can directly follow up with the 3rd-hit of a Basic Attack.","m":["602.8%","Energy Cost per second: 60%","Additional Energy Cost per second: 20%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Swan Song","d":"Press to activate. A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Breach","d":"Press during a dodge to activate. Dash forward and then launch an upward slash, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["49.5%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Lingering Sentiments","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Leap into the air and then perform a downward strike, dealing Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["284%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Tranquil Serenade","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select Qingyi to activate: Launch a series of powerful strikes over a large area in front, dealing massive Electric DMG. When this attack hits an enemy, the skills DMG increases by 3% for every stack of Subjugation in Core Passive: Eternal Seasons the target has. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["647.9%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Eight Sounds of Ganzhou","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate. Launch a series of powerful strikes over a large area in front, followed by a finishing move, dealing massive Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1670.7%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Wind Through the Pines","d":"When the on-field character is launched, press to activate. Leap into the air and perform a downward strike, dealing Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["133.9%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Graceful Embellishment","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, inflicting massive Daze. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Song of the Clear River","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate. Dash forward quickly and inject electrical energy into the ground, then pull back to trigger an explosion, dealing Electric DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["376.4%"]}],"build":{"w":["Ice-Jade Teapot","Precious Fossilized Core","Steam Oven","The Restrained"],"a":["King of the Summit, Shockstar Disco","Shockstar Disco, Thunder Metal","Astral Voice, King of the Summit","Shockstar Disco, King of the Summit"],"core":7,"st":[["CRIT Rate",57],["CRIT DMG",100],["ATK",2397]]},"how":"Despite Qingyi\u0027s complex kit, her gameplay is surprisingly straightforward, focusing on a few key combos and a loose priority order. The essence of playing Qingyi lies in accumulating and spending Voltage on her Enhanced Charged Basic attacks to apply Subjugation stacks effectively. To maximize her impact, it’s crucial to execute the full Enhanced Charged Basic attack with all five dash attacks, unless you’re confident in triggering the bonus dodge with the final blow. Qingyi\u0027s gameplay centers around two primary combos, each tailored to specific battle conditions. This combo is optimal when you have enough energy to execute an EX attack, allowing you to maximize Qingyi\u0027s damage and Daze potential: EX Special Attack: Moonlit Begonia Basic Attack: Penultimate P3 (Tap until empowered P4 is available and Voltage is close to 75) Basic Attack: Penultimate P4 (Empowered) Basic Attack: Enchanted Moonlit Blossoms (Consumes 75 Voltage) This combo is ideal when you don\u0027t have enough energy for an EX but can rely on a Dodge Counter to initiate the sequence. It requires a bit more time spent tapping Basic P3. EX Special Attack: Moonlit Begonia Basic Attack: Penultimate P3 (Tap until empowered P4 is available and Voltage is close to 75) Basic Attack: Penultimate P4 (Empowered) Basic Attack: Enchanted Moonlit Blossoms (Consumes 75 Voltage) If you’re out of energy for an EX and lack an opportunity for a Dodge Counter, you can fall back on a standard combo: Basic Attack: Penultimate P1 Basic Attack: Penultimate P2 Basic Attack: Penultimate P3 (Tap until empowered P4 is available and Voltage is close to 75) Basic Attack: Penultimate P4 (Empowered) Basic Attack: Enchanted Moonlit Blossoms (Consumes 75 Voltage) This combo is less efficient, as the first two attacks don’t generate Voltage, deal less Daze, and offer lower damage output. It should only be used to fill time between Dodge Counters and EX Specials. When you have an abundance of energy or need to Stun an enemy quickly, you can hold down Qingyi’s EX for a burst of high damage, Voltage and Daze per second but makes you more reliant on Dodge Counters or the Standard combo as you’ll have less energy to work with. When faced with a flurry of opportunities to perform Dodge Counters and/or you find yourself with a tonne of energy, the EX and Dodge counter combo can be combined to shoot for a very high Voltage finisher with minimal Basic 3 tapping time required. For a High Voltage \u0026 Daze Combo using both EX and Dodge Counter: Dodge Counter: Lingering Sentiments Basic Attack: Penultimate P3 (Tap only until empowered P4 av","pros":"Strong Daze output capable of stunning enemies in short order. Satisfying combo playstyle that after some practice flows smoothly. Multiple Damage Reductions, Anti-Interrupt buffs and Immunities throughout all of her combos. Applies a completely Generic and tremendous Damage Amplification during the Stun window allowing burst DPS to reach new heights. Can effortlessly slot into almost any team thanks to her flexible Additional Ability requirements.","cons":"Requires a massive amount of the team\u0027s field time outside of the Stun window. Combos take a good chunk of time to fully execute, sometimes making combat encounters awkward. May not always be able to fully unleash all 20 stacks of Subjugation on Boss enemies if they’re Stunned too fast or Qingyi can’t generate enough Voltage in time.","teams":[{"m":"Cissia + Qingyi + Astra Yao + Plugboo","c":"","r":"Rank 202"},{"m":"Claret + Qingyi + Rina + Plugboo","c":"","r":"Rank 230"},{"m":"Ye Shunguang + Qingyi + Zhao + Sprout","c":"","r":"Rank 280"}]},"Banyue":{"slug":"banyue","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Towering Peaks","d":"Press to activate: Launches up to four attacks in front, dealing Fire DMG. Interrupt Level is increased during this skill.","m":["1st-Hit: 39.6%","2nd-Hit: 49.8%","3rd-Hit: 101.3%","4th-Hit: 116.3%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Majestic Summit","d":"Press to activate: Launches up to four attacks in front, dealing Fire DMG. Anti-Interrupt Level is increased during this skill.","m":["1st-Hit: 52.8%","2nd-Hit: 70.4%","3rd-Hit: 135.5%","4th-Hit: 92.4%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Immolate","d":"While not in the Visage of Wrath state and with at least 120 Wrathful Fires, hold to activate: Deals Fire DMG to nearby enemies, then enters the Visage of Wrath state.","m":["110.6%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Inflame","d":"While not in combat and with more than 50% HP and less than 120 Wrathful Fires, hold to activate: Banyue consumes HP to recover Wrathful Fires. Upon reaching 120 Wrathful Fires, Banyue immediately enters the Visage of Wrath state. Upon entering the battlefield, gain one chance to use this skill. In Investigation Zone mode, this effect can trigger once per 180s. HP consumption will at most reduce Banyue\u0027s HP to 50% of Max HP.","m":[]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Toppling Mountain","d":"When Banyue is in the Visage of Wrath state, hold to consume 120 Wrathful Fires and activate: Banyue hurls a massive mountain at the enemy, dealing massive Fire DMG. After using this move, Banyue exits the Visage of Wrath state. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["869.8%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Crushing Peaks","d":"While Banyue is in the Visage of Wrath state and after performing two different EX Special Attacks through Basic Attack branches or quick input commands, hold to activate: Banyue launches his beads forward to imprison enemies, dealing massive Fire DMG. Banyue automatically follows up with Basic Attack: Toppling Mountain. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["378.3%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Earth Shaker","d":"With enough Adrenaline, can be activated in one of three ways: After the 3rd or 4th hit of Basic Attack: Towering Peaks, press to activate: After an Assist Follow-Up, Dodge Counter, or Quick Assist, hold to activate: During an EX Special Attack, Basic Attack: Immolate, Chain Attack, Ultimate, Assist Follow-Up, Dodge Counter, or Quick Assist, quickly input in sequence to activate: Banyue slams the ground repeatedly, dealing Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["254.8%","Adrenaline Cost: 20%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Mountain Tremor","d":"With enough Adrenaline, can be activated in one of two ways: After the 1st or 2nd hit of Basic Attack: Majestic Summit, press to activate: During an EX Special Attack, Basic Attack: Immolate, Chain Attack, Ultimate, Assist Follow-Up, Dodge Counter, or Quick Assist, quickly input in sequence to activate: Banyue throws a mountain, dealing Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["171.3%","Adrenaline Cost: 20%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: One\u0027s Path","d":"With enough Adrenaline, can be activated in one of three ways: After the 3rd or 4th hit of Basic Attack: Majestic Summit, press to activate: After an Assist Follow-Up, Dodge Counter, or Quick Assist, hold to activate: During an EX Special Attack, Basic Attack: Immolate, Chain Attack, Ultimate, Assist Follow-Up, Dodge Counter, or Quick Assist, quickly input in sequence to activate: Banyue throws out his beads, dealing Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["162.4%","Adrenaline Cost: 20%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Lion\u0027s Roar","d":"With enough Adrenaline, can be activated in one of two ways: After the 1st or 2nd hit of Basic Attack: Towering Peaks, press to activate: During an EX Special Attack, Basic Attack: Immolate, Chain Attack, Ultimate, Assist Follow-Up, Dodge Counter, or Quick Assist, quickly input in sequence to activate: Banyue sends out a sonic wave forward, dealing Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["153.7%","Adrenaline Cost: 20%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Mountain Tremor - Wrath","d":"With enough Adrenaline when using EX Special Attack: Earth Shaker, quickly input in sequence to activate: Banyue throws out an even larger mountain, dealing Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["325%","Adrenaline Cost: 40%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Lion\u0027s Roar - Wrath","d":"With enough Adrenaline when using EX Special Attack: One\u0027s Path, quickly input in sequence to activate: Banyue releases a powerful sonic wave in front, dealing Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["300.1%","Adrenaline Cost: 40%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Cancel","d":"When Banyue activates an EX Special Attack ALT through quick input commands, the currently activating EX Special Attack can be interrupted. Each EX Special Attack has its own Perfect Interrupt window. Interrupting an EX Special Attack after its Perfect Interrupt window will not affect the interrupted EX Special Attack\u0027s effect. Interrupting an EX Special Attack during the Perfect Interrupt window is equal to triggering a Perfect Cancel. While in the Visage of Wrath state and with Mountain\u0027s Might, Perfect Cancel is easier to trigger.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Immovable Mountain","d":"While attacking, press without moving the stick/joystick to activate: Banyue enters a defensive stance. If attacked during this time, he parries the enemy\u0027s attack and accumulates Daze. If attacked at the exact moment the skill is activated, a Perfect Block occurs. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["0%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Overcome Peaks","d":"Press to activate. A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Battle Cry","d":"Rotate the stick/joystick in a half-circle and press to activate. Dodges backward and taunts enemies. After any EX Special Attack, follow up with Dodge: Battle Cry and quickly execute the required inputs during Dodge: Battle Cry to then follow up with the corresponding EX Special Attack. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Scattering Sands","d":"During a dodge, press or during Dodge: Battle Cry, hold to activate: Launches beads forward, dealing Fire DMG. After using this skill, can be followed up with the 2nd hit of Basic Attack: Towering Peaks or the 2nd hit of Basic Attack: Majestic Summit.","m":["39.7%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Stoneburst","d":"After a Perfect Dodge is triggered through Dodge: Overcome Peaks, press , or after a Perfect Dodge is triggered though Dodge: Battle Cry, hold to activate: Launches a forward attack that deals Fire DMG. After using this skill, can be chained into the 3rd hit of Basic Attack: Towering Peaks or the 3rd hit of Basic Attack: Majestic Summit. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["194.9%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Blazing Wrath","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Launches a large area attack in front, dealing massive Fire DMG. If Banyue has more than 120 Wrathful Fires, he automatically enters the Visage of Wrath state after the attack. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["560.9%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: The World Trembles","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate: Launches a large area attack in front, dealing massive Fire DMG. If Banyue has more than 120 Wrathful Fires, he automatically enters the Visage of Wrath state after the attack. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["1598.4%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Batholith","d":"When the active character is launched, press to activate. Executes a series of attacks against enemies in front, dealing Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["73.4%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Iron Bastion","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Lofty Ascent","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate: Quickly dash forward and attack, dealing Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["241.6%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Pierce Heavens","d":"After successfully parrying an enemy attack with Dodge: Immovable Mountain, press to activate: Quickly dash forward and attack, dealing Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["221.6%"]}],"build":{"w":["Wrathful Vajra","Cauldron of Clarity","Grill O\u0027Wisp","Qingming Birdcage"],"a":["Yunkui Tales, Branch \u0026 Blade Song","Yunkui Tales, Woodpecker Electro","Yunkui Tales, Inferno Metal","Branch \u0026 Blade Song, Bunny in Wonderland, Flex"],"core":7,"st":[["CRIT Rate",64],["CRIT DMG",155],["ATK",2047]]},"how":"Banyue may have a lot of complexity to his kit and equally steep execution requirements to go with it, but at its core, his game plan is surprisingly simple. More than any other character in the game, Banyue wants to be on the field to build up to Visage of Wrath, so most fights with him boil down to getting as many perfect on-field parries with Immovable Mountain as possible, spending Adrenaline, and trying to line-up stuns so that they’re happening after Banyue is at 120 Wrathful Fires. From there, burst as hard as possible and then make use of the Adrenaline refund from Mountain’s Might to start building his gauge back up and repeat the process. His ideal stun combo has no Adrenaline requirements, as Visage of Wrath makes EX Specials free and refunds Adrenaline on cast, but Banyue should have enough Decibels for an Ultimate. Manual Chain should not be needed (although it does make it more comfortable!), as you can swap out of Banyue before the delayed Heavy Attacks from his EX Specials land. Be on another character to trigger Chain Banyue Chain Attack (buffer Earth Shaker during this) Cancel Earth Shaker (BSB) Mountain Tremor - Wrath (SSB) Swap to another character to trigger Chain Banyue Chain Attack (buffer One’s Path during this) One’s Path (SBS) Lion’s Roar - Wrath (BBS) Crushing Peaks Toppling Mountain Ultimate Assuming Dialyn is used, then the Chain Attack can be replaced with an Ultimate conversion. Alternatively, a double Chain + double Ultimate combo is possible depending on resource economy, in which case swap to Dialyn on the second set of EX Special casts (so just before Crushing Peaks) and use her Ultimate conversion then. If there is enough time after Ultimate (such as if using his M1 or other characters’ Stun extensions, like Dialyn), then loop One’s Path and Lion’s Roar - Wrath with the remaining Adrenaline before stun ends. If using Auto Combo, then: Be on another character to trigger Chain Banyue Chain Attack Cancel Press the Special button and keep it held down Earth Shake Mountain Tremor - Wrath One’s Path Lion’s Roar - Wrath Swap to another character to trigger Chain Banyue Chain Attack Ultimate Toppling Mountain Note that, unlike the Quick Inputs combo, Auto Combo requires Manual Chain! Without it, Chains will trigger halfway through the EX Special strings. It also should not end with Ultimate, which has the unfortunate side effect of making it unable for Banyue to link EX Specials right as the combo ends, but it is necessary as the Ultimate must be used to cancel the Chain Attack’s recovery animations. It must be done this way, ","pros":"Accessible skill floor (has auto combos, can fully on-field, etc.) but high skill ceiling that rewards effort. Unique mechanics that make him stand out from the rest of the cast, with an on-field parry, motion inputs, buffers, varied combos, and much more, Subjectively a very interesting character who pushes the limits of what a \"mobile\" game\u0027s combat can be. The Lion does not concern himself...","cons":"Technical character who demands a high level of player skill to be at his best. Comparatively lacklustre performance, having not even a single encounter in which he is better than other characters for. Expensive to build, with all of his skills needing to be integrated for good gameplay. ...with being a meta pick.","teams":[{"m":"Banyue + Dialyn + Lucia + Birkblick","c":"","r":"Rank 53"},{"m":"Banyue + Norma + Lucia + Ultra Jake","c":"","r":"Rank 116"},{"m":"Banyue + Ju Fufu + Lucia + Belion","c":"","r":"Rank 230"}]},"Burnice":{"slug":"burnice","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Direct Flame Blend","d":"Press to activate: Unleashes up to 5 attacks in front, dealing Physical DMG and Fire DMG.","m":["1st-Hit: 44.8%","2nd-Hit: 43.5%","3rd-Hit: 71.7%","4th-Hit: 66.6%","5th-Hit: 96.3%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Mixed Flame Blend","d":"In the Nitro-Fuel Cocktail state, hold to activate: Spins continuously while spraying flames around, followed by a Finishing Move, then triggers an extra instance of Afterburn that doesn\u0027t cost Heat and deals Fire DMG. Continuing to hold extends the flame-spraying duration. The DMG dealt by this skill also counts as Assist Attack DMG. Upon activation, it consumes 20 Heat. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill. After executing the Finishing Move, press to immediately follow up with EX Special Attack: Intense Heat Stirring Method - Double Shot.","m":["Continuous Spray: 125.4%","Finishing Move: 232.8%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Intense Heat Aging Method","d":"Press to activate. Unleash a fire blast forward, inflicting Fire DMG; Press and hold to charge, boosting the moves power. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["57.8%","Charged Attack: 62.4%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Intense Heat Stirring Method","d":"With enough energy, press to activate: Continuously spray flames with a one-handed flamethrower, then release a fire blast in a straight line ahead, dealing massive Fire DMG. Continue holding to steadily consume Energy and extend the spray\u0027s duration. While continuously spraying, drag the stick/joystick to execute a sidestep dodge, adjusting your position in the corresponding direction. Anti-Interrupt Level is increased while continuously spraying, and DMG taken is reduced by 60%. Character is invulnerable during sidestep dodge and fire blast.","m":["Continuous Spray: 543.8%","Fire Blast: 96.7%","Energy Cost to Use: 40%","Continuous Spray Energy Cost per second: 12.5%","Fire Blast Energy Cost: 5%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Intense Heat Stirring Method - Double Shot","d":"While using EX Special Attack: Intense Heat Stirring Method, with enough Energy, press to activate: Use both flamethrowers to continuously spray flames, followed by a fire blast in a front line, dealing massive Fire DMG. Keep holding to continue consuming Energy and extend the spray\u0027s duration. Character is invulnerable during the moment the spray is activated and during the activation of the fire blast. Anti-Interrupt Level is increased while spraying, and DMG received is reduced by 60%.","m":["Continuous Spray: 958.1%","Fire Blast: 287.1%","Energy Cost to Use: 10%","Continuous Spray Energy Cost per second: 25%","Fire Blast Energy Cost: 10%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Intense Heat Tossing Method","d":"If Burnice has Emberflow, coming on-field activates this skill. After squadmates trigger Afterburn 12 times, Burnice gains 1 point of Emberflow. With Emberflow, Burnice\u0027s next entry onto the field consumes 1 stack to automatically activate this skill. This entry is considered a Quick Assist. When Afterburn triggered by Basic Attack: Mixed Flame Blend hits an enemy, it counts for 2 times. While possessing Emberflow, the counter no longer increases. Consuming Emberflow clears the counter. Quickly dashes forward and passes through the enemy, unleashing a fiery impact that deals Physical DMG and Fire DMG. When the skill\u0027s heavy attack hits a target suffering Ether, Electric, Fire, Physical, Ice, or Wind Anomaly, it triggers Abloom: deals an additional instance of DMG equal to 480%/240%/600%/40%/60%/24% of the original Anomaly\u0027s DMG. The Fire Anomaly Buildup increase from Additional Ability: Fire Kindling applies to this skill. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. After using this skill, press to immediately follow up with EX Special Attack: Intense Heat Stirring Method - Double Shot.","m":["199.9%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Fiery Phantom Dash","d":"Press to activate. A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Dangerous Fermentation","d":"Press during a dodge to activate: Perform a forward rush attack with the flamethrower, dealing Fire DMG.","m":["67.9%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Fluttering Steps","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. SLaunch a series of attacks on enemies in front while spraying flames, dealing Physical DMG and Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["219.7%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Fuel-Fed Flame","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Quickly dash forward while spraying flames in all directions, then launch a fire blast in a fan-shaped area ahead, dealing massive Fire DMG. After using the skill, press to immediately follow up with EX Special Attack: Intense Heat Stirring Method - Double Shot. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["680.9%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Glorious Inferno","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate. Dash forward quickly, then leap into the air and continuously spray flames over a wide area ahead, dealing massive Fire DMG. When leaping into the air, a Quick Assist will be triggered. If the Quick Assist is activated, Burnice will extend the duration of her flame spray. Upon activation, recover 50 Heat. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["2012.2%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Energizing Specialty Drink","d":"When the on-field character is launched, press to activate. Launches a series of attacks at enemies ahead and sprays flames, dealing Physical DMG and Fire DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. After using this skill, press to immediately follow up with EX Special Attack: Intense Heat Stirring Method - Double Shot.","m":["84.4%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Smoky Cauldron","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, inflicting massive Daze. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Scorching Dew","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate: Leap into the air and quickly spin forward while spraying flames in all directions, dealing Fire DMG. After using the skill, press to immediately follow up with EX Special Attack: Intense Heat Stirring Method - Double Shot. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["327.6%"]}],"build":{"w":["Flamemaker Shaker","Weeping Gemini","Fusion Compiler","Electro-Lip Gloss"],"a":["Chaos Jazz, Freedom Blues","Chaos Jazz, Swing Jazz","Chaos Jazz, Moonlight Lullaby","Freedom Blues, Moonlight Lullaby"],"core":6.98,"st":[["CRIT Rate",14],["CRIT DMG",68],["ATK",2980]]},"how":"Burnice’s gameplan then amounts to a pretty simple flowchart: Apply Scorch to enemies (most likely with her Hold Basic Attack at the start of combat to reserve Energy). Stay off-field and allow squad members to trigger Afterburn procs to build Emberflow. Swap in occasionally to restore Heat via EX Special casts, ideally with a skill that allows her to shortcut to Double Shot (like an Assist Follow-Up or a Chain Attack). If there’s enough Energy Regen to allow for frequent refills, using the occasional Hold Basic Attack for more Afterburn procs can help. Once Emberflow is stocked, use it up immediately for an Abloom trigger. There are some optimisations that can be done to her general play. As she’s likely to be running Chaos Jazz 4-piece, the 7.5s CD on its effect upon switching in should be respected else risk losing its bonus when coming in to refill Heat. Ultimate is always a good option for an immediate top-up that is independent from Energy consumption, buying time for resources to recover. Keep in mind that ideally it shouldn’t be used when at over 50 Heat so as to not waste gauge. Anything more would be comp and encounter specific, like looking to balance out Defensive Assists with the main damage dealer for Decibel management which may require Burnice to come on-field slightly more frequently, or making use of her Ultimate to bypass Anomaly/Disorder ICDs with Alice. The greatest gains in score for Burnice are less about how she in particular is played and more on how to route a fight, specifically by getting good at sustaining Heat and balancing out Anomaly build-up across the team.","pros":"Requires minimal field time to function, thanks to off-field playstyle; Strong Fire Anomaly Application - ideal for Burn or Disorder-focused teams; Easy To Play.","cons":"Reliant on energy and/or Ultimate to generate “Heat” and keep her kit fully functional - as such resource management is required.","teams":[{"m":"Remielle + Burnice + Velina + Ariel","c":"","r":"Rank 6"},{"m":"Burnice + Velina + Yuzuha + Ultra Jake","c":"","r":"Rank 39"},{"m":"Miyabi + Burnice + Yuzuha + Sharkboo","c":"","r":"Rank 47"}]},"Miyabi":{"slug":"miyabi","skills":[{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Kazahana","d":"Press or hold to activate: Unleashes up to 5 slashes ahead, the first two deal Physical DMG, and the last three deal Frost DMG. Block enemy attacks during the 5th hit of the Basic Attack.","m":["1st-Hit: 26.9%","2nd-Hit: 29.6%","3rd-Hit: 62.8%","4th-Hit: 96.5%","5th-Hit: 129%"]},{"t":"Basic","n":"Basic Attack: Shimotsuki","d":"With at least 2 points of Fallen Frost, hold to activate: Hoshimi Miyabi sheaths her blade, enters Shimotsuki Stance and starts to charge up. Every level of charge will consume 2 points of Fallen Frost, up to a maximum of three levels of charge. When releasing , or when Fallen Frost is completely depleted, Hoshimi Miyabi will draw her blade and unleash a powerful slash ahead based on the current charge level, dealing massive Frost DMG. She then exits Shimotsuki Stance. Character is invulnerable during Shimotsuki Stance. Hoshimi Miyabi can have up to 6 points of Fallen Frost. Upon entering the battlefield, Hoshimi Miyabi immediately obtains 3 points of Fallen Frost.","m":["Charge Level One Slash: 454.7%","Charge Level Two Slash: 858.1%","Charge Level Three Slash: 2141.1%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"Special Attack: Miyuki","d":"Press to activate. Quickly draws her blade and slashes ahead, dealing Frost DMG. Anti-Interrupt level is increased while using this skill.","m":["35.8%"]},{"t":"Skill","n":"EX Special Attack: Hisetsu","d":"With enough energy, press to activate: Rush forward, unleashing powerful slashes against enemies along the way, dealing massive Frost DMG. Upon activating this skill, gain 2 points of Fallen Frost. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. After using this skill, with enough Energy, press again to activate: Consume extra Energy and unleash a powerful follow-up attack against enemies in front, dealing massive Frost DMG. Upon activating this skill, gain 2 points of Fallen Frost. Character is invulnerable while using this skill","m":["Slash: 393.4%","Follow-Up: 483.2%","Slash  Energy Cost: 40%","Follow-Up Energy Cost: 20%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge: Mizutori","d":"Press to activate. A quick dash dodge. Character is invulnerable while using this skill. While dodging, repeatedly press or hold to activate: A dash dodge that covers a lot of ground. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":[]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dash Attack: Fuyubachi","d":"Press during a dodge to activate: Slashes enemies in front, dealing Physical DMG.","m":["25.8%"]},{"t":"Dodge","n":"Dodge Counter: Kan Suzume","d":"Press during a Perfect Dodge to activate. Slashes enemies in front, dealing Frost DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["245.9%"]},{"t":"Chain","n":"Chain Attack: Spring\u0027s Call","d":"When a Chain Attack is triggered, select the character to activate: Unleashes a powerful slash at enemies in front in a large area, dealing massive Frost DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["628%"]},{"t":"Ultimate","n":"Ultimate: Lingering Snow","d":"When Decibel Rating is at Maximum, press to activate. Unleashes powerful slashes at enemies ahead in a large area then pauses, before unleashing a Finishing Move, dealing massive Frost DMG. Upon activating this skill, gain 3 points of Fallen Frost and increase Ice DMG by 30% for 12s. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["2388%"]},{"t":"Recover","n":"Quick Assist: Dancing Petals","d":"When the on-field character is launched, press to activate. Slashes enemies in front, dealing Frost DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["104.5%"]},{"t":"Parry","n":"Defensive Assist: Drifting Petals","d":"When the character on field is about to be attacked, press to activate. Parries the enemy\u0027s attack, dealing massive Daze. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["Light Defensive: 0%","Heavy Defensive: 0%","Chain Defensive: 0%"]},{"t":"Assist","n":"Assist Follow-Up: Falling Petals","d":"Press after a Defensive Assist to activate: Charges and slashes enemies in front, dealing Frost DMG. Character is invulnerable while using this skill.","m":["337.8%"]}],"build":{"w":["Hailstorm Shrine","Fusion Compiler","Weeping Gemini","Flight of Fancy"],"a":["Branch \u0026 Blade Song, Woodpecker Electro","Branch \u0026 Blade Song, Puffer Electro","Branch \u0026 Blade Song, Astral Voice","Branch \u0026 Blade Song, Polar Metal"],"core":7,"st":[["CRIT Rate",72],["CRIT DMG",151],["ATK",2978]]},"how":"$undefined","pros":"Absurdly large damage multipliers giving \"hit like a truck\" a new meaning, Huge AoE on many attacks, allowing her to quickly deal with big groups of monsters, A good amount of team options for both spenders and F2P, She sets a new bar for how strong a DPS can be in the game.","cons":"As one of the first CRIT Anomaly characters her W-Engine options outside her signature are limited, Relies on applying Frost Anomaly at specific points in her combo for maximum effectiveness - disruption to this can cause issues, Really wants to achieve 80% CRIT RATE for the 80% Anomaly Buildup to assist with the point above, making her stat-hungry, Rotations and playstyle can drastically change based on team composition leading to a steep path to mastery, Has many long animations which you\u0027ll want to Quick Swap to another squad member to alleviate. This introduces a new axis of skill for those looking for the best results.","teams":[{"m":"Miyabi + Nangong Yu + Yuzuha + Biggest Fan","c":"","r":"Rank 2"},{"m":"Miyabi + Vivian + Yuzuha + Robin","c":"","r":"Rank 19"},{"m":"Miyabi + Nangong Yu + Astra Yao + Snap","c":"","r":"Rank 25"}]}};